[Term]
id: HP:0000001
name: All
synonym: "الكل" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الكل عادةً يشير إلى جميع العناصر أو الجزء الكامل من مجموعة معينة.
comment: Root of all terms in the Human Phenotype Ontology.
xref: UMLS:C0444868

[Term]
id: HP:0000002
name: Abnormality of body height
synonym: "شذوذ في طول الجسم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "طول الجسم غير طبيعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انحراف في الطول عن المعتاد وفقًا للمعايير العمرية والجنسية.
def: "Deviation from the norm of height with respect to that which is expected according to age and gender norms." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Abnormality of body height" EXACT layperson []
xref: UMLS:C4025901
is_a: HP:0001507 ! Growth abnormality
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2008-02-27T02:20:00Z

[Term]
id: HP:0000003
name: Multicystic kidney dysplasia
synonym: "خلل تنسجي متعدد الكيسات في الكلى" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "كلى متعددة الكيسات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الخلل التنسجي في الكلى المتعدد الكيسات يتميز بظهور أكياس متعددة بأحجام مختلفة في الكلى مع غياب نظام حويضي كأسي طبيعي. ترتبط الحالة بوجود رتق في الحالب أو في الوصلة الحالبية الحوضية، وتكون الكلية المصابة غير وظيفية.
alt_id: HP:0004715
def: "Multicystic dysplasia of the kidney is characterized by multiple cysts of varying size in the kidney and the absence of a normal pelvicaliceal system. The condition is associated with ureteral or ureteropelvic atresia, and the affected kidney is nonfunctional." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Multicystic kidney dysplasia is the result of abnormal fetal renal development in which the affected kidney is replaced by multiple cysts and has little or no residual function. The vast majority of multicystic kidneys are unilateral. Multicystic kidney can be diagnosed on prenatal ultrasound.
synonym: "Multicystic dysplastic kidney" EXACT []
synonym: "Multicystic kidneys" EXACT []
synonym: "Multicystic renal dysplasia" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:204962002
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:82525005
xref: UMLS:C3714581
is_a: HP:0000107 ! Renal cyst

[Term]
id: HP:0000005
name: Mode of inheritance
synonym: "نمط الوراثة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "كيفية انتقال الصفات الوراثية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: النمط الذي ينتقل من خلاله صفة جينية معينة أو اضطراب من جيل إلى الجيل التالي.
alt_id: HP:0001425
alt_id: HP:0001453
alt_id: HP:0001461
alt_id: HP:0010985
def: "The pattern in which a particular genetic trait or disorder is passed from one generation to the next." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: While there is a close conceptual relationship between allelic requirement and inheritance, they serve different purposes; allelic requirement is necessary for variant annotation pipelines and to determine if a given variant in a specific context is relevant to the phenotype of the patient e.g. a heterozygous variant (in the absence of compound heterozygosity) is relevant for dominant but not for recessive disease; while inheritance is used for describing the mode of inheritance of a phenotype and is particularly applicable in the clinical setting for communicating recurrence risk, to guide family screening, and to guide reproductive advice.
synonym: "Inheritance" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C1708511
is_a: HP:0000001 ! All

[Term]
id: HP:0000006
name: Autosomal dominant inheritance
synonym: "وراثة جسمية سائدة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وراثة جينية من الوالدين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمط من الوراثة يلاحظ في الصفات المتعلقة بجين مشفر على أحد الكروموسومات الجسمية (أي الكروموسومات البشرية 1-22) حيث تظهر الصفة لدى المتغايرين جينياً. في سياق الوراثة الطبية، ينتج الاضطراب الجسماني السائد عندما يكون هناك نسخة واحدة من الأليل الطافر. يتأثر الذكور والإناث بالتساوي ويمكن لكلاهما نقل الاضطراب مع خطر نسبته 50% لكل طفل في وراثة الأليل الطافر.
alt_id: HP:0001415
alt_id: HP:0001447
alt_id: HP:0001448
alt_id: HP:0001451
alt_id: HP:0001452
alt_id: HP:0001455
alt_id: HP:0001456
alt_id: HP:0001463
def: "A mode of inheritance that is observed for traits related to a gene encoded on one of the autosomes (i.e., the human chromosomes 1-22) in which a trait manifests in heterozygotes. In the context of medical genetics, an autosomal dominant disorder is caused when a single copy of the mutant allele is present. Males and females are affected equally, and can both transmit the disorder with a risk of 50% for each child of inheriting the mutant allele." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Autosomal dominant" EXACT []
synonym: "Autosomal dominant form" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Autosomal dominant type" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "monoallelic_autosomal" EXACT allelic_requirement []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:263681008
xref: UMLS:C0443147
is_a: HP:0034345 ! Mendelian inheritance

[Term]
id: HP:0000007
name: Autosomal recessive inheritance
synonym: "وراثة جسمية متنحية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وراثة من كلا الوالدين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمط من الوراثة يلاحظ في الصفات المتعلقة بجين مشفر على أحد الكروموسومات الجسمية (أي الكروموسومات البشرية 1-22) حيث تظهر الصفة لدى الأفراد الذين يحملون أليلين مسببين للمرض، سواء كانوا متماثلي الأليل (حمل نسختين من الأليل الطافر نفسه) أو متغايري الأليل المركب (حيث يكون لكل نسخة من الجين أليل طافر مميز).
alt_id: HP:0001416
alt_id: HP:0001526
alt_id: HP:0031362
def: "A mode of inheritance that is observed for traits related to a gene encoded on one of the autosomes (i.e., the human chromosomes 1-22) in which a trait manifests in individuals with two pathogenic alleles, either homozygotes (two copies of the same mutant allele) or compound heterozygotes (whereby each copy of a gene has a distinct mutant allele)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Autosomal recessive" EXACT []
synonym: "Autosomal recessive form" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Autosomal recessive predisposition" RELATED []
synonym: "biallelic_autosomal" EXACT allelic_requirement []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:258211005
xref: UMLS:C0441748
xref: UMLS:C4020899
is_a: HP:0034345 ! Mendelian inheritance

