[Term]
id: HP:0000095
name: Abnormal renal glomerulus morphology
synonym: "شذوذ مورفولوجيا الكبيبة الكلوية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شذوذ في كبيبة الكلى" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ في كبيبة الكلى.
def: "A structural anomaly of the glomerulus." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:Eurenomics_ewuehl, PMID:18184729]
comment: Each human kidney contains approximately one million nephrons. The glomerulus is the most proximal component of the nephron. The glomerulus of the mammalian kidney is a highly developed vascular bed that acts as a filter, allowing a filtrate of small molecules, such as water, sugars, electrolytes and small proteins, to pass through a barrier that retains high molecular weight proteins and cells in the circulation.
synonym: "Abnormality of renal glomerulus morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "Morphologic abnormality of the renal glomerulus" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4025889
is_a: HP:0031263 ! Abnormal renal corpuscle morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0000096
name: Glomerular sclerosis
synonym: "تصلب كبيبات الكلى" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تليف كبيبات الكلى" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تراكم النسيج الندبي داخل الكبيبة.
alt_id: HP:0030761
def: "Accumulation of scar tissue within the glomerulus." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:Eurenomics_fschaefer]
synonym: "Glomerulosclerosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Renal glomerular fibrosis" BROAD []
