[Term]
id: HP:0000189
name: Narrow palate
synonym: "حنك ضيق" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "سقف فم ضيق" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عرض الحنك أقل من 2 انحراف معياري أقل من المتوسط (موضوعيًا) أو يظهر تناقص في عرض الحنك (شخصيًا).
def: "Width of the palate more than 2 SD below the mean (objective) or apparently decreased palatal width (subjective)." [PMID:19125428]
comment: Palatal width is measured as the distance between the maxillary first permanent molar on the right and left sides, at the lingual cervical line, using a specific device. Palate width is typically assessed subjectively in routine clinical practice. Narrowing is often associated with a High palate, but this should be assessed and coded separately. Gingival overgrowth can give the impression of a narrow palate but should be distinguished and coded separately. The term gothic palate is used to indicate that the roof of the palate is not round but rather has an inverted V-shape, and therefore, only the upper part of the palate is narrow.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Decreased palatal width" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Decreased transverse dimension of palate" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Narrow palate" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Narrow roof of mouth" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
xref: UMLS:C1398312
is_a: HP:0000174 ! Abnormal palate morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0000190
name: Abnormal oral frenulum morphology
synonym: "شذوذ تشكل اللجم الفموي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شذوذ في اللجم الفموي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ في اللجم اللساني، وهو الطية الصغيرة من الأغشية المخاطية التي تثبت اللسان إلى أرضية الفم، أو وجود لجيم إضافي في تجويف الفم.
def: "An abnormality of the lingual frenulum, that is of the small fold of mucous membrane that attaches the tongue to the floor of the mouth, or the presence of accessory frenula in the oral cavity." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:23633765]
comment: A frenulum is a small frenum. There are several frena that are usually present in a normal oral cavity, most notably the maxillary labial frenum, the mandibular labial frenum, and the lingual frenum.
synonym: "Abnormality of frenum of tongue" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Abnormality of lingual frenum" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Abnormality of oral frenula" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormality of oral frenum" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
xref: UMLS:C4025881
is_a: HP:0000163 ! Abnormal oral cavity morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0000191
name: Accessory oral frenulum
synonym: "الحبال الفموية الإضافية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "حبال فموية إضافية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: طية إضافية من النسيج تمتد من الحافة السنخية إلى السطح الداخلي للشفة العليا أو السفلى.
def: "Extra fold of tissue extending from the alveolar ridge to the inner surface of the upper or lower lip." [PMID:19125428]
comment: This finding is assessed by gently retracting the oral mucosa from the alveolar ridge. Typically there is a single maxillary and a single mandibular frenulum located in the midline between the two central incisors. Abnormalities of the alveolar ridges may accompany accessory frenula, but these should be assessed separately.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Accessory oral frenum" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Extra oral frenulum" EXACT []
synonym: "Extra oral frenum" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Multiple oral frenula" EXACT []
synonym: "Supernumerary oral frenulum" EXACT []
synonym: "Supernumerary oral frenum" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
xref: UMLS:C4021814
is_a: HP:0000190 ! Abnormal oral frenulum morphology

