[Term]
id: HP:0000362
name: Otosclerosis
synonym: "التصلب الأذني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: في التصلب الأذني، يتجمع تكاثف عظمي على الركابة مما يسبب تثبيتًا جزئيًا. وهذا يحد من حركة عظْم الركابة، مما يؤدي إلى فقدان السمع.
def: "In otosclerosis, a callus of bone accumulates on the stapes creating a partial fixation. This limits the movement of the stapes bone, which results in hearing loss." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:15931303]
comment: Otosclerosis cannot be seen on an office examination. The audiogram indicates a conductive type of hearing loss. Testing of the stapedial reflexes indicates limited or no movement of the bones of hearing.
subset: hposlim_core
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:11543004
xref: UMLS:C0029899
is_a: HP:0008628 ! Abnormal stapes morphology

