[Term]
id: HP:0000565
name: Esotropia
synonym: "حول تقاطعي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "حول تجاه الداخل" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شكل من أشكال الحول حيث تكون إحدى العينين أو كلاهما متجهة إلى الداخل ('متقاطعة') بدرجة شديدة، تُعرف عادةً بأنها 10 ديوبترات أو أكثر.
def: "A form of strabismus with one or both eyes turned inward ('crossed') to a relatively severe degree, usually defined as 10 diopters or more." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Esotropia is analogous to but more severe than esophoria. Affected children are more likely to have amblyopia or require corrective eye muscle surgery than children with esophoria.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Inward turning cross eyed" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
