[Term]
id: HP:0000679
name: Taurodontia
synonym: "تاورودنشيا" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة حجم اللب السني للضرس الدائم تتمثل في نسبة بين التاج والجذر تساوي أو أكبر من 1:1 أو غرف اللب الممددة وانزياح القمم الجذري.
def: "Increased volume of dental pulp of permanent molar characterized by a crown body-root ratio equal or larger than 1:1 or an elongated pulp chambers and apical displacement of the bifurcation or trifurcation of the roots." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9338-3017, PMID:31468724]
comment: Taurodontia causes a molar shape that is visible on radiographs. Taurodontic teeth display proportionately short roots and enlarged pulp chambers. Body of the tooth and pulp chamber is enlarged.
