[Term]
id: HP:0000759
name: Abnormal peripheral nervous system morphology
synonym: "شذوذ في مورفولوجيا الجهاز العصبي المحيطي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "هيكل غير طبيعي للجهاز العصبي المحيطي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ هيكلي في الجهاز العصبي المحيطي، الذي يتكون من الأعصاب التي تقود إلى أو تتفرع من الجهاز العصبي المركزي. ويتضمن ذلك الأعصاب القحفية (النير بالحاسة الشمية والعصبية البصرية هي تقنيًا جزء من الجهاز العصبي المركزي).
alt_id: HP:0003483
def: "A structural abnormality of the peripheral nervous system, which is composed of the nerves that lead to or branch off from the central nervous system. This includes the cranial nerves (olfactory and optic nerves are technically part of the central nervous system)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The peripheral nervous system is divided into autonomic and somatic components, which both include afferent (sensory) and efferent (motor) nerves.
synonym: "Abnormal peripheral nervous system structure" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Peripheral nervous system disease" RELATED []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:302226006
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:42658009
xref: UMLS:C0031117
xref: UMLS:C4025831
is_a: HP:0012639 ! Abnormal nervous system morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0000762
name: Decreased nerve conduction velocity
synonym: "تراجع في سرعة توصيل الأعصاب" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "بطء سير الإشارات العصبية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انخفاض في السرعة التي تنتقل بها الإشارات الكهربائية عبر محور العصبون.
alt_id: HP:0000761
alt_id: HP:0007118
alt_id: HP:0007218
alt_id: HP:0007231
def: "A reduction in the speed at which electrical signals propagate along the axon of a neuron." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Nerve conduction velocity is usually measured with surface electrodes placed on the skin over nerves at various locations. Following stimulation at one electrode, the speed at which the signal is propagated to other electrodes is recorded. Abnormal values may suggest demyelination, a conduction block, or axonopathy.
synonym: "Decreased NCV" EXACT []
synonym: "Decreased nerve conduction velocities" EXACT []
synonym: "Delayed nerve conduction velocity" EXACT []
synonym: "Reduced nerve conduction velocities" EXACT []
synonym: "Slow nerve conduction velocity" EXACT []
synonym: "Slowed nerve conduction velocities" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C1857640
is_a: HP:0040129 ! Abnormal nerve conduction velocity

