alt_id: HP:0000102
def: "The presence of calculi (stones) in the kidneys." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Urinary stone disease is caused by supersaturation of the urine by stone forming substances including calcium, oxalate, and uric acid. Crystals or foreign bodies can act as a nidus for further stone formation. The resulting kidney stones (calculi) lead to symptoms if they become impacted in the ureter.
