[Term]
id: HP:0000845
name: Elevated circulating growth hormone concentration
synonym: "ارتفاع تركيز هرمون النمو في الدم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "فرط هرمون النمو" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: العملقة هي حالة ناتجة عن زيادة إنتاج هرمون النمو من الغدة النخامية لدى الأشخاص ذوي المشاش المغلق، وتتكون بشكل أساسي من تضخم الأجزاء الطرفية من الجسم. يزداد محيط الجمجمة، يصبح الأنف عريضًا، يتضخم اللسان، تزداد خشونة ملامح الوجه، ينمو الفك السفلي بشكل مفرط، وتتفارق الأسنان. تنمو الأصابع وأصابع القدم بشكل رئيسي في السماكة.
alt_id: HP:0008856
def: "Acromegaly is a condition resulting from overproduction of growth hormone by the pituitary gland in persons with closed epiphyses, and consists chiefly in the enlargement of the distal parts of the body. The circumference of the skull increases, the nose becomes broad, the tongue becomes enlarged, the facial features become coarsened, the mandible grows excessively, and the teeth become separated. The fingers and toes grow chiefly in thickness." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0538-4547, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Disorder resulting from excess pituitary gland production of growth hormone (hGH).
synonym: "Elevated circulating somatotropin concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Growth hormone excess" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Somatotropin excess" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:74107003
xref: UMLS:C0001206
xref: UMLS:C0235986
is_a: HP:0010514 ! Hyperpituitarism
is_a: HP:0032367 ! Abnormal growth hormone level

[Term]
id: HP:0000846
name: Adrenal insufficiency
synonym: "قصور الكظر" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نقص نشاط الغدة الكظرية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: قصور في إنتاج هرمونات الستيرويد (خصوصًا الكورتيزول) من الغدد الكظرية.
alt_id: HP:0000865
alt_id: HP:0008218
def: "Insufficient production of steroid hormones (primarily cortisol) by the adrenal glands." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:11443143]
comment: Adrenal insufficiency may cause persistent vomiting, anorexia, hypoglycemia, poor weight gain in a child, or unexplained weight loss in an adult, malaise, fatigue, muscular weakness, unexplained isotonic or hyponatremic dehydration, hyperkalemia, hypotension, hypoglycemia and especially generalized hyperpigmentation.
synonym: "Hypoadrenalism" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:111563005
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:237785004
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:386584007
xref: UMLS:C0001623
is_a: HP:0011733 ! Abnormality of adrenal physiology

