[Term]
id: HP:0001003
name: Multiple lentigines
synonym: "بقع شحمية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "بقع بنية على الجلد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود عدد غير عادي من الشامات الصغيرة المسطحة ذات اللون البني إلى تان، المعروفة بالنتيجة (مفردها: نتيجة)، وهي بقع بيضاوية الشكل.
def: "Presence of an unusually high number of lentigines (singular: lentigo), which are flat, tan to brown oval spots." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Lentigines are commonly (but not always) due to chronic sun exposure (solar lentigines; sometimes called liver spots) and occur most frequently on the face and back of the hands.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Liver spots" NARROW layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6908-9849]
