[Term]
id: HP:0001019
name: Erythroderma
synonym: "إيريثودرما" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "احمرار وتقشر عام في الجلد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: التهاب جلدي تقشري يشمل تقريبا كل سطح الجلد. يتطور الإيريثودرما فجأة. قد ينتشر الحمامى المتقطع ليؤثر على معظم الجلد. قد يظهر التقشر في غضون 2-6 أيام، ويصاحبه سخونة الجلد واحمراره وجفافه، مع شعور بالضيق والحمى.
def: "An inflammatory exfoliative dermatosis involving nearly all of the surface of the skin. Erythroderma develops suddenly. A patchy erythema may generalize and spread to affect most of the skin. Scaling may appear in 2-6 days and be accompanied by hot, red, dry skin, malaise, and fever." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:11606915, PMID:25710899, PMID:25882661, PMID:32555205, PMID:35238435]
comment: Erythroderma can occur at any age. Erythroderma with a congenital or neonatal onset has a different differential diagnosis than adult-onset erythroderma. Several skin disorders may culminate with erythroderma: seborrheic dermatitis/sarcoidosis; contact (allergic or irritant) dermatitis (eg, stasis dermatitis with generalization); atopic dermatitis/autoimmune disease (systemic lupus/dermatomyositis/bullous pemphigoid/pemphigus foliaceus/lichen planus/graft-versus-host disease); lymphoma/leukemia (including SÃ©zary syndrome); psoriasis, including Reiter syndrome/pityriasis rubra pilaris (PRP); infections (human immunodeficiency virus, dermatophytosis), ichthyoses, infestations (Norwegian scabies); drug reactions. Some cases are also associated with erosions (loss of epidermis with an epidermal base), crusting (serous, sanguineous, or pustular), and the potential for hair and nail changes. Exfoliative dermatitis and erythroderma (the preferred term) have been used synonymously in the literature.
synonym: "Exfoliative dermititis" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6908-9849]
synonym: "Generalised erythroderma" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Generalised erythrodermia" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Generalized erythroderma" EXACT []
synonym: "Generalized erythrodermia" EXACT []
synonym: "Red scaly skin caused by inflammatory skin disease" BROAD layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6548-5200]
