[Term]
id: HP:0001351
name: Jerk-locked premyoclonus spikes
synonym: "موجات قُبيل الرَجفان المرتبط بالانتفاض" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نشاط دماغي قبل الحركات اللاإرادية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: استخدام الجمع المرتبط بالانتفاض لتسجيل توقيت وتوزيع النشاط الدماغي الذي يسبق الحركات اللاإرادية السريعة مثل تلك التي تلاحظ في المرضى الذين يعانون من الرَجفان. يمكن للجمع المرتبط بالانتفاض كشف موجة قُبيل الرَجفان حتى في غياب النشاطات الانتيابية في تخطيط كهرباء الدماغ الروتيني.
def: "Jerk-locked averaging (JLA) is used to record the timing and distribution of brain activity preceding brisk involuntary movements such as those observed in patients with myoclonus. JLA is capable of revealing a premyoclonus spike in the absence of paroxysmal activity in the routine EEG." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:1464676, PMID:30653168]
comment: EEG-EMG jerk-locked averaging is a technique that combines EEG and EMG to assess myoclonus. The technique use electromyography (EMG) electrodes for the arms or legs, and correlates averaged EEG responses with EMG bursts used as a trigger.
xref: UMLS:C3552825
is_a: HP:0030178 ! Abnormality of central nervous system electrophysiology

[Term]
id: HP:0001355
name: Megalencephaly
synonym: "تضخم الدماغ" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "كبر حجم الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تضخم شامل لنصفَي المخ يؤدي إلى ضخامة الرأس (وقد يكون مصحوبًا أو غير مصحوب بخلل في التسطح القشري العلوي).
def: "Diffuse enlargement of the entire cerebral hemispheres leading to macrocephaly (with or without overlying cortical dysplasia)." [http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q90573458, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:28658095, PMID:29594439]
comment: Megalencephaly is defined as fronto-occipital diameter above two standard deviations of the mean for the patient's age because of an oversized brain parenchyma. This is different from macrocephaly, which is defined by an enlarged head circumference and therefore accounts also for the size of the extra-axial spaces.
synonym: "Enlarged brain" BROAD layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6548-5200]
synonym: "Macrencephaly" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:19410003
xref: UMLS:C0221355
is_a: HP:0002060 ! Abnormal cerebral morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0001357
name: Plagiocephaly
synonym: "تسطح الرأس" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدم تناظر الرأس" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شكل الرأس غير المتناظر، وعادةً ما يكون مزيجاً من تسطح في الجهة الخلفية من جانب واحد مع بروز أمامي على نفس الجهة، مما يؤدي إلى شكل جمجمي معيني.
alt_id: HP:0001121
def: "Asymmetric head shape, which is usually a combination of unilateral occipital flattening with ipsilateral frontal prominence, leading to rhomboid cranial shape." [PMID:19125436]
comment: Plagiocephaly may affect the posterior skull alone. With plagiocephaly, one can see a combination of unilateral occipital flattening with ipsilateral frontal prominence, leading to rhomboid cranial shape or asymmetry of the posterior skull alone.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Asymmetry of the posterior cranium" BROAD [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Asymmetry of the posterior head" BROAD layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
