alt_id: HP:0004494
alt_id: HP:0005448
alt_id: HP:0005457
alt_id: HP:0005467
alt_id: HP:0008492
def: "Craniosynostosis refers to the premature closure of the cranial sutures. Primary craniosynostosis refers to the closure of one or more sutures due to abnormalities in skull development, and secondary craniosynostosis results from failure of brain growth." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Skull deformity caused by the premature closure of the cranial sutures. Craniostenosis is a deformity of the skull caused by craniosynostosis, with consequent cessation of skull growth.
