[Term]
id: HP:0001540
name: Diastasis recti
synonym: "كماشة العضلة المستقيمة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "فجوة في عضلات البطن" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انفصال عضلة المستقيمة البطنية إلى نصفين أيمن وأيسر (اللذين عادةً ما يكونان مرتبطين عند الخط الأبيض).
def: "A separation of the rectus abdominis muscle into right and left halves (which are normally joined at the midline at the linea alba)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Diastasis recti looks like a ridge, which runs down the middle of the abdomen and increases with muscle straining. Diastasis recti is not uncommon in pregnant women and is common and normal in newborns.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Gap between large left and right abdominal muscles" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6548-5200]
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:62629000
xref: UMLS:C0221766
