alt_id: HP:0009607
alt_id: HP:0010050
def: "Duplication of all or part of the first ray." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19125433]
comment: This term applies for a wide variety of partial and/or complete duplications of the phalanges of the big toe (sometimes including the 1st metatarsal). A partial duplication can present itself on x-rays as a notched phalanx, bifid phalanx or a broadened phalanx. Polydactyly affecting the big toe is called preaxial or hallucal polydactyly of the feet.
synonym: "Partial/complete duplication of the phalanges of the big toe" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
