[Term]
id: HP:0001857
name: Short distal phalanx of toe
synonym: "قصر سلامية القدم النهائية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "قصر العظم الخارجي البعيد في إصبع القدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: قصر المسافة من نهاية إصبع القدم إلى أقرب نقطة بين سلامية أو نقطة انثناء المفصل البعيد بين السلاميات، أي قصر غير طبيعي لسلامية إصبع القدم النهائية.
def: "Short distance from the end of the toe to the most distal interphalangeal crease or distal interphalangeal joint flexion point, i.e., abnormally short distal phalanx of toe." [PMID:19125433]
comment: This term differs from Partial absence of the toe because in that term the phalanx must be missing, whereas here it may be small, but present. Relative shortening of the distal phalanges of the toes can be harder to assess than in the fingers, as they are normally quite short. Distal phalangeal lengths can be assessed subjectively by comparing that digit segment to the rest of the digit, to other normal digits in that patient, or to typical patients of that age or build.
synonym: "Hypoplastic distal phalanges of feet" EXACT []
synonym: "Short outermost bone of toe" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
