[Term]
id: HP:0001922
name: Vacuolated lymphocytes
synonym: "الخلايا اللمفاوية الفجوية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "الخلايا اللمفاوية ذات الفجوات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود فجوات واضحة وحادة التحديد في السيتوبلازم الخاص بالخلايا اللمفاوية.
alt_id: HP:0008147
alt_id: HP:0008329
def: "The presence of clear, sharply defined vacuoles in the lymphocyte cytoplasm." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20633042]
comment: Vacuolated lymphocytes occur most commonly as the peripheral blood manifestation of inherited metabolic disorders, including Niemann-Pick disease Type A, infantile sialic acid storage disorder, Wolman's disease, Mucolipidoses II and III, Salla disease, mannosidosis, Batten disease, GM1 gangliosidosis, neuraminidase deficiency, galactosidosis, fucosidosis, Pompe's disease, aspartylglycosaminuria and rarely, multiple sulfatase deficiency. The metabolic product, which causes vacuolation, depends on the specific enzyme deficiency.
synonym: "Enlarged lysosomal vacuoles in lymphocytes" EXACT []
synonym: "Vacuolated blood lymphocytes" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C1836855
