[Term]
id: HP:0002196
name: Myelopathy
synonym: "اعتلال النخاع" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تلف في الحبل الشوكي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يشير اعتلال النخاع إلى مرض يؤدي إلى حدوث عجز عصبي مرتبط بالحبل الشوكي. يتطلب التشخيص السريري للاعتلال فحصًا تاريخيًا دقيقًا وفحصًا بدنيًا لتحديد متلازمة المرض.  يوصى عادةً بالتصوير العصبي في حالات الاعتلال النخاعي المفاجئ أو تدهور غير مفسر للاعتلال.
def: "Myelopathy is an descriptive term, referring to pathology leading to a neurologic deficit related to the spinal cord. The clinical diagnosis of myelopathy requires a detailed history and physical examination to define the clinical syndrome. Neuroimaging is indicated in most instances of new-onset myelopathy. It is indicated also when the worsening of a myelopathy is unexplained." [PMID:27430455]
comment: This is a descriptive term that should not be used for new annotations. If possible, choose a more precise HPO term that describes the actual observed abnormality.The most frequent etiology of myelopathy is related to degenerative disease of the spine. This can be due to compression of the spinal cord by an osteophyte or extruded disc material in the cervical spine or, less often, in the thoracic spine. Subsequent to degenerative etiology, the next common etiologies are spinal cord compression due to extradural masses caused by metastatic disease to bone or blunt trauma. There are also primary neoplastic, infectious, inflammatory, neurodegenerative, vascular, nutritional, and idiopathic disorders that lead to myelopathy.
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:48522003
xref: UMLS:C0037928
is_a: HP:0002143 ! Abnormal spinal cord morphology
is_a: HP:0034238 ! Closed neural tube defect

[Term]
id: HP:0002197
name: Generalized-onset seizure
synonym: "صرع ذو بدء معمّم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نوبة صرع شاملة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الصرع ذو البدء المعمم هو نوع من النوبات الصرعية التي تنشأ من نقطة معينة داخل الشبكات المنتشرة ثنائياً بشرية بشكل سريع. قد تتضمن الشبكات مناطق قشرية وتحت قشرية ولكن ليس بالضرورة كامل القشرة.
