def: "A form of hydrocephalus characterized by enlarged cerebral ventricles and normal cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) pressure upon lumbar puncture." [eMedicine:1135286, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Normal pressure hydrocephalus rarely occurs in patients younger than 60 years.
