[Term]
id: HP:0002444
name: Hypothalamic hamartoma
synonym: "ورم وعائي تحتي المهاد" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ورم في منطقة تحت المهاد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود ورم وعائي في منطقة تحت المهاد.
def: "The presence of a hamartoma of the hypothalamus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Hypothalamic hamartoma is a malformation, not a tumor. Hypothalamic hamartomas grow at the rate of, or slower than, the surrounding brain tissue. A hamartoma of the hypothalamus appears as a non-enhancing mass in the floor of the third ventricle posterior to the optic chiasm that is isointense to gray matter on T1 and T2 pulse sequences of an MRI, but may have distinct intensity on FLAIR (neither cranial CT examination nor cranial ultrasound examination is adequate for diagnosis of hypothalamic hamartom). Individuals with hypothalamic hamartomas may have neurologic symptoms, although most are asymptomatic. Removal of the hypothalamic hamartoma is not indicated and often results in iatrogenic pituitary insufficiency.
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:237714006
xref: UMLS:C0342418
is_a: HP:0009731 ! Cerebral hamartoma
is_a: HP:0012286 ! Abnormal hypothalamus morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0002445
name: Tetraplegia
synonym: "شلل رباعي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شلل جميع الأطراف" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شلل في جميع الأطراف والجذع تحت مستوى إصابة مرتبطة في الحبل الشوكي. أسباب الشلل الرباعي مشابهة لتلك في الشلل النصفي إلا أن الإصابة موجودة في الحبل الشوكي العنقي بدلاً من القطاعات الصدرية أو القطنية.
alt_id: HP:0010552
def: "Paralysis of all four limbs, and trunk of the body below the level of an associated injury to the spinal cord. The etiology of quadriplegia is similar to that of paraplegia except that the lesion is in the cervical spinal cord rather than in the thoracic or lumbar segments of the spinal cord." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Paralysis of all four limbs" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Quadriplegia" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:11538006
xref: UMLS:C0034372
is_a: HP:0030182 ! Tetraplegia/tetraparesis

