[Term]
id: HP:0002486
name: Myotonia
synonym: "تشنج عضلي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تأخير غير إرادي وغير مؤلم في ارتخاء العضلات الهيكلية بعد انقباضها أو تحفيزها كهربائياً.
alt_id: HP:0003632
alt_id: HP:0003754
alt_id: HP:0003792
def: "An involuntary and painless delay in the relaxation of skeletal muscle following contraction or electrical stimulation." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Patients often describe myotonia as stiffness that is worse at the onset of activity and that improves with repeated muscle contractions. Myotonia tends to worsen in cold weather. Myotonia can be elicited by voluntary muscle contraction of by muscle percussion (e.g., by tapping the thenar eminence). During physical examination, myotonia may be elicited by asking the patient to make a tight fist and then quickly open the hand. Myotonia is caused by an abnormality in the muscle membrane, i.e., of the ion channels that control the contraction of muscle fibers.
synonym: "Delayed relaxation of muscle fibers after contraction" EXACT []
synonym: "Delayed relaxation of muscle fibres after contraction" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:3434004
xref: UMLS:C0027125
is_a: HP:0011804 ! Abnormal muscle physiology

