[Term]
id: HP:0002495
name: Impaired vibratory sensation
synonym: "ضعف الإحساس بالاهتزاز" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انخفاض القدرة على إدراك الاهتزاز. عادةً يتم اختبار ذلك إكلينيكياً باستخدام شوكة رنانة تهتز بتردد 128 هرتز وتُستخدم على أماكن بارزة في العظام مثل الكاحلين أو المفاصل السلامية المشطية في اليدين. يحدث تلاشي بطيء للاهتزاز من الشوكة الرنانة. يمكن تقدير درجة فقدان الإحساس بالاهتزاز بشكل تقريبي بعدد الثواني التي يستطيع الفاحص إدراك الاهتزاز أطول من المريض.
alt_id: HP:0006836
alt_id: HP:0007116
def: "A decrease in the ability to perceive vibration. Clinically, this is usually tested with a tuning fork which vibrates at 128 Hz and is applied to bony prominences such as the malleoli at the ankles or the metacarpal-phalangeal joints. There is a slow decay of vibration from the tuning fork. The degree of vibratory sense loss can be crudely estimated by counting the number of seconds that the examiner can perceive the vibration longer than the patient." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Impaired vibratory sensation may suggesti involvement of the posterior column-medial lemniscus pathway, which is responsible for transmitting fine touch, vibration and conscious proprioceptive information from the body to the cerebral cortex.
synonym: "Decreased vibration sense" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Decreased vibratory sense" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Diminished vibratory sense" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Hypopallesthesia" EXACT []
synonym: "Impaired vibratory sensation" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Impaired vibratory sense" EXACT layperson []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:130980003
xref: UMLS:C1295585
is_a: HP:0010831 ! Impaired proprioception

