[Term]
id: HP:0002511
name: Alzheimer disease
synonym: "مرض الزهايمر" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مرض تنكسي في الدماغ يتميز ببدء تدريجي للخرف. تتبع اختلال الذاكرة والحكم ومدى الانتباه ومهارات حل المشكلات، بأبراكيسيا شديدة وفقدان كامل للقدرات المعرفية. يحدث الشرط بشكل رئيسي بعد سن 60، ويتميز مرضيًا بضمور قشري حاد وثلاثية اللويحات الشيخوخة، التشابكات الليفية العصبية، والخيوط العصبية.
alt_id: HP:0006878
alt_id: HP:0007213
def: "A degenerative disease of the brain characterized by the insidious onset of dementia. Impairment of memory, judgment, attention span, and problem solving skills are followed by severe apraxia and a global loss of cognitive abilities. The condition primarily occurs after age 60, and is marked pathologically by severe cortical atrophy and the triad of senile plaques, neurofibrillary tangles, and neuropil threads." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Note that this is a bundled term that refers to a disease rather than to phenotypic features. It is retained for convenience since Alzheimer disease is used for annotation of other diseases (e.g., Down syndrome) as if it were a feature. If possible it is preferable to annotate with the precise phenotypic features.
synonym: "Alzheimer disease" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Late-onset form of familial Alzheimer disease" EXACT layperson []
xref: DOID:10652
xref: MONDO:0004975
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:230267005
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:26929004
xref: UMLS:C0002395
xref: UMLS:C1863051
is_a: HP:0002011 ! Morphological central nervous system abnormality

