def: "The presence of calcium deposition within the cerebrum." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: This finding can be demonstrated upon cerebral computer tomography, magnetic resonance imaging, or potentially by standard radiography of the skull. The cerebrum is the largest of the five major components of the brain, which comprise the cerebrum, cerebellum, brain stem, pituitary gland, and hypothalamus.
synonym: "Abnormal deposits of calcium in the brain" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6548-5200]
