xref: SNOMEDCT_US:29980002
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:48641006
xref: UMLS:C0221210
is_a: HP:0002242 ! Abnormal intestine morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0002570
name: Steatorrhea
synonym: "إسهال دهني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "دهون في البراز" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة في كمية الدهون في البراز عن المعدل الطبيعي. يحدث هذا نتيجة سوء امتصاص الدهون في الأمعاء الدقيقة ويؤدي إلى براز رغوي ذو رائحة كريهة يطفو.
def: "Greater than normal amounts of fat in the feces. This is a result of malabsorption of lipids in the small intestine and results in frothy foul-smelling fecal matter that floats." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Fat in faeces" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Fat in feces" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6548-5200]
synonym: "Fatty stool" EXACT []
synonym: "Greasy stools" EXACT layperson []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:27868004
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:66187002
xref: UMLS:C0038238
is_a: HP:0002630 ! Fat malabsorption

[Term]
id: HP:0002571
name: Achalasia
synonym: "تعذر الارتخاء" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تعذر ارتخاء المريء" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: اضطراب في حركية المريء يتميز بعدم قدرة العضلة العاصرة السفلية للمريء على الارتخاء أثناء البلع وكفاية أو غياب التقلصات في النصف السفلي من جسم المريء.
def: "A disorder of esophageal motility characterized by the inability of the lower esophageal sphincter to relax during swallowing and by inadequate or lacking peristalsis in the lower half of the body of the esophagus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Achalasia may lead to regurgitation of food, chest pain, cough, and difficulty swallowing.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Achalasia of the esophagus" EXACT []
synonym: "Achalasia of the oesophagus" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: MEDDRA:10030136 "Oesophageal achalasia"
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:45564002
xref: UMLS:C0014848
is_a: HP:0031857 ! Ineffective esophageal peristalsis

