alt_id: HP:0004477
alt_id: HP:0005459
def: "Trilobar skull configuration when viewed from the front or behind." [PMID:19125436, PMID:29089832]
comment: A deformity of the skull that resembles a cloverleaf and is characterized by very prominent temporal bones with constriction of the remainder of the cranium. Cloverleaf skull is commonly accompanied by hydrocephalus. See figure 3 in PMID:29089832.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Cloverleaf cranium shape" BROAD layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
