[Term]
id: HP:0002728
name: Chronic mucocutaneous candidiasis
synonym: "داء المبيضات المخاطي الجلدي المزمن" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى فطرية مزمنة في الجلد والأغشية المخاطية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى سطحية متكررة أو مستمرة بفطر المبيضات في الجلد والأغشية المخاطية والأظافر.
alt_id: HP:0005392
def: "Recurrent or persistent superficial Candida infections of the skin, mucous membranes, and nails." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20859203]
comment: The most commonly involved Candida species is Candida albicans. Chronic mucocutaneous candidiasis (CMC) is usually confined to the cutaneous surface without systemic dissemination. CMC does not represent a specific disease, but rather a phenotypic feature of several immunologic, endocrinologic, and autoimmune disorders.
synonym: "Chronic candidiasis of mucosa, skin and nails" EXACT []
synonym: "Mucocutaneous candidiasis" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:234568006
xref: UMLS:C0006845
is_a: HP:0011370 ! Recurrent cutaneous fungal infections

[Term]
id: HP:0002729
name: Follicular hyperplasia
synonym: "فرط تنسج جريبي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة نمو الجريبات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: اعتلال العقد اللمفاوية ناتج عن فرط تنسج في المراكز الجريبية.
def: "Lymphadenopathy (enlargement of lymph nodes) owing to hyperplasia of follicular (germinal) centers." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:23281438, PMID:27929264]
comment: Lymphadenopathy can be defined as enlargement of lymph nodes. It is just a sign accompanying a great variety of entities with multiple etiologies: acute vs. chronic, benign vs. malignant. One of the most commonly seen histological pictures is lymphadenopathy owing to hyperplasia of follicular (germinal centers) but this one is by far not the only one.
xref: UMLS:C4014733
is_a: HP:0002716 ! Lymphadenopathy

[Term]
id: HP:0002730
name: Chronic noninfectious lymphadenopathy
synonym: "اعتلال العقد اللمفاوية المزمن غير المعدي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تورم مزمن غير معدي في العقد اللمفاوية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شكل مزمن من اعتلال العقد اللمفاوية الذي لا يرتبط بعدوى.
def: "A chronic form of lymphadenopathy that is not related to infection." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: UMLS:C1858970
is_a: HP:0002716 ! Lymphadenopathy

[Term]
id: HP:0002731
name: Decreased T cell apoptosis
synonym: "انخفاض في موت الخلايا المبرمج للخلايا التائية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نقص موت الخلايا التائية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انخفاض غير طبيعي في موت الخلايا المبرمج للخلايا التائية في الدم المحيطي في ثقافة مختبرية مقارنة بعينة تحكم صحية. قد يكون تلقائيًا أو مستحثًا بواسطة الأشعة فوق البنفسجية أو الأشعة السينية أو عوامل أخرى. يتم قياسه عادة من خلال التعبير السطحي للفوسفاتيد سيرين بواسطة Annexin V، ولكن قد تستخدم طرق أخرى مثل تصبغ الكاسبازات المتحللة.
def: "Abnormal decrease of apoptosis by peripheral blood T cells in an in vitro culture, compared to a healthy control sample. May be either spontaneous, induced by UV, X-ray, FasL or other agens. Commonly measured by surface expression of phosphatidyl serine labelled by Annexin V, but other methods such as staning of cleaved Caspases may be used by different laboratories." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Apoptosis, a form of programmed cell death, is an important mechanism that prevents uncontrolled proliferation of activated lymphocytes and regulates lymphocyte homeostasis.
synonym: "Defective lymphocyte apoptosis" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C1858969
is_a: HP:0030886 ! Abnormal T cell apoptosis

