[Term]
id: HP:0002930
name: Impaired sensitivity to thyroid hormone
synonym: "مقاومة لهرمون الغدة الدرقية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مقاومة هرمون الغدة الدرقية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انخفاض حساسية الأعضاء الطرفية لهرمون الغدة الدرقية يتميز بارتفاع مستويات هرمون الغدة الدرقية الحر في الدم مع عدم كبح هرمون تحفيز الغدة الدرقية.
alt_id: HP:0008215
alt_id: HP:0008243
alt_id: HP:0008262
def: "Reduced sensitivity of end organs to thyroid hormone characterized by elevated serum levels of free thyroid hormone with nonsuppressed thyroid stimulating hormone." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0538-4547, PMID:24847459]
comment: Impaired sensitivity to thyroid hormone may be accompanied by goiter and no clear symptoms and signs of thyrotoxicosis. The etiologies of this feature include defects in the thyroid hormone receptor, reduced cellular access of the biologically active thyroid hormone, T3 related to defects of thyroid hormone cell membrane transport, and a defect reducing the intracellular metabolism generating T3 from T4.
synonym: "Elevated serum levels of free thyroid hormone with nonsuppressed TSH" EXACT []
synonym: "End-organ unresponsiveness to thyroid hormone" EXACT []
synonym: "Resistance to thyroid hormone" EXACT []
synonym: "Thyroid hormone receptor defect" EXACT []
synonym: "Thyroid hormone resistance" EXACT []
