def: "An increased concentration of hydroxyproline in the blood." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:gcarletti]
comment: Hydroxyproline is an imino acid normally present in human plasma and is derived primarily from endogenous collagen turnover and the breakdown of dietary collagen. Hyperhydroxyprolinemic patients show hydroxyproline blood levels between 150 and 500 micromole per liter. Normal levels are around 10-20 micromole per liter.
synonym: "High blood hydroxyproline levels" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
