[Term]
id: HP:0003467
name: Atlantoaxial instability
synonym: "عدم استقرار الأطلسي المحوري" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة حركة الفقرات العنقية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة غير طبيعية في الحركة عند الالتحام بين الفقرة العنقية الأولى (الأطلس) والفقرة العنقية الثانية (المحور) نتيجة لخلل في العظام أو الأربطة.
def: "Abnormally increased movement at the junction between the first cervical (atlas) and the second cervical (axis) vertebrae as a result of either a bony or ligamentous anomaly." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Neurological deficits ensue if the odontoid process, or posterior arch of the atlas, impinges on the spinal cord.
subset: hposlim_core
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:202820009
xref: UMLS:C0410653
is_a: HP:0003413 ! Atlantoaxial abnormality

[Term]
id: HP:0003468
name: Abnormal vertebral morphology
synonym: "شذوذ في شكل الفقرات" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شكل غير طبيعي للفقرات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ يحدث في واحدة أو أكثر من الفقرات في العمود الفقري.
alt_id: HP:0005719
def: "An abnormality of one or more of the vertebrae." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: A vertebra is one of 33 bony segments that form the spinal column of humans. There are 7 cervical, 12 thoracic, 5 lumbar, 5 sacral and 4 coccygeal vertebrae (the coccygeal vertebrae are fused into one coccyx bone).
synonym: "Abnormal vertebrae" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormality of the vertebrae" EXACT []
synonym: "Multiple vertebral anomalies" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Vertebral anomalies" EXACT []
