[Term]
id: HP:0003528
name: Elevated circulating calcitonin concentration
synonym: "زيادة تركيز الكالسيتونين في الدم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة الكالسيتونين في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تركيز هرمون الكالسيتونين، وهو بيتيد مكون من 32 حمض أميني يُنتج بشكل أساسي من خلايا الجريب الدرقي في الغدة الدرقية، في الدورة الدموية يفوق الحد العلوي الطبيعي.
def: "Concentration of calcitonin, a 32-amino acid polypeptide hormone that is produced primarily by the parafollicular cells of the thyroid, in the blood circulation above the upper limit of normal." []
comment: Calcitonin is a 32-amino acid polypeptide hormone that is produced primarily by the parafollicular cells of the thyroid. It acts to reduce blood calcium (Ca2+), opposing the effects of parathyroid hormone.
synonym: "Elevated calcitonin" EXACT layperson []
xref: UMLS:C1868394
is_a: HP:0034902 ! Abnormal circulating calcitonin concentration

[Term]
id: HP:0003529
name: Parathormone-independent increased renal tubular calcium reabsorption
synonym: "زيادة امتصاص الكالسيوم في الأنابيب الكلوية المستقلة عن هرمون الغدة الجار درقية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة امتصاص الكالسيوم في الكلى بدون تأثير هرموني" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: هو زيادة في إعادة امتصاص الكالسيوم بواسطة الأنابيب الكلوية التي لا ترتبط بمستويات مرتفعة من هرمون الغدة الجار درقية.
def: "An increase in the reabsorption of calcium by the renal tubulus that is not associated with increased parathormone levels." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:23802516]
comment: This feature is seen with familial hypocalciuric hypercalcemia. This disease has three known genetic etiologies, in type 1 there is a loss of function mutation in the calcium-sensing receptor (encoded by CASR), in type 2 there is a gain of function mutation in GNA11, which is involved in calcium-sensing receptor signaling, and in type 3 there is a mutation in AP2S1, which encodes the adaptor-related protein complex 2, sigma 1 subunit, which alters calcium-sensing receptor endocytosis.
synonym: "Parathormone-independent increased renal tubular Ca reabsorption" EXACT abbreviation [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7941-2961]
synonym: "Parathormone-independent increased renal tubular Ca2+ reabsorption" EXACT abbreviation [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7941-2961]
xref: UMLS:C4025604
is_a: HP:0003110 ! Abnormality of urine homeostasis

