[Term]
id: HP:0003606
name: Absent urinary urothione
synonym: "غياب اليروثيون البولي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "غياب اليروثيون في البول" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نقصان في اليروثيون (المستقلب البولي للموليبدنوم) في البول.
def: "Lack of urothione (the urinary metabolite of molybdenum cofactor) in the urine." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:6960353]
comment: Urothione, a sulfur-containing pterin, is the normal metabolic degradation product of the molybdenum cofactor.
xref: UMLS:C4025591
is_a: HP:0033354 ! Abnormal urine metabolite level

[Term]
id: HP:0003607
name: 4-hydroxyphenylacetic aciduria
synonym: "4-هيدروكسي فينيل أسيتيك أسيدوريا" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة مستوى 4-هيدروكسي فينيل أسيتيك أسيد في البول" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة تركيز حمض 4-هيدروكسي فينيل أسيتيك في البول.
alt_id: HP:0033304
def: "Increased concentration of 4-hydroxyphenylacetic acid in the urine." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: 4-Hydroxyphenylpyruvate dioxygenase participates in the tyrosine catabolic pathway by catalyzing the conversion of 4-hydroxyphenylpyruvate to homogentisate. A deficiency in this enzyme can result in 4-Hydroxyphenylacetic aciduria.
synonym: "Elevated urine 4-hydroxyphenylacetic acid level" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C1848680
is_a: HP:0040156 ! Elevated urinary carboxylic acid

[Term]
id: HP:0003609
name: Foam cells with lamellar inclusion bodies
synonym: "خلايا رغوية مع أجسام شمولية صفيحية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وجود خلايا رغوية مع مكونات صفيحية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود خلايا رغوية تحتوي على أجسام شمولية لاميلارية.
def: "The presence of foam cells that contain lamellar inclusion bodies." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Foam cells with lamellar inclusion bodies are thought to be a hallmark of cellular phospholipidosis, i.e., of the excess accumulation of phospholipids. This abnormality can be assayed by electron microscopy.
xref: UMLS:C4025590
is_a: HP:0003651 ! Foam cells

[Term]
id: HP:0003610
name: Fibroblast metachromasia
synonym: "تلون الليفoblast metachromasia" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تلون الخلايا الليفية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة تلون السيتوبلازم في الخلايا الليفية مع الصبغة الزرقاء التولويدينية.
def: "Increased cytoplasmic staining of fibroblasts with toluidine blue." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:4195824]
comment: Cultured fibroblasts from the genetic mucopolysaccharidoses store higher than normal amounts of glycosaminoglyeans. Histochemical stains such as toluidine blue and Alcian blue can be used to detect such intracellular glycosaminoglycans which, being negatively charged, are bound and precipitated by the cationic dyes. Cultured fibroblasts from homozygotes -and heterozygotes for the genetic mucopolysaccharidoses accumulate excessive quantities of glycosaminoglycans. The cytoplasmic staining with toluidine blue is referred to as metachromasia (pink) and orthochromasia (blue) and that with Alcian blue as alcianophilia.
xref: UMLS:C1835008
is_a: HP:0003653 ! Cellular metachromasia

[Term]
id: HP:0003612
name: Positive ferric chloride test
synonym: "اختبار كلوريد الحديد الموجب" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: إذا كان الاختبار موجبًا، فإنه يشير إلى زيادة تركيز الفينولات في البول أو الدم.
def: "If positive, the ferric chloride test indicates an increased concentration of phenols in the urine or blood." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The ferric chloride test indicates presence of high levels of phenylpyruvate in urine, because ferric ion forms a blue-green colored complex with phenylpyruvate. Some other compounds can also lead to a positive ferric chloride test. The ferric chloride test is no longer used in modern clinical practice, but this term is kept for historical reasons. The urine phenylpyruvate concentration is elevated in phenylketonuria.
synonym: "Positive FeCl3 test" EXACT abbreviation [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7941-2961]
xref: UMLS:C4025589
is_a: HP:0010893 ! Abnormal circulating phenylalanine concentration

[Term]
id: HP:0003613
name: Antiphospholipid antibody positivity
synonym: "وجود الأجسام المضادة للفوسفوليبيد" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وجود أجسام مضادة للفوسفوليبيد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود الأجسام المضادة الذاتية للفوسفوليبيدات في الدورة الدموية.
def: "The presence of circulating autoantibodies to phospholipids." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: This group of autoantibodies comprises anticardiolipin, antiphosphatidylinositol, atiphosphatidylglycerol, and antiphosphatidylserine antibodies.
synonym: "Antiphospholipid antibodies" EXACT []
synonym: "Antiphospholipid antibody" EXACT []
synonym: "Phospholipid antibody positivity" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4019436
is_a: HP:0030057 ! Autoimmune antibody positivity

[Term]
id: HP:0003614
name: Trimethylaminuria
synonym: "ثلاثي ميثيل أمينوريا" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة ثلاثي ميثيل أمين في البول" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة تركيز ثلاثي ميثيل أمين في البول.
def: "Increased concentration of trimethylamine in the urine." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Increased concentration of trimethylamine, an organic amino compound with an odor characterized as that of rotting fish, in the urine. Trimethylaminuria is generally caused by impaired oxidation of trimethylamine into the odorless compound trimethylamine N-oxide.
synonym: "High urine trimethylamine levels" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:237959005
xref: UMLS:C0342739
is_a: HP:0033354 ! Abnormal urine metabolite level

