[Term]
id: HP:0004222
name: Cone-shaped epiphysis of the distal phalanx of the 5th finger
synonym: "شذوذ في مخروطية مشاشة السلامية البعيدة للإصبع الخامس" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نهاية مخروطية لإصبع الخنصر" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ظهور مخروطي للمشاشة في السلامية البعيدة للإصبع الصغير لليد، مما ينتج عنه مظهر 'كرة في مقبس'. تقع هذه المشاشة في النهاية القريبة للسلامية وهي عادة ما تكون مسطحة تقريباً.
def: "A cone-shaped appearance of the epiphysis of the distal phalanx of the little finger of the hand, producing a 'ball-in-a-socket' appearance. This epiphysis is located at the proximal end of the phalanx and is normally nearly flat. The related entity 'angel-shaped' epiphysis refers to a pronounced cone-shaped epiphysis in combination with a pseudoepiphysis at the distal end of the phalanx." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Cone-shaped end part of the outermost little finger bone" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Cone-shaped end part of the outermost pinkie finger bone" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Cone-shaped end part of the outermost pinky finger bone" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Cone-shaped epiphysis of the distal phalanx of the little finger" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4021675
is_a: HP:0009198 ! Abnormality of the epiphysis of the distal phalanx of the 5th finger
is_a: HP:0009384 ! Cone-shaped epiphyses of the 5th finger
is_a: HP:0010248 ! Cone-shaped epiphyses of the distal phalanges of the hand

