def: "An abnormality of glycosphingolipid metabolism." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Glycosphingolipids are a subtype of glycolipids containing the amino alcohol sphingosine. A glycosphingolipid is a carbohydrate-containing derivative of a sphingoid or ceramide. It is understood that the carbohydrate residue is attached by a glycosidic linkage to O-1 of the sphingoid.
