creation_date: 2008-03-17T03:22:00Z

[Term]
id: HP:0004359
name: Abnormal circulating fatty-acid concentration
synonym: "خلل تركيز الأحماض الدهنية في الدورة الدموية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في تركيز الأحماض الدهنية في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انحراف عن التركيز الطبيعي لحمض دهني في الدورة الدموية، مما قد يؤثر على الوظائف البيولوجية المرتبطة بها.
def: "A deviation from the normal concentration of a fatty acid in the blood circulation." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: A fatty acid is an aliphatic monocarboxylic acid derived from or contained in esterified form. Natural fatty acids commonly have a chain of 4 to 28 carbons (usually unbranched and even-numbered), which may be saturated or unsaturated. R-COOH. Fatty acids are usually derived from triglycerides or phospholipids.
synonym: "Abnormality of fatty acid metabolism" EXACT []
synonym: "Fatty acids abnormal" RELATED []
