alt_id: HP:0004773
def: "Anterior cervical hypertrichosis (ACH) or 'hairy throat' refers to the presence of a tuft of terminal hair on the anterior neck, just above the laryngeal prominence." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20400390]
