synonym: "الرفرفة الأذينية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "اضطراب في نبض القلب الأذيني" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من اضطرابات نبض القلب الأذينية يتميز بمعدلات نبض أذينية بين 240 و400 نبضة في الدقيقة وبعض درجة انسداد في العقدة الأذينية البطينية. عادةً ما تكون معدل النبض البطيني نصف معدل النبض الأذيني. في تخطيط كهربية القلب؛ تظهر موجات الرفرفة الأذينية كنشاط أذيني يشبه أسنان المنشار. فيزيولوجيًا، تعتبر الرفرفة الأذينية شكلًا من أشكال إعادة الدخول الأذيني حيث توجد دفعة كهربائية مبكرة تخلق دائرة ذاتية الانتشار.
def: "A type of atrial arrhythmia characterized by atrial rates of between 240 and 400 beats per minute and some degree of atrioventricular node conduction block. Typically, the ventricular rate is half the atrial rate. In the EKG; atrial flutter waves are observed as sawtooth-like atrial activity. Pathophysiologically, atrial flutter is a form of atrial reentry in which there is a premature electrical impulse creates a self-propagating circuit." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Atrial flutter can lead to palpitations, fatigue, dyspnea, and chest pain. Atrial flutter can be paroxysmal or persistent.
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:5370000
xref: UMLS:C0004239
is_a: HP:0001692 ! Atrial arrhythmia

[Term]
id: HP:0004751
name: Paroxysmal ventricular tachycardia
synonym: "تسارع بطيني انتيابي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نبض قلب سريع ومفاجئ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوبات من التسارع البطيني تبدأ وتنتهي فجأة.
alt_id: HP:0005141
def: "Episodes of ventricular tachycardia that have a sudden onset and ending." []
synonym: "Episodes of ventricular tachycardia" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:66657009
xref: UMLS:C0030591
is_a: HP:0004756 ! Ventricular tachycardia

[Term]
id: HP:0004752
name: Congenital atrioventricular dissociation
synonym: "انفصال أذيني بطيني خلقي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "فصل خلقي بين الأذينين والبطينين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شكل من أشكال الانفصال الأذيني البطيني حيث يكون الأذينان والبطينات تحت سيطرة منظمين مختلفين للإيقاع مع بدء خلقي.
def: "A form of atrioventricular (AV) dissociation (i.e., the atria and the ventricles are under the control of two separate pacemakers) with congenital onset." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: UMLS:C4025299
is_a: HP:0011709 ! Atrioventricular dissociation

[Term]
id: HP:0004754
name: Permanent atrial fibrillation
synonym: "رجفان أذيني دائم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "رجفان دائم في الأذينات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الرجفان الأذيني (AF) الذي لا يمكن إنهاؤه بواسطة تقويم النظم، وحيث يكون طويل الأمد (أكثر من عام) والذي لم يُشر إلى تقويم النظم أو لم يُحاول، يعتبر دائمًا.
def: "Atrial fibrillation (AF) that cannot be successfully terminated by cardioversion, and longstanding (more than 1 year) AF, where cardioversion is not indicated or has not been attempted, is termed permanent." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:12860883]
comment: The natural history of atrial fibrillation (AF) is characterized by a gradual worsening with time. AF itself produces changes in atrial function and structure. Note there is no precise definition of the duration of AF required to be regarded as chronic.
synonym: "Chronic atrial fibrillation" RELATED []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:426749004
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:440028005
xref: UMLS:C0694539
xref: UMLS:C2586056
is_a: HP:0005110 ! Atrial fibrillation

[Term]
id: HP:0004755
name: Supraventricular tachycardia
synonym: "تسرع القلب فوق البطيني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة سرعة نبض القلب" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تسرع القلب فوق البطيني (SVT) هو زيادة غير طبيعية في معدل نبض القلب (أكثر من 100 نبضة في الدقيقة أثناء الراحة) مع مصدر أعلى من مستوى البطينين.
def: "Supraventricular tachycardia (SVT) is an abnormally increased heart rate (over 100 beats per minute at rest) with origin above the level of the ventricles." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:DDD_dbrown, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: A narrow complex (QRS width less than 120 milliseconds) reflects rapid activation of the ventricles via the normal conduction pathway, i.e. His-Purkinje system, which in turn suggests that the tachycardia originated above the AV node and is thus supraventricular.
synonym: "Supraventricular tachyarrhythmia" EXACT []
synonym: "SVT" EXACT abbreviation []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:6456007
xref: UMLS:C0039240
xref: UMLS:C1698480
is_a: HP:0001649 ! Tachycardia
is_a: HP:0005115 ! Supraventricular arrhythmia

[Term]
id: HP:0004756
name: Ventricular tachycardia
synonym: "تسرع القلب البطيني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة سرعة نبض القلب" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تسرع القلب الذي ينشأ من البطينين والذي يتميز بمعدل نبض سريع (أكثر من 100 نبضة في الدقيقة) ومركبات QRS عريضة (أكثر من 120 مللي ثانية).
def: "A tachycardia originating in the ventricles characterized by rapid heart rate (over 100 beats per minute) and broad QRS complexes (over 120 ms)." []
comment: Ventricular tachycardia (VT) is a potentially life-threatening ventricular arrhythmia that presents as a wide QRS complex tachycardia, and is defined as three or more consecutive QRS complexes with a duration longer than 120 milliseconds (ms) and a rate of 100 beats per minute or more, whereby the complexes have a ventricular origin. VT can be subdivided as follows: (i) sustained VT persists for 30 seconds or more; (ii) non-sustained VT lasts less than 30 seconds; (iii) monomorphic VT displays a uniform QRS morphology; and (iv) polymorphic VT displays QRS morphologies that variy from beat to beat. VT is observed most commonly in individuals with structural heart disease or acute myocardial infarction (MI). VT may also be observed in in the setting of drug toxicity or electrolyte abnormalities or in individuals with Mendelian disease.
xref: Fyler:7160
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:25569003
xref: UMLS:C0042514
is_a: HP:0001649 ! Tachycardia

[Term]
id: HP:0004757
name: Paroxysmal atrial fibrillation
synonym: "رجفان أذيني انتيابي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "رجفان أذيني متقطع" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: هي نوبات من الرجفان الأذيني تدوم عادة لبضع ساعات وحتى يوم واحد وتنتهي بشكل تلقائي.
def: "Episodes of atrial fibrillation that typically last for several hours up to one day and terminate spontaneously." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:30571060]
synonym: "Atrial fibrillation, paroxysmal" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Intermittent atrial fibrillation" EXACT []
synonym: "Paroxysmal AF" EXACT abbreviation []
