[Term]
id: HP:0004942
name: Aortic aneurysm
synonym: "أم الدم الأورطية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تضخم في الأورطى" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: توسع الأورطى يشير إلى حجم أكبر من النسبة المئوية لـ95 بالنسبة إلى الشخص الطبيعي حسب العمر والجنس وحجم الجسم. على النقيض، تُعرف أم الدم الأورطية بأنها توسيع محلي للأورطى يتعدى 150 بالمئة من الحجم المتوقع. يجب التمييز بين أم الدم والتمدد، الذي يكون ممتدًا لأكثر من 50 بالمئة من حجم الأورطى الطبيعي.
alt_id: HP:0001724
def: "Aortic dilatation refers to a dimension that is greater than the 95th percentile for the normal person age, sex and body size. In contrast, an aneurysm is defined as a localized dilation of the aorta that is more than 150 percent of predicted (ratio of observed to expected diameter 1.5 or more). Aneurysm should be distinguished from ectasia, which represents a diffuse dilation of the aorta less than 50 percent of normal aorta diameter." []
comment: Aneurysm is considered a severe (pathological) form of dilatation of a segment of a blood vessel. In clinical practice, dilatation and aneurysm are occasionally used interchangeably. In this subhierarchy, we therefore use aneurysm as the primary label and list dilatation as a broad synonym.
synonym: "Aortic dilatation" EXACT []
synonym: "Bulge in wall of large artery that carries blood away from heart" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6548-5200]
synonym: "Enlarged aorta" EXACT layperson []
xref: Fyler:2301
xref: Fyler:2708
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:67362008
xref: UMLS:C0003486
is_a: HP:0001679 ! Abnormal aortic morphology
is_a: HP:0002617 ! Vascular dilatation

[Term]
id: HP:0004943
name: Accelerated atherosclerosis
synonym: "تصلب شرايين متسارع" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تراكم سريع للترسبات في الشرايين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تصلب الشرايين الذي يحدث في شخص يعاني من عوامل خطر معينة (مثل الذئبة الحمامية الجهازية، السكري، التدخين، ارتفاع ضغط الدم، ارتفاع الكوليسترول) في سن مبكرة مقارنة بمن لا يجتمع فيه تلك العوامل.
def: "Atherosclerosis which occurs in a person with certain risk factors (e.g., SLE, diabetes, smoking, hypertension, hypercholesterolaemia, family history of early heart disease) at an earlier age than would occur in another person without those risk factors." [PMID:29040156]
synonym: "Accelerated plaque build-up in arteries" BROAD layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
xref: UMLS:C1849618
xref: UMLS:C4280504
is_a: HP:0002621 ! Atherosclerosis

