[Term]
id: HP:0004950
name: Peripheral arterial stenosis
synonym: "تضيق شرياني محيطي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تضيق شرايين الأطراف" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تضيق الشرايين الطرفية مما يقلل من تدفق الدم إلى الأطراف. يمكن قياس هذه الخاصية بمؤشر الضغط الكاحلي العضدي أقل من 0.9، وقد يظهر سريرياً على شكل عرج.
alt_id: HP:0004928
alt_id: HP:0004973
alt_id: HP:0005296
alt_id: HP:0005299
alt_id: HP:0005309
alt_id: HP:0005315
alt_id: HP:0005794
def: "Narrowing of peripheral arteries with reduction of blood flow to the limbs. This feature may be quantified as an ankle-brachial index of less than 0.9, and may be manifested clinically as claudication." []
comment: The ankle-brachial index (ABI; the ratio of systolic blood pressure in the ankle to that in the arm), is a measure of occlusion of peripheral arteries in the leg. Peripheral arterial stenosis may be observed with atherosclerosis and with increased intima media thickness as seen in diseases such as pseudoxanthoma elasticum. The most common cause of peripheral arterial stenosis in patients over 40 years of age is atherosclerosis. Cerebral and coronary arteries are by definition not included in peripheral artery disease.
synonym: "Arterial disease of legs" RELATED []
synonym: "Occlusive arterial disease" RELATED []
synonym: "Occlusive vascular disease" RELATED []
synonym: "Peripheral artery disease" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6908-9849]
synonym: "Peripheral artery occlusive disease" RELATED []
synonym: "Peripheral vascular disease" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:399957001
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:400047006
xref: UMLS:C0085096
xref: UMLS:C1704436
is_a: HP:0100545 ! Arterial stenosis

