[Term]
id: HP:0005121
name: Posterior scalloping of vertebral bodies
synonym: "تحدب خلفي للأجسام الفقرية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انحناء خلفي للفقرات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود تقعر مفرط على السطح الخلفي لجسم فقري واحد أو أكثر.
alt_id: HP:0004572
alt_id: HP:0004579
def: "An excessive concavity of the posterior surface of one or more vertebral bodies." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The posterior vertebral scalloping sign appears on a lateral radiograph of the spine as an exaggeration of the normal concavity of the posterior surface of one or more vertebral bodies. Neurofibromatosis may be associated with marked scalloping of the posterior borders of the vertebral bodies resulting from intraspinal tumors.
synonym: "Posterior vertebral body scalloping" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C1850196
is_a: HP:0004586 ! Biconcave vertebral bodies

