comment: Arabic Definition: نظام وريدي غير طبيعي يجمع بين الطحال والوريد البوابي.
xref: UMLS:C4025236
is_a: HP:0031941 ! Abnormal portal venous system morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0005202
name: Helicobacter pylori infection
synonym: "عدوى هيليكوباكتر بيلوري" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "التهاب المعدة بالبكتيريا الحلزونية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى متكررة للجهاز الهضمي ببكتيريا هيليكوباكتر بيلوري، وهي بكتيريا سالبة الجرام وميكروائية يتواجد عادة في المعدة.
def: "A recurrent infection of the GI tract with helicobacter pylori, a gram-negative, microaerophilic bacterium usually found in the stomach." [PMID:23652324]
comment: The bacterial pathogen Helicobacter pylori has co-evolved with humans and colonizes approximately half of the human population, but only causes overt gastric disease in a subset of infected hosts.
xref: UMLS:C0850666
is_a: HP:0004798 ! Recurrent infection of the gastrointestinal tract

[Term]
id: HP:0005203
name: Spontaneous esophageal perforation
synonym: "انثقاب تلقائي للمريء" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تمزق فجائي في جدار المريء" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: حدوث تمزق كامل السماكة (انثقاب) لجدار المريء.
alt_id: HP:0005251
def: "The occurrence of the full-thickness tear (perforation) of the wall of the esophagus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Esophageal perforation can lead to retained gastric contents, saliva, bile, and other substances entering the mediastinum, resulting in mediastinitis, which in turn may lead to sepsis.
synonym: "Boerhaave syndrome" RELATED []
synonym: "Spontaneous esophageal rupture" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:19995004
xref: UMLS:C0238115
is_a: HP:0002031 ! Abnormal esophagus morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0005206
name: Pancreatic pseudocyst
synonym: "الكيس الكاذب للبنكرياس" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تجمع سوائل في البنكرياس" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مساحة شبيهة بالكيس غير مبطنة بالنسيج الظهاري محتواة داخل البنكرياس. غالباً ما ترتبط الأكياس الكاذبة للبنكرياس بالتهاب البنكرياس.
def: "Cyst-like space not lined by epithelium and contained within the pancreas. Pancreatic pseudocysts are often associated with pancreatitis." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:111374002
xref: UMLS:C0030299
is_a: HP:0012090 ! Abnormal pancreas morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0005207
name: Gastric hypertrophy
synonym: "تضخم في المعدة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
