[Term]
id: HP:0005295
name: Pseudocoarctation of the aorta
synonym: "التضيق الكاذب للشريان الأبهر" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انثناء غير كامل للشريان الأبهر" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: التضيق الكاذب هو شذوذ خلقي يتضمن التواء الشريان الأبهر دون تشكل فجوة ضغط عبر المنطقة المتأثرة. يتميز بتمدد والتواء الشريان الأبهر عند مستوى الرباط الشرياني.
def: "Pseudocoarctation is a congenital anomaly of kinking, or buckling, of the aorta without a pressure gradient across the lesion. It is characterized by elongation and kinking of the aorta at the level of the ligamentum arteriosum." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:17593995, PMID:18651460]
comment: Note that the ligamentum arteriosum, which develops from the ductus arteriosus, is attached to the superior surface of the pulmonary artery and the inferior surface of the aortic arch.
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:70602002
xref: UMLS:C0345088
is_a: HP:0012303 ! Abnormal aortic arch morphology

