[Term]
id: HP:0005930
name: Abnormal epiphysis morphology
synonym: "شذوذ في شكل المشاشة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شذوذ في شكل الطرف العظمي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ في شكل المشاشة، وهو الطرف المفصلي المتوسع للعظم الطويل الذي يتطور من مركز تعظم ثانوي، والذي خلال فترة النمو يكون إما غضروفياً بالكامل أو مفصولاً عن الجذع بواسطة قرص الغضاريف.
alt_id: HP:0000936
def: "An anomaly of epiphysis, which is the expanded articular end of a long bone that developes from a secondary ossification center, and which during the period of growth is either entirely cartilaginous or is separated from the shaft by a cartilaginous disk." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Abnormal shape of end part of bone" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Abnormality of epiphysis morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormality of the epiphyses" EXACT []
synonym: "Anomaly of the epiphyses" EXACT []
synonym: "Epiphyseal abnormality" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4021611
is_a: HP:0011314 ! Abnormal long bone morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2008-03-27T03:00:00Z

[Term]
id: HP:0005932
name: Abnormal renal corticomedullary differentiation
synonym: "شذوذ التمايز القشري النخاعي الكلوي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شذوذ التمايز الكلوي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ في تمايز القشرة والنخاع في الكلية كما يلاحظ في التصوير التشخيصي كالرنين المغناطيسي، التصوير المقطعي، أو التصوير بالموجات فوق الصوتية.
def: "An abnormality of corticomedullary differentiation (CMD) on diagnostic imaging such as magnetic resonance imaging, computer tomography, or sonography. CMD is a difference in the visualization of cortex and medulla." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22528889]
comment: On T1-weighted magnetic resonance imaging, the signal intensity of the normal renal cortex is typically higher than medulla, resulting in easily visualized corticomedullary differentiation (CMD). Loss of CMD can be seen in disorders such as glomerulonephritis, acute tubular necrosis, end-stage chronic renal failure, obstructive hydronephrosis, and acute allograft rejection. Progressive corticomedullary differentiation (CMD) can be visualized as an echogenic cortex and a hypoechoic medulla. This CMD should be visible during the midtrimester sonographic evaluation.
xref: UMLS:C4025102
is_a: HP:0011035 ! Abnormal renal cortex morphology
is_a: HP:0100957 ! Abnormal renal medulla morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2008-03-27T03:21:00Z

