[Term]
id: HP:0006297
name: Enamel hypoplasia
synonym: "نقص تنسج في مينا الأسنان" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ضعف في مينا الأسنان" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: النقص في تنسج مينا الأسنان يتضمن انخفاض تطور أو تصنيع مينا الأسنان، مما يؤدي إلى طبقة خارجية أرق للأسنان.
alt_id: HP:0000671
alt_id: HP:0001565
alt_id: HP:0003770
def: "Developmental hypoplasia of the dental enamel." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9338-3017, PMID:18499550, PMID:31468724]
comment: Enamel hypoplasia can be caused by genetic or environmental factors. It may occur in both deciduous and permanent dentitions, although more often in the permanent dentition. Enamel hypoplasia may concern a single tooth, several teeth, or the complete dentition and may affect part or the complete surface of the tooth. Enamel hypoplasia regroups different clinical aspects: localized hypoplasia, generalized hypoplasia, enamel pits, enamel striae, and grooves defects. The term should be used to describe a quantitative defect of enamel. Enamel hypotrophy cannot be used as hypotrophy indicates loss of cells, whereas enamel is an acellular structure and thus not a tissue.
synonym: "Defective enamel matrix" BROAD [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Dental enamel hypoplasia" EXACT []
synonym: "Dysplasia of tooth enamel" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Enamel dysplasia" RELATED []
synonym: "Enamel hypotrophy" EXACT []
synonym: "Enamel, underdeveloped" EXACT []
synonym: "Hypoplasia of dental enamel" EXACT []
synonym: "Hypoplasia of tooth enamel" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Thin dental enamel" BROAD layperson []
synonym: "Thin tooth enamel" BROAD layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Underdeveloped teeth enamel" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6548-5200]
