[Term]
id: HP:0006342
name: Peg-shaped maxillary lateral incisors
synonym: "القواطع الجانبية الفكية الحدبية الشكل" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "القواطع الجانبية العلوية المخروطية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تاج السن الذي يلتقي جانبيه الأنسي والبعيد ويتقاربان نحو الحافة القاطعة مما يؤدي إلى تقليل قطر الميسودستال.
def: "A tooth crown with its mesial and distal sides converging or tapering toward the incisal edge causing severe reduction of mesiodistal diameter" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9338-3017, PMID:31468724]
comment: A peg shape appearance of a tooth occurs in lateral incisors only. A peg-shaped tooth is a microdont tooth and may occur isolated or associated with other dental anomalies, such as hypodontia and oligodontia; this should be assessed and coded separately.
synonym: "Cone shaped upper lateral incisors" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Conical maxillary lateral incisors" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Conoid upper lateral incisors" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Peg laterals" BROAD [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Peg shaped upper lateral incisors" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Pointed upper lateral incisors" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
xref: UMLS:C4025060
is_a: HP:0011065 ! Conical incisor

