[Term]
id: HP:0006350
name: Pulp obliteration
synonym: "انطمار اللب السني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انطمار حجرة اللب السني" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مادة معدنية تملأ كامل مساحة لب السن.
def: "Mineralized substance filling the entire dental pulp space." [PMID:162890, PMID:31468724]
comment: The diagnosis pulp obliteration can be established using radiological studies. Gradual obliteration of the pulp is a physiologic process that occurs with aging. On radiographs the contours of the pulp disappear in part or totally, but histologically pulpal tissue remains present.
synonym: "Crescent/chevron-shaped pulp chambers" RELATED []
synonym: "Narrowing of pulp chamber of tooth" NARROW [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Obliteration of the pulp chamber" EXACT []
synonym: "Pulp canal obliteration" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Reduced size of pulp chamber of tooth" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Small pulp chamber of tooth" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
xref: UMLS:C4020817
xref: UMLS:C4025057
xref: UMLS:C4280448
is_a: HP:0006479 ! Abnormal dental pulp morphology

