[Term]
id: HP:0006897
name: Abducens palsy
synonym: "شلل العصب المبعد" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شلل العين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل في وظيفة العصب المبعد كما يتجلى من ضعف القدرة على تحريك العين المصابة للخارج. المرضى الذين يعانون من شلل العصب المبعد يظهر لديهم ازدواج أفقي في الرؤية عند النظر إلى الأشياء جنبًا إلى جنب. سيكون هناك ضعف ملحوظ في عضلة المستقيم الجانبي ipsilateral مما يؤدي إلى عجز في إخراج العين في الجانب المصاب. بعض المرضى قد يظهر لديهم حركة مستمرة لرأسهم للحفاظ على التحام ثنائي العين والتقليل من درجة ازدواج الرؤية.
alt_id: HP:0011349
def: "Malfunction of the abducens nerve as manifested by impairment of the ability of the affected eye to be moved outward. Patients who develop abducens nerve palsy often present with binocular horizontal diplopia, which is a double vision when looking at objects side by side. There will be a notable weakness of the ipsilateral lateral rectus muscle leading to a deficit in of eye abduction on the affected side. Some patients may present with a constant head turning movement to maintain binocular fusion and to lessen the degree of diplopia." [PMID:29489275]
comment: Affected individuals may experience diplopia as well as esotropia or convergent strabismus.
synonym: "Abducens nerve palsy" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Abducens nerve paralysis" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Abducens nerve paresis" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Cranial nerve VI palsy" EXACT []
synonym: "Lateral rectus muscle denervation paresis" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Sixth nerve palsy" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:398760006
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:398925009
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:398963001
xref: UMLS:C0271355
is_a: HP:0006824 ! Cranial nerve paralysis

