xref: UMLS:C1859863
is_a: HP:0007369 ! Atrophy/Degeneration affecting the cerebrum

[Term]
id: HP:0006965
name: Acute necrotizing encephalopathy
synonym: "اعتلال دماغي نخري حاد" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تلف دماغي حاد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: حالة من التلف الحاد في الدماغ يترافق مع نخر في أنسجة الدماغ.
xref: UMLS:C1855020
is_a: HP:0006846 ! Acute encephalopathy

[Term]
id: HP:0006970
name: Periventricular leukomalacia
synonym: "تليّن المادة البيضاء حول البطينات" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تلف في المادة البيضاء حول تجاويف الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يتميز تليّن المادة البيضاء حول البطينات بإصابة منتشرة للمادة البيضاء العميقة في الدماغ، مصحوبة في أشد أشكالها بالنخر البؤري. العلامات المرضية النسيجية المميزة تشمل تنشيط الخلايا الدبقية الصغيرة والنقص البؤري والمنتشر للخلايا الدبقية قليلة التغصن قبل تكوّن النخاعين في منطقة حول البطينات.
def: "Periventricular leukomalacia is characterized by diffuse injury of deep cerebral white matter, accompanied in its most severe form by focal necrosis. The neuropathologic hallmarks of PVL are microglial activation and focal and diffuse periventricular depletion of premyelinating oligodendroglia." [PMID:16808630, PMID:18852342, PMID:28406931]
comment: Periventricular leukomalacia is the leading known cause of cerebral palsy. Magnetic resonance imaging-based neuroimaging techniques provide greater diagnostic sensitivity for PVL than does head ultrasonography and often document the involvement of telencephalic gray matter and long tracts in addition to periventricular white matter.
synonym: "PVL" EXACT abbreviation []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:230769007
xref: UMLS:C0023529
is_a: HP:0002518 ! Abnormal periventricular white matter morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0006976
name: Necrotizing encephalopathy
synonym: "اعتلال دماغي نخري" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تلف دماغي بسبب موت الأنسجة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من الاعتلالات الدماغية يتميز بوجود نخر في أنسجة الدماغ.
def: "A type of encephalopathy (brain disease, damage, or malfunction accompanied by an altered mental state) that is characterized by evidence of necrosis of brain tissue." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:KI_phemming, PMID:23705127]
comment: The disease acute necrotizing encephalopathy is characterized by acute onset encephalopathy with rapid, progressive neurologic deterioration, seizures and symmetric multifocal brain lesions. This term is kept for convenience. For new annotations, it is recommended that the specific phenotypic abnormalities be noted.
xref: UMLS:C1396481
is_a: HP:0001298 ! Encephalopathy

