[Term]
id: HP:0007872
name: Choroidal hemangioma
synonym: "ورم وعائي مشيمي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ورم حميد في المشيمية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ورم حميد يظهر في قاع العين كمكان مشيمي ذو لون محمر أو برتقالي وغالبًا ما يرتبط بالأوديما الكيسية وأحيانًا أقل بسائل شبكي تحت الشبكية.
def: "Benign choroidal tumour, seen in the fundus as a reddish or orange choroidal lesion and usually associated with cystoid edema, and less commonly with Subretinal fluid." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:15763200]
comment: Choroidal hemangiomas can cause hyperopia or other visual symptoms such as blurred or distorted vision. Some choroidal hemangiomas are asymptomatic, and only diagnosed after angiography. Diffuse choroidal hemangioma is seen associated with Sturge-Weber syndrome.
xref: NCIT:C3086
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:255022003
xref: UMLS:C0346390
is_a: HP:0001028 ! Hemangioma
is_a: HP:0025568 ! Abnormal morphology of the choroidal vasculature

