[Term]
id: HP:0007894
name: Fundus hypopigmentation
synonym: "نقص تصبغ قاع العين" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "قلة التصبغ في قاع العين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انخفاض في التصبغ العام أو البؤري لقاع العين، والذي يتم تقييمه في سياق لون الجلد والشعر. قد يكشف تنظير القاع عن مستويات منخفضة من التصبغ.
alt_id: HP:0001111
alt_id: HP:0001487
alt_id: HP:0007680
alt_id: HP:0007746
alt_id: HP:0007752
def: "Generalized or focal reduced pigmentation of the fundus, evaluated in the context of skin and hair color. Fundoscopy may reveal a low level pigment." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
comment: Fundus hypopigmentation is consistently observed in albinism. Pigmentation is also reduced with age in some individuals, high myopia, and in chronic inflammation, such as Harada disease. Ocular pigmentation is essential for normal vision, and persons with ocular albinism tend to have severely reduced visual acuity often associated with nystagmus, strabismus, and photophobia.
synonym: "Decreased fundus pigmentation" EXACT []
synonym: "Depigmented fundus" EXACT []
synonym: "Hypopigmentation of the fundus" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031605 ! Abnormal fundus pigmentation

