[Term]
id: HP:0008150
name: Elevated serum transaminases during infections
synonym: "ارتفاع الإنزيمات الناقلة أثناء العدوى" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة إنزيمات الكبد في العدوى" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ارتفاع مستويات SGOT (الإنزيم الناقل للغلوتميك والأكسالوأسيتك) وSGPT (الإنزيم الناقل للغلوتميك والبيروفيك) التي تحدث أثناء العدوى.
def: "Elevations of the levels of SGOT (serum glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase) and SGPT (serum glutamic pyruvic transaminase) that occur during infections." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: UMLS:C1864179
is_a: HP:0002910 ! Elevated circulating hepatic transaminase concentration

[Term]
id: HP:0008151
name: Prolonged prothrombin time
synonym: "زمن البروثرومبين المطول" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تطويل زمن تخثر الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة الوقت اللازم لتجلط الدم في اختبار زمن البروثرومبين، وهو مقياس للمسار الخارجي للتجلط. غالبًا ما يتم التعبير عن نتائج اختبار زمن البروثرومبين من حيث النسبة الدولية الموحدة (INR)، والتي تُحسب كنسبة زمن البروثرومبين للمريض إلى زمن الضبط القياسي باستخدام كواشف محددة طورتها منظمة الصحة العالمية.
alt_id: HP:0012201
def: "Increased time to coagulation in the prothrombin time test, which is a measure of the extrinsic pathway of coagulation. The results of the prothrombin time test are often expressed in terms of the International normalized ratio (INR), which is calculated as a ratio of the patient's prothrombin time (PT) to a control PT standardized for the potency of the thromboplastin reagent developed by the World Health Organization (WHO) using the formula: INR is equal to Patient PT divided by Control PT." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:26351955, PMID:29939529]
comment: The prothrombin time (PT) and the activated partial thromboplastin time (APTT) are the most requested tests to investigate patients with congenital or acquired coagulopathies and drug monitoring. They are defined as the time (seconds) needed to clot platelet-poor plasma upon addition of coagulation triggers, such as tissue factor in complex with phospholipids and calcium chloride (in the PT), or negatively charged phospholipids-activators and calcium chloride (in the APTT). They can hence be considered as global coagulation tests sensitive to deficiencies of many coagulation factors. In brief, they are both sensitive to factor X, V, II and fibrinogen, whereas the PT is only sensitive to factor VII deficiency and the APTT is sensitive to pre-kallikrein, high molecular weight kininogen (HMWK), factor XII, XI, IX and VIII deficiencies. Normal plasma in the PT clots approximately within 10-12 s upon triggering coagulation, and the normal reference range is (usually) narrow. PT results have been reported as clotting time, percentage activity, PT-ratio (patient-to-normal clotting time) and as international normalized ratio (INR). The INR scale has been devised to harmonize results stemming from different thromboplastins from patients on treatment with vitamin K antagonists. Some recommend abandoning the approach of using percentage activity to assess PR.
synonym: "Increased INR" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Increased international normalised ratio" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Increased international normalized ratio" EXACT []
synonym: "Low factor II activity" EXACT []
synonym: "Prolonged PT" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Reduced factor II activity" EXACT []
synonym: "Reduced prothrombin activity" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:409674002
xref: UMLS:C0151872
is_a: HP:0032199 ! Abnormal prothrombin time

