comment: Arabic Definition: انشقاق (شق أو تفتت) يصيب الأجسام الفقرية.
alt_id: HP:0000942
def: "Schisis (cleft or cleavage) of vertebral bodies." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Cleft vertebrae result when there are two, instead of one, primary ossification centers in a vertebral body. An unossified cartilaginous brdige may be observed radiographically with the shape of a cleft. If the two ossification centers are ventral/dorsal, a coronal cleft is observed, and if the two ossification centers are left/right, than a sagittal cleft is observed.
synonym: "Vertebral clefts" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C1855828
