[Term]
id: HP:0009792
name: Teratoma
synonym: "مسخي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ورم مسخي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود ورم مسخي.
def: "The presence of a teratoma." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Teratomas are germ-cell tumors commonly composed of multiple cell types derived from one or more of the three germ layers. They derive from embryonic pluripotent cells and may have various degrees of maturation, according to which they are classified as mature, immature, and malignant. Teratomas are found with decreasing frequency in the ovaries and testis, mediastinum, retroperitoneal space, sacrococcygeal zone, pineal and other intracranial locations.
xref: NCIT:C3403
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:55818009
xref: UMLS:C0039538
is_a: HP:0002898 ! Embryonal neoplasm
is_a: HP:0100728 ! Germ cell neoplasia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-02-03T05:23:03Z

[Term]
id: HP:0009793
name: Presacral teratoma
synonym: "مسخي قبل عجزي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ورم مسخي في منطقة العصعص" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من الورم المسخي العجزي يقع أمام العجز ويكون بالكامل داخل الجسم (النوع الرابع حسب تصنيف ألتمان).
def: "A type of sacrococcygeal teratoma located anterior to the sacrum and entirely inside the body (Altman type IV)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Sacrococcygeal teratomas are thought to originate from multipotential cells in Henson's node, which migrates caudally to rest in the coccyx.
synonym: "Altman type IV sacrococcygeal teratoma" EXACT []
synonym: "Retrorectal teratoma" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C1867782
is_a: HP:0030736 ! Sacrococcygeal teratoma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-02-03T05:23:57Z

[Term]
id: HP:0009794
name: Branchial anomaly
synonym: "شذوذ في الثنيات الغلصمية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في الثنيات الغلصمية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عيب تطوري خلقي ناتج عن الجهاز الغلصمي البدائي.
def: "Congenital developmental defect arising from the primitive branchial apparatus." [https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154]
comment: During embryonic development the major head and neck structures are formed from the five pharyngeal arches (bands of tissue). Incomplete, failed or persistent embryonic development of these arches results in several anomalies or defects in the neck.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Abnormality of branchial apparatus" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Abnormality of branchial arch" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Branchial abnormality" EXACT []
synonym: "Branchial anomalies" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C1862066
is_a: HP:0025668 ! Abnormal neck morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-02-11T05:16:20Z

[Term]
id: HP:0009795
name: Branchial fistula
synonym: "ناسور خيشومي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ناسور في الرقبة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ناسور خلقي في العنق ناتج عن عدم الانغلاق الكامل للشق الخيشومي.
def: "A congenital fistula in the neck resulting from incomplete closure of a branchial cleft." [https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154]
