[Term]
id: HP:0009896
name: Abnormal antitragus morphology
synonym: "شذوذ في شكل مضادة الوتدة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شكل غير طبيعي لمضادة الوتدة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ في المضادة الوتدة، وهي نتوء صغير مقابل للوتدة في الأذن. يتم فصل المضادة الوتدة والوتدة بواسطة فجوة بين الوتد.
def: "An abnormality of the antitragus, which is a small tubercle opposite to the tragus of the ear. The antitragus and the tragus are separated by the intertragic notch." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
subset: hposlim_core
xref: UMLS:C4024167
is_a: HP:0000377 ! Abnormal pinna morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-04-30T10:13:21Z

[Term]
id: HP:0009897
name: Horizontal crus of helix
synonym: "الساق الأفقية للولب" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شكل أفقى للساق في الأذن" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: اتجاه محور أفقي غير طبيعي للساق للولب. أي أن المحور الرئيسي للساق من الولب يكون عموديًا على المحور الطولي الإنسي للأذن، بدلاً من الميل إلى الأسفل والخلف.
def: "An abnormal horizontal axis orientation of the crus of the helix. That is, the main axis of the crus of the helix is perpendicular to the medial longitudinal axis of the ear, instead of sloping inferoposteriorly." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19152421]
comment: The term 'railroad track sign' has been used to describe prominent horizontal crus of the helix in combination with prominent and parallel inferior crus of the antihelix. It is preferable to simply describe each component separately.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Helix, crus, horizontal" EXACT []
synonym: "Horizontal orientation of the crus of helix" EXACT []
synonym: "Horizontal orientation of the ear crus" EXACT []
synonym: "Railroad track ears" RELATED obsolete_synonym []
synonym: "Railroad track sign" RELATED obsolete_synonym []
xref: UMLS:C4021379
is_a: HP:0009895 ! Abnormality of the crus of the helix
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-04-30T10:34:52Z

