[Term]
id: HP:0009902
name: Cleft helix
synonym: "شق في لولب الأذن" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شكل مشقوق للولب الأذني، أي عيب في استمرارية اللولب يمكن أن يظهر في أي نقطة على طوله.
def: "A notched form of the helix of the ear. That is, a defect in the continuity of the helix, which may occur at any point along its length." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19152421]
comment: This may take the form of a sharp cleft or a less well-demarcated area. This should be distinguished from a Question-mark ear. If the defect or notch occurs at the junction of the superior and descending portions of the helix, it should be coded as Darwin notch of the helix.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Notched helix" EXACT []
synonym: "Notching of the ear helix" EXACT []
