[Term]
id: HP:0009908
name: Anterior creases of earlobe
synonym: "طيات أمامية لشحمة الأذن" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "طيات شحمة الأذن" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: حفر واضحة تحدد غالباً بشكل خطي وأفقي تقريباً في السطح الخارجي لشحمة الأذن.
alt_id: HP:0008604
def: "Sharply demarcated, typically linear and approximately horizontal, indentations in the outer surface of the ear lobe." [PMID:19152421]
comment: Shallow grooves or indentations are quite common, especially in large lobes. Ear lobe creases may arise postnatally. Posterior helical pits can be a related finding but should be assessed and coded separately.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Earlobe crease" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Transverse earlobe creases" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C1851897
is_a: HP:0000363 ! Abnormal earlobe morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-05-01T03:00:22Z

[Term]
id: HP:0009909
name: Uplifted earlobe
synonym: "شحمة الأذن المرفوعة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وضعية غير طبيعية لشحمة الأذن بحيث تشير إلى الخارج والأعلى، بحيث يواجه السطح الجانبي لشحمة الأذن إلى الأعلى.
alt_id: HP:0009764
def: "An abnormal orientation of the earlobes such that they point out- and upward. That is, the lateral surface of ear lobe faces superiorly." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19152421]
comment: This finding is characteristic of Mowat-Wilson syndrome.
subset: hposlim_core
