[Term]
id: HP:0010033
name: Triangular shaped 1st metacarpal
synonym: "المشط الأول على شكل مثلث" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "العظمة الأولى لليد على شكل مثلث" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يشير هذا المصطلح إلى المشط الأول الذي يكون على شكل مثلث.
def: "This term applies to a triangular shaped 1st metacarpal." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: In contrast to the metacarpals 2-5, the first metacarpal is embryologically of phalangeal origin and as such equivalent to the proximal phalanges of the digits 2-5, whereas the proximal phalanx of the thumb is equivalent to the middle phalanges of the other digits. A triangular or so called delta shaped phalanx is a typical result after a bracket epiphysis of the affected phalanx (in this case metacarpal, see explanation above).
synonym: "Triangular shaped 1st long bone of hand" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
xref: UMLS:C4024092
is_a: HP:0010009 ! Abnormal 1st metacarpal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154
creation_date: 2009-05-27T04:24:30Z

