[Term]
id: HP:0010296
name: Ankyloglossia
synonym: "اللسان المربوط" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ربط اللسان" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود لحمة لسانية قصيرة أو متصلة بالأمام، ترتبط بقلة حركة اللسان.
def: "Short or anteriorly attached lingual frenulum, associated with limited mobility of the tongue." [PMID:19125428]
comment: The anterior third of the tongue is usually free or is partially attached to the floor of the mouth by the lingual frenulum. There is a spectrum ranging from fusion of the tongue to the floor of the mouth (ankyloglossia inferiorum) to a lingual frenulum that is short or anchored toward the tip of the tongue (sometimes called tongue tie). Ankyloglossia may be associated with a mild indentation of the tip of the tongue, which should not be coded as a Bifid tongue.
synonym: "Tongue tie" RELATED []
synonym: "Tongue tied" EXACT layperson []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:67787004
xref: UMLS:C0152415
is_a: HP:0000190 ! Abnormal oral frenulum morphology
is_a: HP:0030809 ! Abnormal tongue morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-07-12T11:44:22Z

