[Term]
id: HP:0010316
name: Ebstein anomaly of the tricuspid valve
synonym: "تَشَوُّه إبشتاين في الصمام ثلاثي الشرفات" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تشوه إبشتاين في الصمام ثلاثي الشرفات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تشير تشوه إبشتاين إلى تموضع وتشوه غير طبيعي في الصمام الثلاثي الشُرَف مُتميّز بإزاحة قمية للنشرات الصمام الثلاثي الشُرَف الحاجزي والخلفي، مما يؤدي إلى أُذَينَة البطين الأيمن بدرجات متفاوتة من التشوه والإزاحة في النشرة الأمامية.
alt_id: HP:0006674
def: "Ebstein's anomaly refers to an abnormally placed and deformed tricuspid valve characterized by apical displacement of the septal and posterior tricuspid valve leaflets, leading to atrialization of the right ventricle with a variable degree of malformation and displacement of the anterior leaflet." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:DDD_dbrown, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Ebstein's anomaly is often associated with a hypoplastic right ventricle, patent foramen ovale, and a degree of cyanosis dependent on the amount if inadequacy of the tricuspid valve. Ebstein's anomaly may be associated with Wolf-Parkinson-White syndrome or other arrythmias.
synonym: "Ebstein's anomaly" EXACT []
synonym: "Ebstein's anomaly of the tricuspid valve" EXACT []
synonym: "Ebstein's malformation" EXACT []
xref: EPCC:06.01.34
xref: ICD-10:Q22.5
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:204357006
xref: UMLS:C0013481
is_a: HP:0001702 ! Abnormal tricuspid valve morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-07-14T11:12:07Z

