[Term]
id: HP:0010499
name: Patellar subluxation
synonym: "خلع رضفة جزئي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلع جزئي في الرضفة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تكون الرضفة عادةً في وضعية مركزية داخل القناة على نهاية عظم الفخذ ويمكن أن تنزلق لأعلى ولأسفل فيها. يشير خلع الرضفة الجزئي إلى وضع غير مستقر للرضفة حيث لا تنزلق مركزياً داخل القناة، أي خلع جزئي للرضفة.
def: "The kneecap normally is located within the groove termed trochlea on the distal femur and can slide up and down in it. Patellar subluxation refers to an unstable kneecap that does not slide centrally within its groove, i.e., a partial dislocation of the patella." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Partial knee cap dislocation" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Subluxation of patella" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C0857276
is_a: HP:0003045 ! Abnormal patella morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-09-17T11:46:41Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010500
name: Hyperextensibility of the knee
synonym: "فرط قابلية التمدد للركبة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تمدد الركبة بشكل مفرط" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: قدرة مفصل الركبة على التمدد لتتجاوز المدى الطبيعي للحركة (تحرك الساق بأسفل وضعية أكثر من المستقيم بالمقارنة مع الفخذ).
def: "The ability of the knee joint to extend beyond its normal range of motion (the lower leg is moved beyond a straight position with respect to the thigh)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: UMLS:C4023802
is_a: HP:0034670 ! Abnormal knee physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-09-19T09:44:04Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010501
name: Limitation of knee mobility
synonym: "تقييد حركة الركبة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "حركة محدودة في الركبة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تحديد غير طبيعي لحركة مفصل الركبة.
alt_id: HP:0005030
alt_id: HP:0005192
def: "An abnormal limitation of knee joint mobility." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The knee permits four types of movement: (i) Extension (straightening the lower leg); (ii) Flexion (bending the knee); (iii) Lateral rotation (turning outwards); and (iv) Medial rotation (turning inward)
synonym: "Limitation of knee mobility" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Limited knee movement" EXACT layperson []
