[Term]
id: HP:0010551
name: Paraplegia/paraparesis
synonym: "الشلل النصفي السفلي/الشلل الجزئي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ضعف الساقين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ضعف في كلا الطرفين السفليين مع تجنيب الطرفين العلويين. يشير الشلل النصفي إلى فقدان شديد أو كامل للقوة، بينما يشير الشلل الجزئي إلى فقدان نسبي أو طفيف للقوة.
def: "Weakness of both lower extremities with sparing of the upper extremities. Paraplegia refers to a severe or complete loss of strength, whereas paraparesis refers to a relatively mild loss of strength." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: UMLS:C4023792
is_a: HP:0010549 ! Weakness due to upper motor neuron dysfunction
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-10-01T08:36:05Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010553
name: Oculogyric crisis
synonym: "أزمة عينية دوارة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تشنجات العين الحادة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: رد فعل حاد ديستوني يتضمن تشنج في عضلات الجفن وتشنجات حول العين وحلقات ثابتة من التحديق. قد يكون هناك انحراف صاعد شديد في العينين بشكل مستدام. يمكن أن تثير أزمة عينية دوارة بسبب عدد من العوامل بما في ذلك الأدوية المضادة للذهان.
def: "An acute dystonic reaction with blepharospasm, periorbital twitches, and protracted fixed staring episodes. There may be a maximal upward deviation of the eyes in the sustained fashion. Oculogyric crisis can be triggered by a number of factors including neuroleptic medications." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:5332004
xref: UMLS:C0085637
is_a: HP:0001332 ! Dystonia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-10-01T08:56:39Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010554
name: Cutaneous finger syndactyly
synonym: "التصاق جلدي للأصابع" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "التصاق الأصابع" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: استمرار في النسيج الطري في المحور الطولي بين إصبعين يمتد بعيدًا على الأقل إلى مستوى المفاصل بين السلاميات القريبة، أو استمرار في النسيج الطري في المحور الطولي بين إصبعين يقع بشكل كبير بعيدًا عن الثنية فوق المفصل السلامي للسلاميات المجاورة.
alt_id: HP:0001214
alt_id: HP:0005637
alt_id: HP:0006054
alt_id: HP:0006220
def: "A soft tissue continuity in the A/P axis between two fingers that extends distally to at least the level of the proximal interphalangeal joints, or a soft tissue continuity in the A/P axis between two fingers that lies significantly distal to the flexion crease that overlies the metacarpophalangeal joint of the adjacent fingers." [PMID:19125433]
comment: We have set an arguably arbitrary threshold to distinguish the object form the subjective finding. While severe degrees of cutaneous syndactyly are clearly objective, more subtle degrees are subjective. We set this threshold to distinguish these two situations. The digits (or parts of) are joined together by tissue that is not normally present between the digits at that point in the P/D axis. A modifier of "complete" may be used if the cutaneous syndactyly extends to the distal end of the nail bed of the digits. The affected digits should be specified. Note that the unqualified term "syndactyly" is no longer allowed as it is unclear whether this refers to bony or cutaneous syndactyly.
subset: hposlim_core
synonym: "Cutaneous syndactyly of fingers" EXACT []
synonym: "Cutaneous syndactyly of hands" EXACT []
synonym: "Webbed fingers" EXACT layperson [PMID:16200145]
synonym: "Webbed skin of fingers" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
xref: UMLS:C4021254
is_a: HP:0006101 ! Finger syndactyly
is_a: HP:0012725 ! Cutaneous syndactyly
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154
creation_date: 2009-10-07T10:59:57Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010557
name: Overlapping fingers
synonym: "تداخل الأصابع" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "أصابع متداخلة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود إصبع يستريح على السطح الظهري لإصبع مجاور عندما تكون اليد في حالة راحة.
def: "A finger resting on the dorsal surface of an adjacent digit when the hand is at rest." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19125433]
comment: Overlapping of the fingers occurring as the result of a deviation of the fingers from their normal position. Fingers that are laterally deviated, but do not rest on top of adjacent fingers should be coded as Clinodactyly.
subset: hposlim_core
xref: UMLS:C1446712
is_a: HP:0004097 ! Deviation of finger
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154
creation_date: 2009-10-13T09:21:52Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010558
name: Abnormality of the clivus
synonym: "شذوذ الجيباني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في العظم بين الرأس والرقبة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ في الجيباني، الذي هو المنطقة العظمية المائلة في الحفرة الخلفية القحفية بين السرج التركي والثقبة الكبرى.
def: "An abnormality of the clivus, which is the inclined bony region of the posterior cranial fossa located between the sella turcica and the foramen magnum." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: UMLS:C4023791
is_a: HP:0000932 ! Abnormal posterior cranial fossa morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-10-14T09:37:19Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010559
name: Vertical clivus
synonym: "قاعدة رأسية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "قاعدة رأسية غير طبيعية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود وضع عمودي غير طبيعي للقاعدة الجمجمية (والتي تشكل عادةً نوعًا من المنحدر من السرج التركي إلى منطقة الفورامين ماغنوم).
def: "An abnormal vertical orientation of the clivus (which normally forms a kind of slope from the sella turcica down to the region of the foramen magnum)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: UMLS:C1844702
is_a: HP:0010558 ! Abnormality of the clivus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2009-10-14T09:39:04Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010560
name: Undulate clavicles
synonym: "عظام الترقوة المتموجة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عظمة الترقوة مموجة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: سطح أو حافة الترقوة تبدو غير طبيعية ومتموجة.
