[Term]
id: HP:0010847
name: EEG with spike-wave complexes (<2.5 Hz)
synonym: "مخطط كهربية الدماغ مع مجمعات موجة-شلل (<2.5 هرتز)" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نشاط كهربائي بطيء في الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود مجمعات من موجات بطيئة الشلل والموجات البطيئة (<2.5 هرتز) في مخطط كهربية الدماغ.
def: "The presence of complexes of slow spikes and slow waves (<2.5 Hz) in electroencephalography (EEG)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Spikes (<70 ms) and sharp waves (70-200 ms) are sharp transient waves that have a strong association with epilepsy. No difference is noted in terms of clinical significance of spikes and sharp waves. Significant spikes usually are followed by a slow wave.
synonym: "Electroencephalogram demonstrated spike-slow wave discharges" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4023686
is_a: HP:0010850 ! EEG with spike-wave complexes
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2010-07-10T08:18:25Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010848
name: EEG with spike-wave complexes (2.5-3.5 Hz)
synonym: "EEG مع مركبات موجة سبايك (2.5-3.5 هرتز)" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "موجات سبايك في تخطيط كهربية الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود مركبات من سبايك وموجات بتردد يتراوح بين 2.5 و3.5 هرتز في تخطيط كهربية الدماغ (EEG).
def: "The presence of complexes of spikes and waves (2.5-3.5 Hz) in electroencephalography (EEG)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: UMLS:C4023685
is_a: HP:0010850 ! EEG with spike-wave complexes
