creation_date: 2010-07-10T08:21:13Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010849
name: EEG with spike-wave complexes (>3.5 Hz)
synonym: "مخطط كهربية الدماغ مع مجمعات موجة-شلل (>3.5 هرتز)" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نشاط كهربائي سريع في الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود مجمعات من موجات الشلل والموجات (>3.5 هرتز) في مخطط كهربية الدماغ.
alt_id: HP:0007261
def: "The presence of complexes of spikes and waves (>3.5 Hz) in electroencephalography (EEG)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "EEG with 3-4-Hz spike waves" RELATED []
xref: UMLS:C4020765
xref: UMLS:C4023684
is_a: HP:0010850 ! EEG with spike-wave complexes
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2010-07-10T08:22:40Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010850
name: EEG with spike-wave complexes
synonym: "مخطط كهربية الدماغ مع مجمعات موجة-شلل" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نشاط كهربي غير طبيعي في الدماغ مرتبط بالصرع" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تواجد مجمعات من شلل (<70 مللي ثانية) وموجات حادة (70-200 مللي ثانية) والتي تعتبر موجات عابرة حادة ترتبط بشكل قوي مع الصرع، في النشاط الكهربائي الدماغي المسجل عبر فروة الرأس باستخدام مخطط كهربية الدماغ.
def: "Complexes of spikes (<70 ms) and sharp waves (70-200 ms), which are sharp transient waves that have a strong association with epilepsy, in cerebral electrical activity recorded along the scalp by electroencephalography (EEG)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: UMLS:C4023683
is_a: HP:0011198 ! EEG with generalized epileptiform discharges
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2010-07-10T08:23:28Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010851
name: EEG with burst suppression
synonym: "مخطط كهربية الدماغ مع نمط التثبيط الانفجاري" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نمط غير طبيعي في نشاط الدماغ الكهربائي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمط التثبيط الانفجاري في مخطط كهربية الدماغ يشير إلى نمط دوري مميز من خلفية ذات جهد منخفض (<10 ميكروفولت) وقمعية ونمط أقصر نسبياً من مجمعات بطيئة، حادة ومتقطعة ذات جهد مرتفع.
def: "The burst suppression pattern in electroencephalography refers to a characteristic periodic pattern of low voltage (<10 microvolts) suppressed background and a relatively shorter pattern of higher amplitude slow, sharp, and spiking complexes." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22323592]
comment: Burst suppression can occur in a generalized or lateralized distribution and is often a sign of severe encephalopathy. Generally, an interburst interval of 30 seconds or less is associated with a better prognosis than longer interburst intervals (>30 sec). Burst suppression is an electroencephalogram (EEG) pattern in which high voltage activity (burst) and flatline (suppression) periods alternate systematically but quasiperiodically (almost periodic but with variations in inter- and intra-burst duration) is a state of profound brain inactivation.
xref: UMLS:C1969156
is_a: HP:0011198 ! EEG with generalized epileptiform discharges
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2010-07-11T08:02:41Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010852
name: EEG with photoparoxysmal response
synonym: "EEG مع استجابة فوتوبروكسيسمالية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "استجابة للنوبات الضوئية في تخطيط كهربية الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذات في تخطيط كهربية الدماغ (تفريغات نوباتية) تستحثها الأضواء الوامضة أو الأنماط المخططة بالأبيض والأسود.
alt_id: HP:0001330
def: "EEG abnormalities (epileptiform discharges) evoked by flashing lights or black and white striped patterns." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: In some patients, seizures can be provoked by specific external factors (reflex epilepsy), including flickering lights and patterns. These patients commonly show epileptiform discharges in the EEG when stimulated with flashing lights, black and white striped patterns and television. These evoked EEG abnormalities are called photoparoxysmal responses.
synonym: "Photoparoxysmal response on EEG" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C3552821
is_a: HP:0002353 ! EEG abnormality
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2010-07-11T08:10:17Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010853
name: EEG with periodic lateralized epileptiform discharges
synonym: "EEG مع تفريغات نوباتية جانبية متموجة دورية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تفريغات نوباتية دورية في تخطيط كهربية الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: التفريغات النوباتية الجانبية المتموجة الدورية (PLEDs) هي تفريغات دورية، جانبية، ونوباتية، وتظهر فاصلًا زمنيًا ثابتًا نسبيًا بين التفريغات (0.5 إلى 3 ثواني).
def: "Periodic lateralized epileptiform discharges (PLEDs)are periodic, lateralized, and epileptiform. PLEDs show a relatively constant interval between discharges (0.5 to 3 seconds)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The epileptiform morphology of the discharges is not invariable, as PLEDS are often closer to slow waves than to sharp waves in morphology. PLEDs are often are caused by acute destructive focal lesions. PLEDs are often a transitory phenomenon, disappearing in a matter of weeks, even if the causal lesion persists, and often transforming into a less specific but more persistent focal slow appearance.
synonym: "EEG: periodic lateralized epileptiform discharges" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4021215
is_a: HP:0011186 ! Focal epileptiform discharges with limited propagation to contralateral hemisphere
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2010-07-11T08:25:02Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010854
name: EEG with generalized low amplitude activity
synonym: "EEG مع نشاط منخفض السعة بشكل عام" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نشاط دماغي منخفض السعة حسب EEG" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انخفاض غير طبيعي في سعة النشاط الكهربائي للدماغ المسجل على طول فروة الرأس بواسطة تخطيط كهربية الدماغ (EEG).
def: "An abnormal generalized reduction in amplitude of the cerebral electrical activity recorded along the scalp by electroencephalography (EEG)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "EEG with generalised low amplitude activity" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "EEG: generalised low amplitude activity" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "EEG: generalized low amplitude activity" EXACT []
