[Term]
id: HP:0010864
name: Severe intellectual disability
synonym: "إعاقة ذهنية شديدة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تأخر ذهني شديد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الإعاقة الذهنية الشديدة تُعرّف كنوع من الإعاقة الذهنية التي تتميز بأداء وظيفي وتفكير فكري دون المعدل بشكل كبير، مع معامل ذكاء (IQ) يتراوح بين 20-34.
alt_id: HP:0007196
def: "Severe intellectual disability (ID) is defined as a type of ID characterized by severely sub-average adaptive functioning and intellectual functioning, with an intelligence quotient (IQ) the range of 20-34." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Persons with severe mental retardation can be taught basic life skills and simple tasks with supervision.
synonym: "Early and severe mental retardation" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Intellectual disability, severe" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Mental retardation, severe" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Severe mental retardation" EXACT layperson []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:40700009
xref: UMLS:C0036857
is_a: HP:0001249 ! Intellectual disability
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2010-08-03T06:29:35Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010865
name: Oppositional defiant disorder
synonym: "اضطراب التحدي المعارضة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "اضطراب السلوك المعتارض" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمط مستمر من السلوك الذي يتسم بالعناد والتمرد والعدائية تجاه الشخصيات الاعتبارية دون ارتكاب مخالفات اجتماعية خطيرة، ولا يمكن تحديده بالمرحلة التطورية للطفل، مما يؤدي إلى ضعف وظيفي ملحوظ. يعتبر مستوى معين من السلوك المعاكس شائعاً في الأطفال والمراهقين.
def: "An enduring pattern of uncooperative, defiant, and hostile behavior towards authority figures that does not involve major antisocial violations, is not accounted for by the child's developmental stage, and results in significant functional impairment. A certain level of oppositional behavior is common in children and adolescents." []
comment: Oppositional defiant disorder is essentially a persistent pattern of tantrums, arguments, and angry or disruptive behavior that exceeds what can be considered normal.
synonym: "ODD" EXACT abbreviation []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:18941000
xref: UMLS:C0029121
is_a: HP:0000718 ! Aggressive behavior
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1111-7357
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7954-5235
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2897-0458
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4298-5074
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4618-6544
