[Term]
id: HP:0010942
name: Echogenic intracardiac focus
synonym: "بؤرة قلبية صدوية داخلية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "بؤرة مشعة في القلب" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود تركيز صدوي زائد عند فحص الموجات الصوتية للجنين في الفترة قبل الولادة. يمكن لهذه البؤر أن تكون موجودة في أحد البطينين القلبيين أو كليهما. تعرف البؤرة القلبية الصدوية بأنها بؤرة ذات صدوى يعادل العظمة، في منطقة العضلة الحليمية في أحد البطينين أو كليهما للجنين.
def: "A finding of a focus of increased echogenicity upon prenatal ultrasound examination of the fetus. The foci may be present in one or both ventricles. Echogenic intracardiac focus (EICF) is defined as a focus of echogenicity comparable to bone, in the region of the papillary muscle in either or both ventricles of the fetal heart." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:16100637, PMID:9527573]
comment: An echogenic intracardiac focus (EIF) is generally believed to be a normal variant, observed in 5% of all fetuses during second trimester sonography, but the risk of aneuploidies such as Down syndrome is increased in fetuses with EIF.
xref: UMLS:C4023634
is_a: HP:0010948 ! Abnormal fetal cardiovascular morphology
is_a: HP:0011425 ! Fetal ultrasound soft marker
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2011-01-16T02:52:26Z

[Term]
id: HP:0010943
name: Echogenic fetal bowel
synonym: "أمعاء جنينية صدوية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "أمعاء مشعة للجنين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تعتبر الأمعاء الصدوية الجنينية أمعاء للجنين تحتوي على مناطق متجانسة من الصدوي تعادل أو تزيد على الأنسجة العظمية المحيطة.
def: "Echogenic bowel is defined as fetal bowel with homogenous areas of echogenicity that are equal to or greater than that of surrounding bone." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:16100637, PMID:20175047]
comment: Echogenic fetal bowel may be observed in fetuses with normal outcomes, but may also be a marker for diseases such as cystic fibrosis, congenital infection, chromosomal anomalies, and intraamniotic bleeding. This finding can be observed on prenatal ultrasound. The echogenicity has been classified as either focal or multifocal. Grade 2 suggests that echogenicity is equal to bone whereas grade 3 suggests that it is greater.
synonym: "Echogenic bowel" EXACT []
synonym: "Echogenic foetal bowel" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Hyperechogenic fetal bowel" EXACT []
synonym: "Hyperechogenic foetal bowel" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Prenatal ultrasound: hyperechogenic bowel" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C2936423
is_a: HP:0011425 ! Fetal ultrasound soft marker
is_a: HP:0034207 ! Abnormal fetal gastrointestinal system morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2011-01-16T03:04:36Z

