[Term]
id: HP:0010945
name: Fetal pyelectasis
synonym: "تمدد حوض الكلية الجنيني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "اتساع حوض كلى الجنين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يُعرَف التمدد الطفيف لحوض الكلية بأنه مساحة حلقية متناغمة أو بيضاوية داخل حوض الكلية تبلغ ما لا يقل عن 5 ملم ولا تزيد عن 10 ملم. يتم القياس على مقطع عرضي من خلال حوض الكلية الجنيني باستخدام القياس الأقصى من الأمام إلى الخلف.
def: "Mild pyelectasis is defined as a hypoechoic spherical or elliptical space within the renal pelvis that measures at least 5mm and not more than 10 mm. The measurement is taken on a transverse section through the fetal renal pelvis using the maximum anterior-to-posterior measurement." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:16100637]
comment: The renal pelvis is the part of the kidney that collects urine. Fetal pyelectasis is a prenatal ultrasound finding that is diagnosed with enlargement of the renal pelvis from 4 to 10 millimeters. In many cases, fetal pyelectasis resolves spontaneously. Note that dilatation of the renal pelvis to more than 10 mm is referred to as severe pyelectasis or hydronephrosis. Measurements less than 5mm are normal, should not be designated as pyelectasis, and should not be reported (PMID:16100637).
synonym: "Fetal renal pelvic dilatation" EXACT []
synonym: "Foetal pyelectasis" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Foetal renal pelvic dilatation" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Mild fetal hydronephrosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Mild foetal hydronephrosis" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:430035004
xref: UMLS:C2317073
