[Term]
id: HP:0011034
name: Amyloid deposition
synonym: "ترسب الأميلويد" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تراكم الأميلويد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ترسبات مرضية لمجموعات بروتينية ليفية ذات خصائص مجهرية مميزة، خصوصًا عند الارتباط بصبغة كونغو الحمراء مع انكسار مميز.
def: "Pathologic deposits of specific fibrillar protein aggregates with distinct microscopic properties, particularly affinity for the dye Congo red with typical birefringence." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:21039326]
comment: Amyloid deposition is associated with amyloidosis, the pathologic process or disease caused by the tissue deposition of amyloid, often leading to organ dysfunction. This term, and its descendents, refer to the amyloid deposition (the phenotypic feature). Other clinical manifestations of amyloidosis should be coded separately.
synonym: "Amyloid disease" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6908-9849]
synonym: "Amyloidosis" BROAD []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:17602002
xref: UMLS:C0002726
is_a: HP:0001939 ! Abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2011-03-06T10:56:39Z

