[Term]
id: HP:0011169
name: Generalized clonic seizure
synonym: "نوبة رمعية معممّة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نوبة رمعية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: النوبة الرمعية المعممة هي نوع من النوبات الحركية المعممة التي تتميز برعشة ثنائية الجانبين، إما متناظرة أو غير متناظرة، تتكرر بانتظام وتشمل نفس المجموعات العضلية.
def: "Generalized clonic seizure is a type of generalized motor seizure characterized by sustained bilateral jerking, either symmetric or asymmetric, that is regularly repetitive and involves the same muscle groups." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:jalbers, PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
comment: Generalized clonic seizures are much less common than are tonic-clonic seizures, usually occur in infants, and should be distinguished from jitteriness or shuddering attacks.
synonym: "Generalised clonic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Generalised clonic seizures" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Generalised onset clonic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Generalised-onset clonic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Generalized clonic seizures" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Generalized onset clonic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Generalized-onset clonic seizure" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4023499
is_a: HP:0020221 ! Clonic seizure
is_a: HP:0032677 ! Generalized-onset motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
creation_date: 2011-11-19T09:53:43Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011170
name: Generalized myoclonic-atonic seizure
synonym: "النوبة الرمعية الوهطية المعممة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "اختلاج عام مفاجئ مع فقدان الطاقة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: النوبة الرمعية الوهطية المعممة هي نوع من النوبات الحركية المعممة التي تتميز برجفان رمعي يتبعه فقدان مفاجئ للطاقة الحركية.
def: "A generalized myoclonic-atonic seizure is a type of generalized motor seizure characterized by a myoclonic jerk followed by an atonic motor component." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:jalbers, PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
comment: A myoclonic-tonic seizure was previously called a myoclonic-astatic seizure. ILAE2017 does not currently consider myoclonic-atonic seizures to be a form of myoclonic seizure which is why it is classified as a motor seizure.
synonym: "Generalised myoclonic-atonic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Myoclonic atonic seizures" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Myoclonic-astatic seizure" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:230421008
xref: UMLS:C0393702
is_a: HP:0032677 ! Generalized-onset motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
creation_date: 2011-11-19T10:00:46Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011171
name: Simple febrile seizure
synonym: "نوبة حموية بسيطة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نوبة حموية خلال الحمى" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوبة معممة قصيرة، لا تتجاوز مدتها 15 دقيقة، ولا تتكرر خلال 24 ساعة، تحدث أثناء نوبة حمى غير ناتجة عن مرض حاد في الجهاز العصبي أو عدوى داخل الجمجمة أو اضطراب أيضي شديد.
def: "A short generalized seizure, of a duration of <15 min, not recurring within 24 h, occurring during a febrile episode not caused by an acute disease of the nervous system intracranial infection or severe metabolic disturbance." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:jalbers, PMID:19125841, PMID:6779259, PMID:972656]
comment: Fever may not be detected before the seizure, but it must be present at least in the immediate postacute period. In most cases these seizures are of a generalized tonic-clonic semiology.
synonym: "Simple febrile convulsion" EXACT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/febrile_seizure, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Simple febrile seizures" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Simple fever fit" EXACT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/febrile_seizure, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:432354000
xref: UMLS:C0149886
is_a: HP:0002373 ! Febrile seizure (within the age range of 3 months to 6 years)
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
creation_date: 2011-11-19T10:09:04Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011172
name: Complex febrile seizure
synonym: "نوبة حمى معقدة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوبة صرع حموية تتميز بواحدة أو أكثر من الخصائص التالية: دلالات بؤرية (أو مرتبطة بشذوذات عصبية بعد النوبة تتجاوز النعاس، مثل الشلل التودي)، نوبة ممتدة تتجاوز 15 دقيقة، أو تتكرر (تحدث أكثر من مرة) في فترة 24 ساعة.
def: "A febrile seizure that has any of the following features: focal semiology (or associated with post-ictal neurologic abnormalities beyond drowsiness, such as a Todd's paresis), prolonged seizure beyond 15 minutes, or recurring (occurring more than once) in a 24 hour period." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:jalbers, PMID:19125841, PMID:972656]
comment: Children presenting with a prolonged seizure stopped with anticonvulsive therapy (i.e., diazepam) before the 15th minute should be classified within this group.
synonym: "Complex febrile convulsion" EXACT []
synonym: "Complex febrile seizures" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Complex fever fit" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:433083002
xref: UMLS:C0751057
is_a: HP:0002373 ! Febrile seizure (within the age range of 3 months to 6 years)
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
creation_date: 2011-11-19T10:10:00Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011173
name: Focal behavior arrest seizure
synonym: "نوبة سلوك بؤري مع توقف" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نوبة توقف السلوك" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من النوبات البؤرية غير الحركية التي تتميز بتوقف أو تجميد الأنشطة، التجميد، أو التثبيت كميزة سيولوجية رئيسية طيلة النوبة.
def: "A type of focal non-motor seizure characterized by an arrest or pause of activities, freezing, or immobilization as the predominant semiological feature throughout the seizure." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:jalbers, PMID:28276060]
comment: The word 'focal' is explicit in the term title to emphasize the difference between these seizures and absence (generalized non-motor) seizures. Because brief behavior arrest is common and difficult to identify at the start of many seizures, the arrest must be persistent and dominant through the entire seizure. If the patient is able to identify that fear is the primary onset feature of the seizure, and results in immobility, the seizure is a focal emotional seizure with fear, and the immobility is then considered a descriptive feature, due to the fear. If the focal seizure is not characterized by this feature at the very outset of the seizure, it is not used to classify the seizure, it is instead used as a seizure descriptor, after the seizure is classified according to its onset feature.
synonym: "Focal behaviour arrest seizure" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Focal hypokinetic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Hypokinetic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Hypokinetic seizures" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Localised seizure with behavioral arrest" EXACT []
synonym: "Localised seizure with behavioural arrest" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Localized seizure with behavioral arrest" EXACT []
synonym: "Partial hypokinetic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Partial seizure with behavior arrest" EXACT []
synonym: "Partial seizure with behaviour arrest" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: UMLS:C4023498
is_a: HP:0032679 ! Focal non-motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
creation_date: 2011-11-19T10:12:04Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011174
name: Focal hyperkinetic seizure
synonym: "نوبة حركية مفرطة بؤرية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوبة بؤرية تتميز عند البداية بحركات بالستية غير منتظمة أساسها عضلات الأطراف القريبة أو العضلات المحورية، مثل التدوير، الدفع الحوضي، التزحلق، وحركات الاهتزاز.
def: "A focal seizure characterized at onset by predominantly proximal limb or axial muscles producing irregular sequential ballistic movements, such as pedaling, pelvic thrusting, thrashing, rocking movements." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:jalbers, PMID:11580774, PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
comment: The 2017 ILAE classification arbitrarily groups pedaling activity with hyperkinetic seizures, rather than with automatism seizures. However, some automatisms overlap other motor behaviors and where pedaling is slow and coordinated it may be considered an automatism.
synonym: "Hyperkinetic seizures" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Localised hyperkinetic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Localized hyperkinetic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Partial hyperkinetic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Segmental hyperkinetic seizure" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4023497
is_a: HP:0011153 ! Focal motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
creation_date: 2011-11-19T10:13:17Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011175
name: Focal motor seizure with version
synonym: "نوبة حركية بؤرية مع التوجه" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من النوبات الحركية البؤرية التي تتميز بتدوير قسري مستدام للعيون، الرأس، و/أو الجذع أو الانحراف الجانبي من الخط الوسطي كالأعرض السيولوجي الأصلي.
def: "A type of focal motor seizure characterized by sustained, forced conjugate ocular, cephalic, and/or truncal rotation or lateral deviation from the midline as the initial semiological manifestation." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:jalbers]
synonym: "Versive seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Versive seizures" EXACT plural_form []
