[Term]
id: HP:0011310
name: Bridged palmar crease
synonym: "خط راحة اليد المتصل" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خط يصل بين ثنايا راحة اليد المستعرضة القريب والبعيد.
def: "A crease that connects the proximal and distal transverse palmar creases." [PMID:19125433]
comment: The crease that connects the two transverse creases should itself be more in the transverse (antero-posterior) than longitudinal (proximo-distal) orientation.
synonym: "Bridged palm line" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Transitional palmar crease" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4021166
is_a: HP:0010490 ! Abnormality of the palmar creases
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
creation_date: 2012-02-12T12:56:40Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011311
name: Sydney crease
synonym: "ثني سيدني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خط سيدني في اليد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: امتداد للثنية المستعرضة القريبة (ثنية الخمس الأصابع) إلى حافة باطن اليد الزندية.
def: "Extension of the proximal transverse crease (five finger crease) to the ulnar edge of the palm." [PMID:19125433]
comment: The proximal transverse (five finger) crease starts on the radial side of the hand near the base of the index finger and extends toward the ulnar side of the palm, but does not reach the ulnar side. In this finding, the crease extends completely to the ulnar margin of the palm.
xref: UMLS:C4023420
is_a: HP:0010490 ! Abnormality of the palmar creases
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
creation_date: 2012-02-12T12:58:13Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011312
name: Fused nails
synonym: "أظافر ملتحمة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "أظافر ملتصقة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: لوح أظافر يحتوي على انشقاق طولي مع انفصال جزئي للأظافر، كل منها بتقوس جانبي منفصل.
def: "A nail plate that has a longitudinal separation with partially separated nails, each with a separate lateral radius of curvature." [PMID:19125433]
comment: The use of the word "fused" is not meant to imply that pathogenetically these nails were separate and merged. This is distinct from a split or cleaved nail, where the two parts of the nails share the same radius of curvature. The involved digits should be specified. It may be associated with underlying syndactylous digits, but these are coded separately.
synonym: "Fused nails" EXACT layperson []
xref: UMLS:C4023419
is_a: HP:0002164 ! Nail dysplasia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
creation_date: 2012-02-12T01:12:22Z

