[Term]
id: HP:0011333
name: Asymmetric crying face
synonym: "وجه بكاء غير متناظر" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدم تناسق يُلاحظ في وجه الوليد أو الرضيع الذي يبدو وجهه متناظرًا أثناء الراحة لكنه يصبح غير متناظر أثناء البكاء بسبب سحب الفم إلى الأسفل من جهة واحدة بينما لا يتحرك من الجهة الأخرى.
def: "Asymmetry observed in the face of a neonate or infant whose face appears symmetric at rest and asymmetric during crying as the mouth is pulled downward on one side while not moving on the other side." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2958-5076]
comment: Asymmetric crying facies is caused by underdevelopment of the depressor anguli oris muscle or compression of one of the branches of the facial nerve.
synonym: "Asymmetric crying face" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Hypoplasia of depressor angula oris muscle" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Partial unilateral facial paresis" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
