is_a: HP:0011395 ! Aplasia/Hypoplasia of the cochlea
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2012-03-07T08:31:27Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011376
name: Abnormal morphology of the vestibule of the inner ear
synonym: "شذوذ في شكل دهليز الأذن الداخلية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شكل غير عادي لدهليز الأذن" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ في شكل دهليز الأذن، وهو الجزء المركزي من المتاهة العظمية الذي يقع خلف القوقعة وأمام القنوات الهلالية.
def: "A morphological abnormality of the vestibule, the central part of the osseous labyrinth that is situated medial to the tympanic cavity, behind the cochlea, and in front of the semicircular canals." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:DDD_mbitner-glidicz]
comment: The vestibular system consists of five distinct components, three semicircular canals that are sensitive to angular acceleration and two otolith organs that are sensitive to linear acceleration.
synonym: "Morphological abnormality of the vestibule of the inner ear" EXACT []
synonym: "Vestibular abnormality" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C0542259
is_a: HP:0011390 ! Abnormal inner ear morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2012-03-07T08:35:08Z

