[Term]
id: HP:0011400
name: Abnormal CNS myelination
synonym: "شذوذ في تكوين المايلين في الجهاز العصبي المركزي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في تكوين أغشية الأعصاب" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ في تكوين المايلين للأعصاب في الجهاز العصبي المركزي.
alt_id: HP:0002520
alt_id: HP:0004335
def: "An abnormality of myelination of nerves in the central nervous system." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9102-5232]
comment: In the CNS, myelin is the product of oligodendrocytes (and not of Schwann cells, as in the PNS). This term refers to an abnormality of the process in which myelin sheaths are formed and maintained around neurons or the result of such an abnormality.
synonym: "Abnormal formation of myelin sheaths" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4021152
is_a: HP:0002011 ! Morphological central nervous system abnormality
is_a: HP:0012447 ! Abnormal myelination
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2012-03-12T07:24:42Z

