[Term]
id: HP:0011438
name: Maternal teratogenic exposure
synonym: "تعرض الأم لمواد مشوهة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تعرض الأم لمواد مشوهة خلال الحمل" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تاريخ طبي لتعرض أم طفل أو جنين لمادة مشوهة خلال الحمل.
def: "A medical history of exposure of the mother of a child or fetus to a teratogenic substance during pregnancy." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6410-0882]
comment: Commonly encountered maternal teratogens include alcohol, antiepileptic drugs, antihypertensive and antithyroid medications, aspirin, bisphosphonates, chemotherapy, monoclonal antibodies, ionizing radiation, recreational drugs, and serotonin-specific reuptake inhibitors (a class of antidepressants).
