id: HP:0011496
name: Corneal neovascularization
synonym: "الأوعية الدموية الجديدة في القرنية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تكون الأوعية الجديدة في القرنية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمو الأوعية الدموية الجديدة في القرنية.
def: "Ingrowth of new blood vessels into the cornea." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:DDD_ncarter, PMID:22898649]
comment: New blood vessels, which sprout from the capillaries and venules of the pericorneal plexus, may block light, compromise visual acuity, and lead to inflammation, corneal scarring, and edema. Corneal neovascularization may be a consequence of corneal hypoxia. Neovascular patterns can be separated into three clinical groups: deep neovascularization overlying Descemet's membrane (seen in herpetic and luetic interstitial keratitis), stromal neovascularization (as a result of stromal keratitis), and vascular pannus (from ocular surface disorders). Corneal pannus is subepithelial fibrovascular tissue ingrowth from the limbus onto the cornea that can be observed with corneal neovascularization.
synonym: "Corneal neovascularisation" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Corneal pannus" NARROW []
synonym: "Corneal vascularization" EXACT []
synonym: "Limbal neovascularization" EXACT []
synonym: "New blood vessel formation in cornea" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:19161004
xref: UMLS:C0085109
is_a: HP:0000481 ! Abnormal cornea morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2012-04-03T07:15:37Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011497
name: Rubeosis iridis
synonym: "روبيوسيس إيريديس" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تكون الأوعية الجديدة في القزحية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تكون الأوعية الدموية الجديدة على القزحية. لا تظهر الأوعية الجديدة نمط النمو الدائري المتناظر للأوعية الدموية الطبيعية للقزحية، بل تظهر بشكل غير منتظم. تبدأ الروبيوسيس عادة من حافة البؤبؤ مع زغب صغير من الشعيرات المتضخمة أو نقاط حمراء لا يمكن رؤيتها إلا بتكبير عالي.
alt_id: HP:0025319
def: "Formation of new blood vessels on the iris. The new vessels do not display the typical radially symmertic growth pattern of normal iris blood vessels, but rather appear disorganized. Rubeosis usually starts from the pupillary border with tiny tufts of dilated capillaries or red spots that can only be appreciated with high magnification." [PMID:27895936, PMID:29881517]
comment: See Figure 1 of PMID:29881517.
synonym: "Iris neovascularization" EXACT []
synonym: "Neovascularization of the iris" EXACT []
synonym: "New blood vessel formation in iris" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:51995000
xref: UMLS:C0154916
is_a: HP:0007905 ! Abnormal iris vasculature
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2012-04-03T07:32:43Z

