[Term]
id: HP:0011575
name: Imperforate tricuspid valve
synonym: "الصمام الثلاثي الشرفات غير المثقب" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "الصمام الثلاثي الشرفات المسدود" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الصمام الثلاثي الشرفات الذي لم يفتح.
def: "A tricuspid valve that has failed to open." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:DDD_dbrown, PMID:7066117]
comment: Imperforate valve is distinct from atretic valve. The hallmark of an imperforate valve is that it provides potential communication between an atrium and a ventricle. It exists as fused valve leaflets usually possessing their own hypoplastic tensor apparatus. The presence of an imperforate valve may have important surgical implications. Imperforate valve is in contrast to atretic valve with an absent atrioventricular connection. The cornerstone of the diagnosis of an imperformate valve is the identification of a thin mobile membrane between an atrium and a ventrile and the recognition of the tensor apparatus of the valve. In most cases the tensor apparatusis hypoplastic and it maynot be possible to delineate it by echocardiography.
synonym: "Unopened tricuspid valve" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6908-9849]
xref: UMLS:C4023292
is_a: HP:0001702 ! Abnormal tricuspid valve morphology
is_a: HP:0011574 ! Imperforate atrioventricular valve
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2012-04-08T10:37:55Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011576
name: Intermediate atrioventricular canal defect
synonym: "عيب قناة أذينية بطينية متوسط" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مجموعة من العيوب القلبية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مجموعة محددة من العيوب القلبية التي تشمل عيب الحاجز الأذيني البادئ، وشق الورقة الأمامية للصمام التاجي، وخلل مدخل البطين. هناك حلقة صمامية واحدة ومنافذ صمامية اثنين.
def: "A specific combination of heart defects with a primum atrial septal defect, cleft anterior mitral valve leaflet, and inlet ventricular defect. There is one valve annulus and two valve orifices." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:DDD_dbrown]
synonym: "Intermediate atrioventricular septal defect" EXACT []
xref: Fyler:1121
xref: UMLS:C4023291
is_a: HP:0006695 ! Atrioventricular canal defect
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2012-04-08T10:56:04Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011577
name: Partial atrioventricular canal defect
synonym: "عيب قناة أذينية بطينية جزئي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مجموعة من العيوب القلبية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مجموعة محددة من العيوب القلبية التي تشمل عيب الحاجز الأذيني البادئ وشق الورقة الأمامية للصمام التاجي. لا يوجد خلل في الحاجز البطيني للمدخل. هناك حلقتان صماميتان ومنافذ صمامية اثنين.
def: "A specific combination of heart defects including a primum atrial septal defect and cleft anterior mitral valve leaflet. There is not an inlet ventricular septal defect present. There are two valve annuluses and two valve orifices." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:DDD_dbrown]
synonym: "Incomplete atrioventricular septal defect" EXACT []
synonym: "Incomplete AVSD" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Partial atrioventricular septal defect" EXACT []
synonym: "Partial AVC defect" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Partial AVSD" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "PAVSD" EXACT abbreviation []
