[Term]
id: HP:0011636
name: Abnormal coronary artery origin
synonym: "شذوذ منشأ الشريان التاجي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "منشأ غير طبيعي للشريان التاجي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذات معزولة في مناشئ الشريان التاجي. قد تكون مرتبطة بأخرى من تشوهات القلب البنائية ولكن ليس الأنماط المعقدة من تشوهات القلب البنائية التي ينتج عنها مسار شاذ للشرايين التاجية.
def: "Isolated abnormalities of the coronary artery origins. This may be in associated with other structural heart malformations but not the patterns of complex structural heart malformations which result in abnormal course of the coronary arteries." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:DDD_dbrown]
xref: UMLS:C4023253
is_a: HP:0006704 ! Abnormal coronary artery morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2012-04-09T08:32:24Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011637
name: Anomalous origin of coronary artery from the pulmonary artery
synonym: "نشوء شريان تاجي شاذ من الشريان الرئوي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نشوء غير طبيعي لشريان القلب من الشريان الرئوي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يبدأ الشريان التاجي (يتفرع) من الشريان الرئوي بدلاً من أن يبدأ كالمعتاد من جذر الشريان الأورطي.
def: "A coronary artery begins (branches off from) the pulmonary artery rather than as normal from the root of the aorta." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:DDD_dbrown, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: UMLS:C4023252
is_a: HP:0011636 ! Abnormal coronary artery origin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2012-04-09T08:33:57Z

[Term]
id: HP:0011638
name: Anomalous origin of left coronary artery from the pulmonary artery
synonym: "النشوء الشاذ للشريان التاجي الأيسر من الشريان الرئوي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نشوء غير طبيعي للشريان التاجي من الشريان الرئوي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يبدأ الشريان التاجي الأيسر الرئيسي (يتفرع من) الشريان الرئوي بدلاً من أن يبدأ بشكل طبيعي من جذر الشريان الأبهر، فوق الوريقة اليسرى لصمام الأبهر.
def: "Left main coronary artery begins (branches off from) the pulmonary artery rather than as normal from the root of the aorta, above the left cusp of the aortic valve." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:DDD_dbrown, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:27358682]
comment: In this anomaly the function of the LMCA territory often requires extensive collateral formation from the RCA, which is often dilated. In the first month of life, physiologic pulmonary hypertension tends to preserve anterograde flow within the left coronary artery, and infants are usually asymptomatic. As pulmonary pressure drops, left-to-right shunting from the higher pressure left coronary arterial system to the lower pressure pulmonary arterial system occurs, and patients become symptomatic. Imaging findings may include markedly dilated collateral arteries and coronary veins.
synonym: "ALCAPA" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Anomalous left coronary artery from the pulmonary artery" EXACT []
synonym: "Bland-Garland-White syndrome" EXACT []
xref: Fyler:3101
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:450301003
xref: UMLS:C3472166
is_a: HP:0011637 ! Anomalous origin of coronary artery from the pulmonary artery
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2012-04-09T08:40:53Z

