creation_date: 2012-07-26T09:25:32Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012021
name: Persistent patent ductus venosus
synonym: "بقاء القناة الوريدية مفتوحة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "استمرار تدفق الدم عبر صلة وعائية بعد الولادة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: استمرار تدفق الدم عبر القناة الوريدية لفترة أطول من الوقت الطبيعي بعد الولادة.
def: "Persistence of blood flow through the ductus venosus for longer than the normal time after birth." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:16449256]
comment: The ductus venosus is a bypass between the umbilical vein and the inferior vena cava in the fetus. The blood flow through this bypass decreases immediately after birth. Functional closure, which is followed by anatomic closure, is virtually complete within a few weeks of birth.
xref: UMLS:C4023072
is_a: HP:0034190 ! Abnormal fetal cardiovascular physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2012-07-26T10:10:58Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012022
name: Congenital portosystemic venous shunt
synonym: "تحويلة وريدية بابية جهازية خلقية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في الأوعية الدموية بعدم مرور الدم عبر الكبد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل خلقي في الأوعية الدموية يؤدي إلى مرور الدم بطريقة مباشرة من الوريد البابي إلى الوريد الأجوف دون أن يتم تصفيته من خلال الكبد.
def: "A congenital defect of the vasculature such that there is a shunt (by-pass) of blood directly from the portal vein to the vena cava (i.e., the blood from the portal vein is not filtered through the liver)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:253330006
