creation_date: 2013-03-11T07:06:29Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012198
name: Juvenile colonic polyposis
synonym: "داء السلائل القولونية اليفع" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "سلائل متعددة في القولون" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود أكثر من 5 سلائل يفعية في القولون. يشير مصطلح 'السلائل اليفعية' إلى نسيج خاص وليس إلى عمر البداية حيث يمكن تشخيص السليل في جميع الأعمار. يظهر السليل اليفعي بشكل كروي ويتميز نسيجيًا بنمو مفرط للصفيحة المخاطية الوذمية مع خلايا التهابية وغدد كيسية.
def: "The presence of more than 5 juvenile polyps of the colon. The term juvenile polyps refer to a special histopathology and not the age of onset as the polyp might be diagnosed at all ages. The juvenile polyp has a spherical appearance and is microscopically characterized by overgrowth of an oedematous lamina propria with inflammatory cells and cystic glands." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:17768394, PMID:25022750]
comment: A juvenile polyp is a hamartomatous growth that projects from the lining of the intestine. It does not arise from the colonocytes themselves but from the tissues underneath the lining cells.
xref: UMLS:C4023006
is_a: HP:0004390 ! Hamartomatous polyposis
is_a: HP:0030255 ! Large intestinal polyposis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2013-03-11T07:09:42Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012199
name: Cluster headache
synonym: "صداع العنقود" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "صداع متكرر وشديد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من الصداع يتميز بهجمات متكررة من الألم الأحادي الجانب التي تدوم من 15 إلى 180 دقيقة وترتبط بعلامات تلقائية محلية.
def: "A type of headache characterized by repeated attacks of unilateral pain lasting 15 to 180 minutes and associated with local autonomic signs." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:21912573]
comment: According to the International Classification of Headache Disorders (ICHD-II), the diagnosis of cluster headache can be made with at least five attacks fulfilling criteria B-D: (B) Severe or very severe unilateral orbital, supraorbital and/or temporal pain lasting 15-180 minutes if untreated. (C) Headache is accompanied by at least 1 of the following: (i) Ipsilateral conjunctival injection and/or lacrimation. (ii) Ipsilateral nasal congestion and/or rhinorrhea. (iii) Ipsilateral eyelid edema. (iv) Ipsilateral forehead and facial sweating. (v) Ipsilateral miosis and/or ptosis. (vi) A sense of restlessness or agitation. (D) Attacks have a frequency from 1 every other day to 8/day. Additionally, the headaches cannot attributed to another disorder.
xref: ICD-10:G44.0 "Cluster headache syndrome"
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:193031009
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:193947008
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:230473009
xref: UMLS:C0009088
is_a: HP:0002315 ! Headache
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2013-03-12T11:37:40Z

