[Term]
id: HP:0012272
name: J wave
synonym: "موجة J" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "موجة J في تخطيط القلب" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: موجة J هي انحراف إيجابي محدب يحدث عند تقاطع المركب QRS مع مقطع ST، عند نقطة J.
def: "The J wave is a positive convex deflection that occurs at the junction of the QRS complex and ST segment, the J-point." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19561994]
comment: J waves can be seen in hypothermia when the core body temperature falls below 32 degrees C. Then, they occur most prominently in the inferior leads: II, III, and aVF and the precordial leads: V5-V6. J waves can also be observed in other conditions such as some forms of Brugada syndrome.
synonym: "EKG J waves" EXACT []
synonym: "Osborne waves" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4018858
is_a: HP:0003115 ! Abnormal EKG
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2013-04-07T02:11:05Z

