[Term]
id: HP:0012318
name: Occipital neuralgia
synonym: "ألم عصبي قذالي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "صداع في قاعدة الرأس" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع مميز من الصداع يتميز بألم مزمن حاد أو نابض أو يشبه الصدمة الكهربائية في أعلى العنق، الجزء الخلفي من الرأس، وخلف الأذنين، وعادةً ما يكون في جهة واحدة.
def: "A distinct type of headache characterized by piercing, throbbing, or electric-shock-like chronic pain in the upper neck, back of the head, and behind the ears, usually on one side." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:21569290]
comment: Typically, the pain of occipital neuralgia begins at the base of the head and spreads upward within the distribution of the greater and lesser occipital nerves. Characteristically, it is neuropathic, with paroxysmal episodes of shooting electric shock-like symptoms.
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:71760005
xref: UMLS:C0007863
is_a: HP:0002315 ! Headache
is_a: HP:0033345 ! Neuralgia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2013-08-10T01:07:45Z

