[Term]
id: HP:0012422
name: Villous hypertrophy of choroid plexus
synonym: "تضخم خيمات في الضفيرة المشيموية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تضخم في الضفيرة المشيموية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمو زائد في الضفيرة المشيموية.
def: "Overgrowth of the choroid plexus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:16523225]
comment: The most common location for overgrowth is the lateral ventricles. The choroid plexus folds into many villi around capillaries, creating frond-like processes that project into the ventricles. The terms choroid plexus hypertrophy or choroid plexus hyperplasia are used interchangeably to refer to an increase in size of these structures. Diffuse villous hyperplasia of choroid plexus (DVHCP) is a rare condition which is characterized by the presence of diffuse enlargement of the entire choroid plexus throughout the length of the choroidal fissure and overproduction of CSF.
synonym: "Choroid plexus hypertrophy" EXACT []
synonym: "Diffuse villous hypertrophy of choroid plexus" RELATED []
xref: UMLS:C4020728
xref: UMLS:C4021089
is_a: HP:0007376 ! Abnormal choroid plexus morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2013-11-11T07:50:37Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012423
name: Colonic inertia
synonym: "الجمود القولوني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدم حركة القولون" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدم قدرة القولون على تعديل البراز إلى قوام مقبول وتحريكه من الأعور إلى منطقة المستقيم السيني مرة واحدة على الأقل كل ثلاثة أيام.
def: "The inability of the colon to modify stool to an acceptable consistency and move the stool from the cecum to the rectosigmoid area at least once every three days." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:23449085]
xref: UMLS:C1257861
is_a: HP:0012700 ! Abnormal large intestine physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2013-11-11T08:04:46Z

