[Term]
id: HP:0012456
name: Medial arterial calcification
synonym: "تكلس الشريان الإنسي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تكلس في الشرايين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تكلس، وهو ترسب مرضي لأملاح الكالسيوم في الطبقة الوسطى من الشرايين.
def: "Calcification, that is, pathological deposition of calcium salts in the tunica media of arteries." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Medial arterial calcification causes stiffening and decreased compliance of the affected arteries.
xref: UMLS:C4022896
is_a: HP:0003207 ! Arterial calcification
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
