[Term]
id: HP:0012463
name: Elevated transferrin saturation
synonym: "ارتفاع تشبع الترانسفيرين" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة في التشبع بالحديد في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مستوى أعلى من المعتاد لتشبع ترانسفيرين المصل بالحديد.
def: "An above normal level of saturation of serum transferrin with iron." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Transferrins are iron-binding blood plasma glycoproteins that control the level of free iron in biological fluids. The transferrin saturation test (TSAT) refers to the ratio of serum iron to total iron-binding capacity, expressed as a percentage. Transferrin saturations of less than 20% indicate iron deficiency, while transferrin saturations of more than 50% suggest iron overload. Note that the results of the TSAT can be influenced by inflammation.
xref: UMLS:C4022892
is_a: HP:0040135 ! Abnormal transferrin saturation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2013-11-24T12:46:56Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012464
name: Decreased transferrin saturation
synonym: "انخفاض تشبع الترانسفيرين" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انخفاض مستوى الترانسفيرين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مستوى أقل من الطبيعي لتشبع ترانسفيرين السيروم بالحديد.
def: "A below normal level of saturation of serum transferrin with iron." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Transferrins are iron-binding blood plasma glycoproteins that control the level of free iron in biological fluids. The transferrin saturation test (TSAT) refers to the ratio of serum iron to total iron-binding capacity, expressed as a percentage. Transferrin saturations of less than 20% indicate iron deficiency, while transferrin saturations of more than 50% suggest iron overload. Note that the results of the TSAT can be influenced by inflammation.
xref: UMLS:C0919785
is_a: HP:0040135 ! Abnormal transferrin saturation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2013-11-24T12:51:51Z

