[Term]
id: HP:0012491
name: Abnormal dense tubular system
synonym: "شذوذ الجهاز الأنبوبي الكثيف" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تغير في الجهاز الأنبوبي الكثيف" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل في المركبات الغشائية الداخلية المعروفة بالجهاز الأنبوبي الكثيف.
def: "An anomaly of the intracellular membrane complexes known as the dense tubular system." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7744-1790, PMID:1322202]
comment: The dense tubular system (DTS) functions to regulate platelet activation by sequestering or releasing calcium, similar to the sarcotubules of skeletal muscle. In resting platelets, the DTS exists as thin elongated membranes. Within 10 seconds of the addition of thrombin, platelets show a major ultrastructural change in their DTS: from the thin elongated form to a rounded vesicular form.
xref: UMLS:C4022881
is_a: HP:0011875 ! Abnormal platelet morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2013-11-29T09:35:44Z

