[Term]
id: HP:0012705
name: Abnormal metabolic brain imaging by MRS
synonym: "اضطراب في التصوير الأيضي للدماغ بواسطة MRS" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في التصوير الأيضي للدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل في الأيض في الدماغ يتم تحديده بواسطة مطيافية الرنين المغناطيسي (MRS).
def: "An anomaly of metabolism in the brain identified by magnetic resonance spectroscopy (MRS)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: MRS can only detect a few metabolites as least millimolar concentrations are necessary for the metabolites to be detected. The major brain metabolites detected are choline (Cho), creatine (Cr), N-acetyl aspartate (NAA), lactate, myo-inositol, glutamine and glutamate, lipids, and the amino acids leucine and alanine.
xref: UMLS:C4022764
is_a: HP:0410263 ! Brain imaging abnormality
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2014-03-22T08:04:18Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012706
name: Elevated brain choline level by MRS
synonym: "ارتفاع مستوى الكولين في الدماغ بواسطة الرنين المغناطيسي الطيفي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة الكولين في الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة في مستوى مركبات الكولين في الدماغ تُكتشف بواسطة الرنين المغناطيسي الطيفي.
def: "An increase in the level of choline-containing compounds in the brain identified by magnetic resonance spectroscopy (MRS)." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:UToronto_htrang]
comment: The Choline (Cho) peak is a heterogeneous peak representing various choline-containing compounds such as acetylcholine, phosphocholine (lecithin), glycerophosphocholine, and various other intermediates of phospholipids metabolism. It is an indicator of cell density and cell wall turnover. Elevated levels are found in tumors, especially malignant ones, and in certain demyelinating diseases. Choline resonance presents at 3.22 ppm. Studies have shown there is also a direct association between Cho and levels of Ki-67, a protein expressed in all phases of the cell cycle except GO that serves as a good marker for cellular proliferation. This observation makes Cho a reliable predictor of cellular activity in tumor tissue.
xref: UMLS:C4022763
is_a: HP:0025047 ! Abnormal brain choline level by MRS
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2014-03-22T08:06:29Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012707
name: Elevated brain lactate level by MRS
synonym: "ارتفاع مستوى اللاكتات في الدماغ بواسطة الرنين المغناطيسي الطيفي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة اللاكتات في الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة في مستوى اللاكتات في الدماغ تُكتشف بواسطة الرنين المغناطيسي الطيفي.
def: "An increase in the level of lactate in the brain identified by magnetic resonance spectroscopy (MRS)." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:UToronto_htrang]
comment: Lactate (Lac) is absent in normal brain tissue and its presence is indicative of anerobic glycolysis at the cellular level. Elevated levels are associated with ischemic conditions or metabolic disorders (where anerobic glycolysis predominates) but is also noted at the edges of large brain tumors. The peak is very sensitive to the technique employed and unless the correct echo time is employed, it may be artifactually suppressed. The spectral peak lies at 1:33 ppm. The peak is often inverted or bifid.
xref: UMLS:C4022762
is_a: HP:0025045 ! Abnormal brain lactate level by MRS
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2014-03-22T08:08:20Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012708
name: Reduced brain N-acetyl aspartate level by MRS
synonym: "انخفاض مستوى الأسيتيل أسبارتات N في الدماغ بواسطة الرنين المغناطيسي الطيفي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انخفاض N-acetyl aspartate في الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انخفاض في مستوى الأسيتيل أسبارتات N في الدماغ يُكتشف بواسطة التصوير بالرنين المغناطيسي الطيفي.
def: "A decrease in the level of N-acetyl aspartate in the brain identified by magnetic resonance spectroscopy (MRS)." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:UToronto_htrang]
comment: N-Acetyl Aspartate (NAA) is an amino acid found exclusively in neurons. It is regarded as a non-specific marker and is thought to be involved in Coenzyme A interactions and lipogenesis within the brain. It is a marker of neuronal viability. Normal NAA concentration is in the range of 8-9 mmol/kg in healthy adult brain. Concentrations are decreased in conditions leading to axonal injury or neuronal loss. NAA is also decreased in other conditions such as neoplasm, infarction, and inflammatory conditions such as multiple sclerosis. NAA peak is seen at 2.0 ppm (parts per million) on MR spectra.
synonym: "MR Spectroscopy: N-acetylaspartate low in brain" EXACT []
synonym: "Reduced brain N-acetyl aspartate level by magnetic resonance spectroscopy" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4022761
is_a: HP:0025052 ! Abnormal brain N-acetyl aspartate level by MRS
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2014-03-22T08:09:12Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012709
name: Abnormal brain choline/creatine ratio by MRS
synonym: "شذوذ في نسبة الكولين/الكرياتين في الدماغ بواسطة MRS" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نسبة غير طبيعية للكولين/الكرياتين في الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انحراف عن النسبة الطبيعية بين الكولين والكرياتين في الدماغ يتم تحديده بواسطة مطيافية الرنين المغناطيسي (MRS).
def: "A deviation from normal in the ratio of choline to creatine in the brain identified by magnetic resonance spectroscopy (MRS)." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:UToronto_htrang]
comment: Creatine (Cr) is related to cell energy pathways, being both the substrate and product of creatine kinase. Creatine reflects the energy potential available in brain tissue. Its concentration in normal brain remains very high and stable due to high metabolic energy needs of brain cells. Its peak is noticed at 3.0 ppm. Creatine-Choline ratios are an important indicator of disease states such as demyelization.
xref: UMLS:C4022760
is_a: HP:0012705 ! Abnormal metabolic brain imaging by MRS
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2014-03-22T08:12:15Z

