[Term]
id: HP:0012757
name: Abnormal neuron morphology
synonym: "شذوذ شكل العصبون" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شكل غير طبيعي للعصبون" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ هيكلي للعصبون. العصبونات هي خلايا قابلة للتحفيز الكهربي تنقل الإشارات في الجسم. يستخدم العصبون مكونات كهربائية وكيميائية لنقل المعلومات. يتصل العصبون بعصبونات أخرى عند المشابك العصبية ويتصل بالأعضاء أو الخلايا المستهدفة عند مفاصل العصبون-المؤثر.
def: "A structural anomaly of a neuron. Neurons are electrically excitable cells that transmit signals throughout the body. Neurons employ both electrical and chemical components in the transmission of information. Neurons are connected to other neurons at synapses and connected to effector organs or cells at neuroeffector junctions." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:KI_phemming, PMID:28723006]
synonym: "Abnormal neuron shape" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Abnormal neuronal morphology" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4022739
is_a: HP:0012639 ! Abnormal nervous system morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2014-04-02T05:12:30Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012758
name: Neurodevelopmental delay
synonym: "تأخر النمو العصبي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تأخر في النمو العصبي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يشير تأخر النمو العصبي إلى التأخير في نضج الدماغ والجهاز العصبي المركزي؛ وقد يعاني الرضع والأطفال الصغار الذين يعانون من تأخر النمو العصبي من تأخيرات في تطور مهارات متعددة مثل القدرات الحركية الجسيمة، والتنسيق الحركي الدقيق، والقدرات اللغوية والقدرة على حل المشكلات المعقدة بشكل متزايد.
def: "Neurodevelopmental delay (NDD) refers to delays in the maturation of the brain and central nervous system; infants and young children with NDD may experience delays in the development of one or more skills including gross motor abilities, fine-motor coordination, language abilities and ability to solve increasingly complex problems." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6670-9157, PMID:31783983]
comment: Though the definitions of NDD vary broadly in the literature, all are used to signify a delay in one or more developmental domains compared to typical development.
synonym: "NDD" EXACT abbreviation []
xref: UMLS:C4022738
is_a: HP:0012759 ! Neurodevelopmental abnormality
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2014-04-03T12:16:19Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012759
name: Neurodevelopmental abnormality
synonym: "شذوذ في النمو العصبي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تأخر في النمو العصبي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انحراف عن الطبيعي في النمو العصبي للطفل، وقد يشمل أيا أو جميع جوانب تطور القدرات الشخصية والاجتماعية والحركية الكبرى أو الدقيقة والقدرات المعرفية.
def: "A deviation from normal of the neurological development of a child, which may include any or all of the aspects of the development of personal, social, gross or fine motor, and cognitive abilities." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:KI_phemming]
comment: This term should be used to describe abnormalities with onset in the developmental period.
xref: UMLS:C4022737
is_a: HP:0012638 ! Abnormal nervous system physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2014-04-03T12:20:28Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012760
name: Reduced social responsiveness
synonym: "استجابة اجتماعية منخفضة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "صعوبة في التفاعل الاجتماعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: قدرة منخفضة على المشاركة في التدفق المتبادل للتفاعل الاجتماعي المناسب للثقافة والمستوى التطوري، الذي يتميز عادة بتأثير سلوك شخص ما على سلوك شخص آخر. ينتج عن ذلك صعوبة في التفاعل مع الآخرين عبر التواصل العاطفي أو البدني أو اللفظي.
alt_id: HP:0000735
alt_id: HP:5200004
alt_id: HP:5200103
alt_id: HP:5200131
def: "A reduced ability to participate in the back-and-forth flow of social interaction appropriate to culture and developmental level, which is normally characterized by an influence of the behavior of one person on the behavior of another person. This results in difficulty interacting with others through emotional, physical, or verbal communication." [PMID:28707360, PMID:34924788]
comment: Reciprocity can be assessed by determining the extent to which a child demonstrates activity similar to that of peers or of the examiner (e.g., playing the same game), shows turn-taking behavior, or recognizes the intentions of the other person and contributes to an activity that a peer or the examiner has initiated. In the diagnostic process, it may be difficult to decide whether limitations in social behavior of children with intellectual disability (ID) are due to a co-occurring autism spectrum disorder (ASD) and are often unduly attributed to the ID, a phenomenon also known as diagnostic overshadowing. This term is intended to apply to impaired social reciprocity that is not attributed to ID.
synonym: "Impaired social interaction" EXACT []
synonym: "Impaired social interactions" EXACT []
synonym: "Impaired social reciprocity" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9112-5148, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6670-9157, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9593-5508]
synonym: "Poor social interactions" EXACT layperson []
xref: UMLS:C4022736
is_a: HP:0025732 ! Abnormal social development
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9112-5148
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6670-9157
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9593-5508
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2014-04-03T12:52:44Z

[Term]
id: HP:0012761
name: Absent mastoid
synonym: "غياب النتوء الحلمي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدم وجود النتوء الحلمي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل تطوري حيث يفشل النتوء الحلمي في التكون ويكون غائباً خلقياً.
alt_id: HP:0200110
def: "A developmental anomaly in which the mastoid process fails to form and is thus found to be congenitally absent." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Absent mastoids" EXACT []
synonym: "Failure of development of mastoid" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Mastoid agenesis" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
