[Term]
id: HP:0020085
name: Infection following live vaccination
synonym: "عدوى بعد التطعيم الحي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى بسبب لقاح حي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى ناتجة عن اللقاحات الموهنة الحية، وهي لقاحات تُحضر من فيروسات أو بكتيريا حية تم إضعافها في المختبر. تتكاثر هذه اللقاحات في الشخص المطعم وتنتج استجابة مناعية ولكن عادة ما تسبب مرضًا خفيفًا أو لا تسبب مرضًا. تُشتق من مسببات الأمراض المسببة للأمراض.
def: "An infection resulting from live attenuated vaccines (LAV), that is, a vaccine prepared from living viruses or bacteria that have been weakened under laboratory conditions. LAV vaccines will replicate in a vaccinated individual and produce an immune response but usually cause mild or no disease. are derived from disease-causing pathogens." []
is_a: HP:0032101 ! Unusual infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-04-08T17:21:47Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0020086
name: BCGitis
synonym: "عدوى بكتيريا السل بعد التطعيم BCG" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى موضعية بسبب لقاح BCG" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى موضعية أو إقليمية ببكتيريا السُل-كالْميت-غِيران (BCG) بعد التطعيم.
def: "Local or regional infection with Bacillus Calmette-Guerin (BCG) following vaccination." [PMID:24722620]
comment: The Bacillus Calmette-Guerin (BCG) vaccine has existed for 80 years and is one of the most widely used of all current vaccines. The BCG vaccine has a protective effect against meningitis and disseminated tuberculosis in children. or most children, BCG vaccination is harmless. However, infection, even disseminated infection, caused by BCG has occasionally been reported. The incidence of BCG infection is approximately one in ten thousand to a million. The BCG-induced disease phenotypes were designated as local, regional, distant, or disseminated pattern. The former two patterns were conventionally termed as BCGitis and the latter two as BCGosis.
is_a: HP:0020085 ! Infection following live vaccination
property_value: dc:date "2019-04-08T17:25:28Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0020087
name: BCGosis
synonym: "عدوى موزعة بكتيريا BCG" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى منتشرة بسبب لقاح BCG" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى بعيدة أو موزعة ببكتيريا السُل-كالْميت-غِيران (BCG) بعد التطعيم، والتي ترتبط بفشل في احتواء بكتيريا BCG مما يؤدي إلى انتشارها في العديد من الأماكن في الجسم. يحتوي لقاح السل BCG على ميكوبكتيريا موهنة من الـ Mycobacterium bovis.
alt_id: HP:0031698
def: "Distant, or disseminated infection with Bacillus Calmette-Guerin (BCG) following vaccination associated with failure to contain thebacillus Calmette-Guerin (BCG) following vaccination leading to spread of BCG to many sites in the body. The tuberculosis vaccine BCG contains live attenuated Mycobacterium bovis." [PMID:21412596, PMID:24722620]
comment: The Bacillus Calmette-Guerin (BCG) vaccine has existed for 80 years and is one of the most widely used of all current vaccines. The BCG vaccine has a protective effect against meningitis and disseminated tuberculosis in children. or most children, BCG vaccination is harmless. However, infection, even disseminated infection, caused by BCG has occasionally been reported. The incidence of BCG infection is approximately one in ten thousand to a million. The BCG-induced disease phenotypes were designated as local, regional, distant, or disseminated pattern. The former two patterns were conventionally termed as BCGitis and the latter two as BCGosis.
synonym: "BCGiosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Disseminated Bacillus Calmette-Guerin infection" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020085 ! Infection following live vaccination
property_value: dc:date "2019-04-08T17:27:13Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0020088
