[Term]
id: HP:0020101
name: Invasive fungal infection
synonym: "عدوى فطرية غازية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى فطرية متوغلة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى فطرية تتسم بتوغلات في أنسجة العائل.
def: "Fungal infection characterized by invasion of host tissues." [PMID:24718393]
comment: Invasive fungal infections are a significant health problem in immunocompromised patients. Major risk factors for IFI include neutropenia less than 500 neutrophils/ml for more than 10 days, hematological malignancies, bone marrow transplantation, prolonged (over 4 wk) treatment with corticosteroids; prolonged (over 7 days) stays in intensive care, chemotherapy, HIV infection, invasive medical procedures, and the newer immune suppressive agents.
is_a: HP:0020100 ! Unusual fungal infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-04-08T19:11:15Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0020102
name: Pneumocystis jirovecii pneumonia
synonym: "ذات الرئة بواسطة الفطر المتكيسة الجؤجؤية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى فطرية في الرئة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مرض انتهازي ناتج عن توغل الفطر المتكيسة الجؤجؤية الأحادي الخلية. يتم نقل أكياس المتكيسة الجؤجؤية عبر الطرق الهوائية، وعادةً ما تكون موجودتها في الرئتين بدون أعراض. ومع ذلك، فإن الأشخاص الذين يعانون من ضعف المناعة، خاصةً أولئك الذين يكون لديهم عد خلايا T CD4+ أقل من 200/ ميكرولتر، يكونون عرضة لخطر تطور ذات الرئة المتكيسة بسبب توغل المتكيسة الجؤجؤية. الأعراض الناتجة عن هذا المرض غير محددة: ضيق نفسي تطوري، سعال غير منتج، حمى طفيفة، ضغط جزئي للشريان تحت 65 ملم زئبقي، وصور الصدر تظهر ظلالًا بينية ثنائية.
alt_id: HP:0034286
def: "An opportunistic disease caused by invasion of unicellular fungus Pneumocystis jirovecii. Transmission of P. jirovecii cysts takes place through the airborne route, and usually, its presence in lungs is asymptomatic. However, people with impaired immunity, especially those with CD4+ T cell count below 200/microliter, are still at risk of the development of Pneumocystis pneumonia due to P. jirovecii invasion. Symptoms induced by this disease are not specific: progressive dyspnea, non-productive cough, low-grade fever, arterial partial pressure of oxygen below 65 mmHg, and chest radiographs demonstrating bilateral, interstitial shadowing." [PMID:26281787]
comment: Pneumocystis pneumonia (PCP) is caused by Pneumocystis jirovecii, a ubiquitous fungus. The taxonomy of the organism has been changed; Pneumocystis carinii now refers only to the Pneumocystis that infects rats, and P. jirovecii refers to the distinct species that infects humans. However, the abbreviation PCP is still the preferred acronym to designate the clinical syndrome of Pneumocystis pneumonia, although PJP is commonly used.
synonym: "Pneumocystis carinii pneumonia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032255 ! Opportunistic fungal infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-04-08T19:15:19Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0020103
name: Invasive pulmonary aspergillosis
synonym: "التهاب رئوي غزوي بالأَسبرجِلَّس" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى فطرية في الرئة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى الرئة بالأَسبرجِلَّس. قد تتبرعم الأبواغ في المخاطية التنفسية إلى خيوط فطرية، والتي بدورها يمكن أن تتوغل في المخاطية مسببة التهاب رئوي غزوي بالأَسبرجِلَّس.
def: "Infection of the lungs with aspergillus. In the respiratory mucosa, the spores may germinate into hyphae, which in turn can invade the mucosa leading to invasive pulmonary aspergillosis." [PMID:25656673]
comment: Invasive pulmonary aspergillosis usually occurs in severely immunocompromised patients. Classic at-risk patients are those with prolonged neutropenia, either due to chemotherapy or immunosuppressive therapy, post hematopoietic stem cell transplant (SCT), or solid organ transplant.
is_a: HP:0020101 ! Invasive fungal infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-04-08T19:17:44Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

