synonym: "الحمل بواسطة تقنيات المساعدة على الإنجاب" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "الإخصاب الصناعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تاريخ الحمل بواسطة تقنيات المساعدة على الإنجاب مثل التخصيب في المختبر (IVF)، وحقن الحيوانات المنوية داخل السيتوبلازم (ICSI)، وحفظ الأجنة بالتجميد.
def: "A history of conception by an assisted reproductive technology such as in vitro fertilization (IVF), intracytoplasmic sperm injection (ICSI), and cryopreservation." [PMID:28844405]
comment: Assisted reproductive technology is used primarily for infertility treatments to achieve pregnancy.
is_a: HP:0032443 ! Past medical history
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2019-07-02T16:46:09Z

[Term]
id: HP:0020122
name: Bite cells
synonym: "خلايا العضة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلايا الدم بشكل غير طبيعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلايا دم حمراء تبدو وكأن أجزاء منها مقضومة.
def: "Red blood cells that appear to have parts of them bitten away." [ISBN:978-0-07174889-6]
comment: This feature can be observed with acute hemolytic anemia (AHA) related to glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency. In this disorder, AHA can be triggered by ingestion of fave beans, infections, and certain medications. The blood film can show poikilocytosis with bite cells.
synonym: "Blister cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Degmacytes" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004447 ! Poikilocytosis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2019-07-02T20:24:07Z

[Term]
id: HP:0020123
name: Tympanosclerosis
synonym: "تصلب الطبلة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تصلب في طبلة الأذن" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تصلب في غشاء الطبلة بسبب التكلس، يظهر عادةً على شكل لويحات بيضاء، ويشمل مناطق محددة من غشاء الطبلة و/أو الأذن الوسطى.
def: "A stiffening of the tympanic membrane due to calcification, typically presents as white plaque-like lesions, involving discrete regions of the tympanic membrane and/or middle ear." [PMID:27656306]
comment: Plaques related to tympanosclerosis do not form spherical lesions and are typically within the drum substance itself which is normally easily discerned when using the binocular view of a microscope rather than the monocular, two-dimensional view of a hand-held otoscope. Such plaques can alter compliance of the tympanic membrane and can lead to sclerotic fixation of the ossicles, both of which can result in a mild conductive hearing loss. Histologically, lesions vary slightly according to their stage of development showing differing amounts of increased fibroblasts, abnormal fibers, areas of hyalinization, and areas of calcification into an osseous-like matrix. Most patients require no treatment.
synonym: "Tympanic calcification" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0008609 ! Abnormal middle ear morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2019-07-02T20:36:06Z

