[Term]
id: HP:0020141
name: Blood pressure substantially higher in legs than arms
synonym: "ضغط الدم أعلى بشكل ملحوظ في الساقين مقارنة بالذراعين" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "فرق ضغط الدم بين الساقين والذراعين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: فرق غير طبيعي في ضغط الدم بين الأطراف العلوية والسفلية حيث يكون ضغط الدم في الساقين أعلى بكثير من ضغط الدم في الذراعين. في الأفراد الأصحاء، تكون قياسات ضغط الدم الانقباضي للكاحل أعلى قليلاً فقط من ضغط الدم الانقباضي المقيس في الذراع.
def: "An abnormal blood pressure discrepancy between the upper and lower extremities with the blood pressure measured in the legs being much higher than the blood pressure measure in the arms. In healthy individuals, ankle systolic blood pressures are only slightly higher than the systolic blood pressure measured in the arm." [PMID:12101189]
comment: This feature may be seen, for instance, in Takayasu arteritis.
synonym: "Blood pressure substantially higher in lower than upper extremities" EXACT []
synonym: "Blood pressure substantially lower in arms than legs" EXACT []
synonym: "Blood pressure substantially lower in upper than lower extremities" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030972 ! Abnormal systemic blood pressure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2019-07-05T17:52:19Z

[Term]
id: HP:0020142
name: Blood pressure substantially higher in arms than legs
synonym: "ضغط الدم أعلى بشكل ملحوظ في الذراعين مقارنة بالساقين" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "فرق ضغط الدم بين الذراعين والساقين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: فرق غير طبيعي في ضغط الدم بين الأطراف العلوية والسفلية حيث يكون ضغط الدم في الذراعين أعلى بكثير من ضغط الدم في الساقين. في الأفراد الأصحاء، تكون قياسات ضغط الدم الانقباضي للكاحل أعلى قليلاً فقط من ضغط الدم الانقباضي المقيس في الذراع.
def: "An abnormal blood pressure discrepancy between the upper and lower extremities with the blood pressure measured in the arms being much higher than the blood pressure measure in the legs. In healthy individuals, ankle systolic blood pressures are only slightly higher than the systolic blood pressure measured in the arm." [PMID:28377475]
comment: This feature can be observed in aortic coarctation.
synonym: "Blood pressure substantially higher in upper than lower extremities" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased arm-leg blood pressure gradient" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030972 ! Abnormal systemic blood pressure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2019-07-05T17:56:44Z

[Term]
id: HP:0020143
name: Tracheal duplication cyst
synonym: "كيس تكراري في الرغامى" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "كيس في الرغامى" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: كيس في الرغامى، جدرانه تتكون من نسيج مشابه لشجرة القصبات، بما في ذلك الغضاريف والعضلات الملساء، وهو مبطن بنسيج ظهاري تنفسي إفرازي يتكون من خلايا مهدبة مكعبة أو عمودية.
def: "A cyst in the trachea, whose wall is made up by tissue similar to the bronchial tree, including cartilage and smooth muscle, and is lined by secretory respiratory epithelium composed of cuboid or columnar ciliated epithelium." [PMID:25313910]
comment: Tracheal duplication cyst is a rare congenital malformation presenting in childhood with stridor or dysphagia from a mass effect on the trachea or esophagus. The features of the tracheal duplication cyst are similar to those of bronchogenic duplication cyst and laryngeal duplication cyst, but with histopathological features of the trachea. The trachea is known to originate from the respiratory diverticulum, a ventral outpouching of foregut lumen. The postulated embryological basis of a tracheal duplication cyst may be similar to that of the anomalous bronchi and is a result of abnormal budding of the bronchial tree during the fourth to sixth weeks of embryogenesis.
is_a: HP:0002778 ! Abnormal tracheal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2019-07-05T19:01:46Z

[Term]
id: HP:0020144
name: Calcium phosphate crystalluria
synonym: "بلورات فوسفات الكالسيوم في البول" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "بلورات في البول" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود بلورات فوسفات الكالسيوم في البول.
def: "The presence of calcium phosphate crystals in the urine." [PMID:26509782, PMID:3599249, PMID:8671802]
comment: Calcium phosphate crystals are pleiomorphic, often appearing as birefringent stars or needles, occurring in isolation or in clumps. Plates are granular and non-birefringent.
is_a: HP:0020074 ! Crystalluria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2019-07-05T19:05:11Z

[Term]
id: HP:0020145
name: Calcium oxalate crystalluria
synonym: "جير بولي أوكزالات الكالسيوم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "أوكسالات الكالسيوم في البول" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود بلورات أوكزالات الكالسيوم في البول.
def: "The presence of calcium oxalate crystals in the urine." [PMID:26509782, PMID:3599249, PMID:8671802]
comment: There are two types of calcium oxalate crystals, the dihydrate (or Wedellite) and the monohydrate (orWhewellite), which are frequently found together in the same sample. The former have mostly a typical bipyramidal shape, while the latter are more pleiomorphic, although the ovoid shape is the most frequent. Bipyramidal crystals are birefringent only when large or in aggregates, but even then birefringence is usually not intense. The monohydrates, however, are always strongly birefringent. Calcium oxalate may be found in normal subjects, often as a consequence of ingestion of foods like chocolate, beet-root, peanuts, rhubarb, spinach, etc., in stoneformers, in patients with hyperoxaluria, or after ethylene glycol poisoning.
is_a: HP:0020074 ! Crystalluria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2019-07-05T19:06:11Z

[Term]
id: HP:0020146
name: Calcium carbonate crystalluria
synonym: "جير بولي كربونات الكالسيوم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "كربونات الكالسيوم في البول" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود بلورات كربونات الكالسيوم في البول.
def: "The presence of calcium carbonate crystals in the urine." [PMID:26509782, PMID:8671802]
comment: Calcium carbonate crystals usually appear as clumped granules.
is_a: HP:0020074 ! Crystalluria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
creation_date: 2019-07-05T19:11:59Z

[Term]
id: HP:0020147
name: 2-Methylbutyryl glycinuria
synonym: "2-ميثيلبوتيريل غليسين بولي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مركب عضوي غير طبيعي في البول" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
