[Term]
id: HP:0025081
name: Darier's sign
synonym: "علامة دارير" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "حكة وطفح عند فرك الجلد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: هو تغير جلدي يظهر عند فرك الآفة الجلدية في حالة الشرى الصباغي (UP)، حيث يبدأ المكان بالحكة ويصبح مرتفعًا ومحاطًا بالاحمرار. بخلاف الأشكال الأخرى لعلامات الجلد، تشير علامة دارير إلى تفاعل يتمركز في المناطق المتأثرة بالشرى الصباغي وتستثني الجلد السليم.
def: "A skin change elicited by briskly rubbing the skin lesion in urticaria pigmentosa (UP), whereby the area begins to itch and becomes raised and surrounded by erythema. Unlike other forms of dermatographism, Darier's sign refers to urtication that is limited to the UP involved areas and, as in this case, spares the skin unaffected by UP." [PMID:24701633]
is_a: HP:0001025 ! Urticaria
property_value: dc:date "2016-10-12T23:46:34Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025082
name: Abnormal cutaneous elastic fiber morphology
synonym: "شذوذ في شكل الألياف المرنة الجلدية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في الألياف المطاطية للجلد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أي شذوذ بنيوي في الألياف المرنة للجلد. الألياف المرنة هي الجزيئات الأساسية في المصفوفة الخلوية خارج الخلية التي تتكون من نواة من الإيلاستين محاطة بغلاف من الألياف الدقيقة الغنية بالفبرلين.
def: "Any structural anomaly of the elastic fibers of the skin. Elastic fibers are the essential extracellular matrix macromolecules comprising an elastin core surrounded by a mantle of fibrillin-rich microfibrils." [PMID:12082143, PMID:21738362]
comment: Elastic fibers help the skin return to its normal configuration after being stretched or deformed. The elastic fibers consist of two components: microfibrils and matrix elastin. The microfibrillar component amounts to only 15% of the elastic fiber, whereas the amorphous, electron-lucid elastin makes up 85% of the fiber. In light microscope sections that are routinely stained, elastic fibers are inconspicuous. With special elastic tissue stains, such as orcein or resorcin-fuchisin, or in plastic-embedded sections they are found entwined among the collagen bundles [PMID:21738362].
synonym: "Abnormal cutaneous elastic fibre morphology" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0011121 ! Abnormal skin morphology
property_value: dc:date "2016-10-15T12:16:20Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025083
name: Elevated dermal desmosine content
synonym: "زيادة محتوى الجلد من الديزموسين" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة مادة الديزموسين في الجلد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة في كمية الديزموسين المقاسة في الجلد. الديزموسين هو حمض أميني يربط بين الألياف المرنة ويتكون من بقايا الليزين.
def: "An increased amount of desmosine measure in the skin. Desmosine is a cross-linking amino acid formed from lysyl residues in elastin." [PMID:2307214]
comment: Disorders of elastosis may show an increased content of desmosines, whereas elastolytic disorders may show a reduced content of desmosine.
is_a: HP:0034924 ! Abnormal dermis morphology
property_value: dc:date "2016-10-15T13:13:02Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025084
name: Folliculitis
synonym: "التهاب الجريبات" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "التهاب بصيلات الشعر" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود خلايا التهاب داخل جدار وفتحات الجريب الشعري، مما يتسبب في ظهور البثور المرتبطة بالجريبات.
def: "Inflammatory cells within the wall and ostia of the hair follicle, creating a follicular-based pustule." []
comment: In contrast to folliculitis, perifolliculitis refers to inflammatory cells, usually lymphocytes, within the perifollicular tissues with focal extension into the adjacent reticular dermis. Folliculitis and perifolliculitis can occur independently or incombination owing to follicular disruption and irritation.
synonym: "Follicular pustule" EXACT []
synonym: "Hair follicle inflammation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011123 ! Inflammatory abnormality of the skin
property_value: dc:date "2016-10-15T13:35:26Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

