[Term]
id: HP:0025114
name: Hypergranulosis
synonym: "فرط التقرن الحبيبي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "سماكة في طبقة الجلد الحبيبية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة في سماكة الطبقة الحبيبية.
def: "Hypergranulosis is an increased thickness of the stratum granulosum." []
comment: Note that the epidermis includes five main layers: the stratum corneum, stratum lucidium, stratum granulosum, stratum spinosum, and stratum germinativum. This term refers to thickening that primarily affects the stratum granulosum.
is_a: HP:0011368 ! Epidermal thickening
property_value: dc:date "2016-11-01T01:48:14Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025115
name: Civatte bodies
synonym: "أجسام سيفاتي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "أجسام غير طبيعية في الجلد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أجسام مستديرة زجاجية الأيوزينوفيليك توجد غالبًا في المناطق تحت البشرة أو أحيانًا في البشرة نفسها. تظهر ككتل متجانسة زجاجية الأيوزينوفيليك على صبغة الهيماتوكسيلين والإيوسين وُجدت في الأجزاء الأعمق من البشرة/الظهارة وفي الأغلب في الأدمة/النسيج الضام. تُعرف أيضًا بأجسام كوليد أو أجسام زجاجية. يتراوح قطرها بين 10 و25 ميكرومتر وتقع في الأغلب داخل أو فوق التسلل الالتهابي.
def: "Eosinophilic hyaline ovoid bodies which are often found in the subepidermal papillary regions or sometimes in the epidermis. Civatte bodies (CBs) are seen as rounded, homogenous, eosinophilic masses on routine H and E staining lying in the deeper parts of epidermis/epithelium and more frequently in dermis/connective tissue. They are known as CBs (in epithelium/epidermis), colloid bodies, or hyaline bodies (in connective tissue). They are 10-25 micrometers in diameter and situated mostly within or above the inflammatory cell infiltrate. In lichen planus, the number of necrotic keratinocytes may be so large that they are seen lying in clusters in the uppermost dermis. These bodies show a positive periodic acid Schiff reaction and are diastase resistant" [PMID:23919028]
comment: The presence of numerous civatte bodies (CBs) in biopsies is a characteristic finding in skin lesions of patients with various dermatoses, particularly lichen planus (LP) and discoid lupus erythematosus (DLE). Achille Civatte (1877-1956) was a French dermatologist.
synonym: "Colloid bodies" EXACT []
synonym: "Colloid bodies of Civatte" EXACT []
synonym: "Cytoid bodies" EXACT []
synonym: "Hyaline bodies" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011124 ! Abnormal epidermal morphology
property_value: dc:date "2016-11-01T01:58:56Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025116
name: Fetal distress
synonym: "ضائقة الجنين" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مشاكل الجنين خلال الحمل" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: حالة داخل الرحم تتميز بقيم غير مثالية في معدل ضربات قلب الجنين أو تأكسج دم الجنين أو مؤشرات أخرى تدل على مشكلة في الجنين. تشمل علامات ضائقة الجنين التباطؤ المتغير المتكرر في معدل ضربات القلب، زيادة أو انخفاض معدل ضربات القلب، تباطؤ متأخر، أو انخفاض في النتيجة الحيوية.
def: "An intrauterine state characterized by suboptimal values in the fetal heart rate, oxygenation of fetal blood, or other parameters indicative of compromise of the fetus. Signs of fetal distress include repetitive variable decelerations, fetal tachycardia or bradycardia, late decelerations, or low biophysical profile." []
comment: Fetal distress in itself is a non-specific term as the various parameters characterizing the type and degree of distress are themselves ill defined. Nonethless the term is in broad clinical use and thus is included as an HPO term. It is preferable to annotate with more precise terms if possible.
synonym: "Foetal distress" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0034059 ! Abnormal fetal physiology
property_value: dc:date "2016-11-01T10:13:06Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025117
name: Rete ridge flattening
synonym: "تسطح النتوءات الجلدية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تسطح جلد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: النتوءات الجلدية هي الامتدادات الظهارية التي تمتد إلى النسيج الضام في كل من الجلد والأغشية المخاطية. يشير تسطح النتوءات الجلدية إلى فقدان هذه الامتدادات بحيث يكتسب الجلد مظهراً مسطحاً نسبياً.
def: "Rete pegs (or ridges) are the epithelial extensions that project into the underlying connective tissue in both skin and mucous membranes. Rete ridge flattening refers to the loss of these projections so that the skin epithelium acquires a relatively flat appearance." [PMID:20548894]
synonym: "Flattened rete pegs" EXACT []
synonym: "Flattened rete ridges" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034767 ! Abnormal rete ridge morphology
property_value: dc:date "2016-11-01T10:52:20Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

