synonym: "هزات شديدة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "هزات قوية مع الارتعاش" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: قشعريرة شديدة مع ارتعاش عنيف. النوبة تتمثل في اهتزاز أو ارتعاش مبالغ فيه يمكن أن يحدث مع حمى شديدة.
def: "Severe chills with violent shivering. A rigor is an episode of shaking or exaggerated shivering which can occur with a high fever." []
comment: A sudden attack of severe shivering accompanied by chills (a feeling of coldness) is called a rigor and may be associated with a marked rise in body temperature. Patients often describe rigors as an attack of uncontrollable shaking. Rigors are often a sign of infection, particularly bacterial infection.
synonym: "Rigours" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0025143 ! Chills
is_a: HP:0025144 ! Shivering
property_value: dc:date "2016-11-29T11:15:45Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025146
name: Foveal degeneration
synonym: "تنكس النقرة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تدهور في بقعة العين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مصطلح غير محدد يشير إلى فقدان تدريجي في الخلايا الصبغية الشبكية (RPE) و/أو الخلايا العصبية الحسية الشبكية في النقرة.
def: "A nonspecific term denoting progressive loss of the retinal pigment epithelium (RPE) and/or neurosensory retinal cells within the fovea." []
is_a: HP:0000493 ! Abnormal foveal morphology
is_a: HP:0000608 ! Macular degeneration
property_value: dc:date "2016-11-29T11:24:05Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025147
name: Beaten bronze macular sheen
synonym: "لمعان اللطخة الشبيه بالبرونزي المضروب" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "لمعان العيون غير طبيعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مظهر غير منتظم لون الرمادي لللطخة، والذي يُقال إنه يشبه الشكل المضروب للبرونز أو المعدن المضروب.
def: "An irregular grayish appearance of the macula, which is said to resemble beaten bronze or hammered metal." []
comment: This feature wasn initially described in Stargardt disease, but can also be observed in other macular dystrophies.
synonym: "Beaten metal macular appearance" EXACT []
synonym: "Beaten-bronze macular appearance" EXACT []
synonym: "Beaten-bronze macular sheen" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0008002 ! Abnormal macular pigmentation
property_value: dc:date "2016-11-29T11:37:39Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025148
name: Dark choroid
synonym: "المشيمية الداكنة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ظلام المشيمية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: اكتشاف بالتصوير الظليل الفلورسيني يظهر غياب الإشعاع الخلفي الطبيعي (مشيمية مظلمة).
def: "A fluorescein angiographic finding of absence of the normal background fluorescence (a dark choroid)." [PMID:27739528, PMID:7248243]
comment: The cause of dark choroid is thought to relate to the deposition of an abnormal material (lipofuscin) in the retinal pigment epithelial cells. Fluorescein angiography should no longer be used for diagnosis of Stargardt disease.
is_a: HP:0000610 ! Abnormal choroid morphology
is_a: HP:0030604 ! Abnormal fundus fluorescein angiography
property_value: dc:date "2016-11-29T11:49:16Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025149
name: Atrophic muscularis propria
synonym: "ضمور العضلية الخاصة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "فقدان نسيج العضلات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: فقدان جزئي أو كامل لنسيج العضلية الخاصة الذي كان موجودًا سابقاً. قد يتضمن الضمور تنكس فجوي بارز لخلايا العضلات، فقدان الألياف العضلية، وفي بعض الحالات تليف يشبه خلايا العسل.
def: "Partial or complete wasting (loss) of muscularois propria tissue that was once present. The atrophy may involve a marked vacuolar degeneration of myocytes, loss of muscle fibers and some cases a highly characteristic honeycomb fibrosis." [PMID:18329691]
synonym: "Autonomic visceral myopathy" RELATED []
synonym: "Degenerative enteric myopathy" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0030935 ! Abnormal intestinal smooth muscle morphology
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-03T14:04:10Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025150
name: Hypoganglionosis
synonym: "نقص العقد العصبية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "قلة العقد العصبية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: قلة وصغر العقد المعوية العضلية.
def: "Sparse and small myenteric ganglia" []
comment: Enteric ganglia are the nerve cell clusters (groups of nerve cell bodies) that are involved in mediating the muscular activity of the intestines.
is_a: HP:0004362 ! Abnormal enteric ganglion morphology
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-03T14:28:39Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025151
name: Ganglioneuromatosis
synonym: "التكاثف العصبي العقدي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة نمو الأعصاب في الأمعاء" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة في نمو الضفيرة تحت المخاطية والضفيرة المعوية العضلية تحتوي على عدد متزايد من خلايا العقد، والخلايا الدبقية والألياف العصبية.
def: "Hyperplastic submucosal and myenteric plexus containing an increased number of ganglion cells, glial cells and nerve fibers." [PMID:26361414]
is_a: HP:0004362 ! Abnormal enteric ganglion morphology
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-03T14:36:23Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025152
name: Poor visual behavior for age
synonym: "سلوك بصري ضعيف للعمر" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ضعف الرؤية وفقاً للعمر" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نقص في الاستجابة البصرية أو انخفاض في القدرات البصرية مما يشير إلى نقص في الاستجابة البصرية أو انخفاض في القدرات البصرية عند الرضع أو الأطفال الصغار حيث يفشل السلوك البصري في تحقيق معايير النمو الطبيعية.
def: "Lack of visual responsiveness or decrease in visual capabilities suggesting a lack of visual responsiveness or decrease in visual capabilities in an infant or young child in which visual behavior fails to meet normal developmental milestones." []
comment: A failure to meet age-related milestones in areas such as (i) focusing ability, (ii) eye coordinationg and tracking of objects in the visual field, (iii) depth perception, (iv) color perception, and (v) object and face recognition. These milestones are generally met in the first three months of life, and failure to meet them may indicate abnormal visual development or function.
synonym: "Abnormal visual behavior for age" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal visual behaviour for age" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Poor visual behavior for age" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000504 ! Abnormality of vision
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-03T21:34:47Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025153
name: Transient
synonym: "مؤقت" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "قصير الأمد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: قصير الأجل وليس دائم. ينطبق هذا المصطلح على شذوذ شكلي مؤقت وقصير المدة.
def: "Short-lived and not permanent. This term applies to a phenotypic abnormality that is temporary and of short duration." []
is_a: HP:0011008 ! Temporal pattern
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-03T22:19:26Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025154
name: Portosystemic collateral veins
synonym: "أوردة جانبية بابية جهازية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "الأوردة الجانبية الزائدة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود الأوردة الصفراوية التي تعمل كقناة جانبية للدورة الدموية الجهازية.
def: "Presence of biliary veins that serve as a collateral channel to the systemic circulation" []
comment: Venous blood returning from the small intestine, stomach, pancreas and spleen converges into the portal vein. The terminal branches of the hepatic portal vein and hepatic artery empty together and mix as they enter sinusoids in the liver. Conditions such as liver cirrhosis, in which scar tissue partially blocks the normal flow of blood, may increases the pressure in the portal vein (portal hypertension).When blood flow through a vessel or a vascular bed is obstructed due to occlusion, collateral pathways open up as blood bypasses the occlusion or obstruction, and this can lead to portosystemic collateral veins in the case of cirrhosis and some other hepatobiliary diseases.
synonym: "Collateral biliary circulation" EXACT []
synonym: "Collateral biliary veins" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012440 ! Abnormal biliary tract morphology
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-03T22:24:40Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025155
name: Abnormal hepatobiliary system physiology
synonym: "خلل فسيولوجيا الجهاز الكبدي الصفراوي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مشاكل في وظيفة الكبد والقنوات الصفراوية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل وظيفي في الجهاز الكبدي الصفراوي.
def: "A functional anomaly of the hepatobiliary system" []
is_a: HP:0025032 ! Abnormality of digestive system physiology
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-04T12:05:04Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025156
name: Dependency on intravenous nutrition
synonym: "الاعتماد على التغذية الوريدية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "حاجة التغذية عن طريق الوريد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدم القدرة على التوقف عن التغذية الوريدية (التغذية بالحقن)، ومن خلال تتبع حالة الترطيب (إنتاج البول، نيتروجين البول، الكرياتينين، تركيز الصوديوم في البول)، القدرة على الحفاظ على الوزن، خروج البراز، وحالة الإلكتروليتات في الدم.
def: "Inability to be weaned from intravenous (parenteral) nutrition, as judged by the hydration status (urine output, blood urea nitrogen, creatinine, urine sodium concentration), ability to maintain weight, stool output, and serum electrolyte status." [PMID:16770168]
comment: Total parenteral nutrition (TPN) refers to the application of an intravenous nutritional solution in individuals with gastrointestinal disorders that prevent them from absorbing a sufficient amount of nutrients from the gut to maintain health. The solution contains protein, carbohydrates (in the form of glucose), glucose, fat, vitamins, and minerals. Dependency on TPN is essentially a manifestation of the continued severity of a gastrointestinal disorder.
synonym: "Dependency on IV nutrition" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0025032 ! Abnormality of digestive system physiology
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-04T12:14:59Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025157
name: Increased urinary sedoheptulose
synonym: "زيادة السيديوهيبتولوز في البول" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "سكر في البول" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة تركيز مادة السيديوهيبتولوز في البول. السيديوهيبتولوز هو سكر أحادي يحتوي على سبعة ذرات كربون ومجموعة كيتون وظيفية.
def: "An increased concentration of sedoheptulose in the urine. Sedoheptulose is a monosaccharide with seven carbon atoms and a ketone functional group." []
is_a: HP:0031979 ! Abnormal urine carbohydrate level
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-04T12:36:02Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

