[Term]
id: HP:0025240
name: Preretinal hemorrhage
synonym: "نزيف تحت الشبكية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نزيف أمام الشبكية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تراكم الدم بين الشبكية والهالويد الخلفي المنفصل، أو في تجويف الجسم الزجاجي. يتميز نزيف تحت الهالويد عادة بكتلة دموية دائرية أو على شكل جرس أسفل الغشاء المحدود الداخلي بالقرب من منطقة البقعة المركزية.
alt_id: HP:0025239
alt_id: HP:0031804
def: "An accumulation of blood that is located between the retina and the detached posterior hyaloid, or in the vitreous cavity. Subhyaloid premacular hemorrhage is typically characterized by a circumscribed, round or dumb-bell shaped, bright red mound of blood beneath the internal limiting membrane (ILM) or between the ILM and hyaloid face, in or near to the central macular area." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123, PMID:27090882]
comment: Clinically speaking, distinguishing between preretinal and subhyaloid hemorrhages is difficult. Therefore, clinicians often use the terms interchangeably. A boat-shaped appearance may be observed, because the blood accumulates within loosely adherent tissue of the superficial retina and can spread and settle inferiorly with gravity. A sharp demarcation line is usually evident. Not infrequently, a subhyaloid hemorrhage is also associated with a sub-ILM hemorrhage.
synonym: "Premacular hemorrhage" NARROW []
synonym: "Preretinal haeme" EXACT []
synonym: "Preretinal haemorrhage" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Preretinal heme" EXACT []
synonym: "Subhyaloid haemorrhage" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Subhyaloid heme" EXACT []
synonym: "Subhyaloid hemorrhage" NARROW []
is_a: HP:0031803 ! Fundus hemorrhage
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-17T00:54:15Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025241
name: Flame-shaped retinal hemorrhage
synonym: "نزيف شبكي على شكل لهب" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نزيف الشبكية بشكل اللهب" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من النزيف الشبكي يوجد في طبقة الألياف العصبية من الشبكية ويتميز بشكل اللهب الناتج عن القيود الهيكلية لطبقة الألياف العصبية.
def: "A type of retinal hemorrhage that is located within the nerve fiber layer (NFL) of the retina and that exhibits a characteristic flame shape which results from constraints by the structure of the NFL (axons of the ganglion cells)." []
comment: Flame-shaped hemorrhages are typically located in the posterior pole and tend to resolve within around six weeks. THeir pathophysiology is thought to reflect ischemic leakage from arterioles or veins that are ischemic or, in the case of veins, under high pressure.
synonym: "Feathered retinal heme" EXACT []
synonym: "Flame-shaped retinal haemorrhage" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Linear retina heme" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031805 ! Intraretinal hemorrhage
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-17T01:14:14Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025242
name: Dot-and-blot retinal hemorrhage
synonym: "نزيف شبكي نقطي وبقعي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نزيف نقطي في الشبكية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تراكم الدم الموجود في الطبقات النووية الداخلية والطبقات الخارجية البكسيفية للشبكية، ويكون على شكل نقاط أو بقع. الشكل ناتج عن الضغط الداخلي للشبكية الذي يقيِّد النزيف في مكان محدد.
def: "Accumulation of blood located in the retina's inner nuclear and outer plexiform layers, and having a dot-like or blot-like shape. THe shape results from intraretinal compression, restricting the hemorrhages within a specific location." []
comment: Dot-ant-blot Intraretinal hemorrhages take longer to resolve than superficial hemorrhages because they're deeper than flame-shaped hemorrhages.
synonym: "Dot-and-blot retinal haemorrhage" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Round retinal heme" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031805 ! Intraretinal hemorrhage
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-17T01:25:52Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025243
name: Subretinal hemorrhage
synonym: "نزيف تحت الشبكية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نزيف أسفل الشبكية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تراكم الدم الموجود تحت الشبكية العصبية في المساحة بين الشبكية العصبية وظهارة الصباغ الشبكية.
def: "Accumulation of blood located beneath the neurosensory retina in the space between the neurosensory retina and the retinal pigment epithelium." []
comment: Subretinal hemorrhages are located deep in the retina, displaying a dark coloration with the retinal vessels clearly visible above. Subretinal hemorrhages tend not to be well delineated because of the lack of firm attachments between the neurosensory retina and the retinal pigment epithelium, allowing the blood to spread.
synonym: "Subretinal haemorrhage" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Subretinal heme" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000573 ! Retinal hemorrhage
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-17T01:29:29Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025244
name: Sub-retinal pigment epithelium haemorrhage
synonym: "نزف تحت ظهارة الصبغيات الشبكية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نزف تحت الشبكية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تراكم الدم الموجود بين ظهارة الصبغيات الشبكية والغشاء الزجاجي.
def: "An accumulation of blood located between the retinal pigment epithelium (RPE) and Bruch membrane." []
comment: This can be associated with 'polypoidal lesions', neovascularization, or trauma.
synonym: "Sub-RPE hemorrhage" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Subretinal pigment epithelium haemorrhage" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Subretinal pigment epithelium hemorrhage" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000573 ! Retinal hemorrhage
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-17T01:39:54Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025245
name: Cutaneous cyst
synonym: "كيس جلدي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: كتلة جوفاء موجودة في الجلد محاطة بجدار مبطن بالظهارة وتُحدد بوضوح عن النسيج المحيط. يُقال عن الأكياس أنها تشبه الحويصلات وقد تحتوي على سائل مصلي أو مادة شبه صلبة.
def: "A hollow mass located in the skin that is surrounded by an epithelium-lined wall and is well demarcated from the adjacent tissue. Cysts are often said to be sac-like and may contain serous liquid or semisolid material." []
comment: In contrast to cysts, vesicles, pustules and bullae do not have a complete epithelial lining and are therefore less well demarcated.
synonym: "Skin cyst" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0011355 ! Localized skin lesion
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-17T13:11:37Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025246
name: Trichilemmal cyst
synonym: "كيس الشعر" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: كيس جلدي أو تحت جلدي مستدير وغير مؤلم ولكنه صلب قليلاً وقابل للانضغاط، يتراوح قطره بين 0.5 و5 سم. الأكياس الشعرية مكتسبة وليست خلقية، وعادة ما تظهر على فروة الرأس أكثر من الوجه، وتكون داخل الأدمة أكثر من تحت الجلد.
def: "Nontender, round and firm, but slightly compressible, intradermal or subcutaneous cyst measuring 0.5-5 cm in diameter. Trichilemmal cysts are acquired rather than congenital, and tend to appear on the scalp rather than the face, and to be intradermal rather than subcutaneous." []
comment: Epidermal cysts and trichilemmal cysts are clinically indistinguishable. The wall of the epidermal cyst conserves the epidermal layers, but the wall of the trichilemmal cysts, which arise from the external root sheath, shows palisading of unlayered epithelial cells. Homogeneous horny material that is further degraded to fat and cholesterol forms within both types of cysts.
synonym: "Pilar cyst" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025245 ! Cutaneous cyst
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-17T13:45:04Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025247
name: Dermoid cyst
synonym: "كيس جلدي أدموي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "كيس جلدي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: كيس تحت الجلد الخلقي ينتج عن انحباس الجلد على طول خطوط الاندماج الجنيني. على عكس الأكياس الظهارية، تحتوي الأكياس الجلدية على هياكل ملحقة مثل الشعر والغدد الدهنية والغدد العرقية والغدد العرقية المفترزة. تكون الأكياس الجلدية موجودة عند الولادة، صلبة، وعميقة، وتكون في صورة عقد تحت جلدية غير مؤلمة. غالباً ما توجد في الرأس والرقبة ونادراً في منطقة العجان. تتطور الأكياس الجلدية ببطء ويمكن أن تنمو إلى حجم بين 1 إلى 4 سم.
def: "A congenital subcutaneous cyst that arises from entrapment of skin along the lines of embryonic fusion. In contrast to epidermal cysts, dermoid cysts tend to contain various adnexal structures such as hair, sebaceous, eccrine or apocrine glands. Dermoid cysts are present at birth, and are indolent, firm, deep, subcutaneous nodules. They are often located on the head and neck, and rarely in the anogenital area. Dermoid cysts are slowly progressive and can grow to a size of 1 to 4 cm." []
comment: Hair protruding from a dermoid cyst punctum is pathognomic for dermoid cysts.
is_a: HP:0025245 ! Cutaneous cyst
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-17T13:49:23Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025248
name: Eruptive vellus hair cyst
synonym: "كيس الشعر الزغبي الناشئ" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "كيس زغبي صغير" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: كيس جلدي صغير (قطره واحد إلى اثنين مليمتر) وغير مؤلم، يظهر على هيئة حطاطة جريبية غالباً ما تكون بلون الجلد ولكن قد تظهر بظل مائل إلى الأحمر أو البني.
def: "A cutaneous cyst that is small (one or two millimeters in diameter) and painless, presenting as a follicular papule that usually is skin colored but may have a reddish or brownish tinge." []
comment: Eruptive vellus hair cysts result from occlusion and cystic dilation of vellus hair follicles.
is_a: HP:0025245 ! Cutaneous cyst
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-17T13:52:25Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025249
name: Comedo
synonym: "كوميدو" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "رؤوس سوداء" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: سويداء دهنية جلدية مسدودة، وهو غدة جلدية تفرز الزهم (عادة في بصيلة الشعر).
def: "A clogged cutaneous sebaceous follicle, which is a cutaneous gland that secretes sebum (usually into a hair follicle)." []
