[Term]
id: HP:0025314
name: Choroidal nevus
synonym: "وحمة عنبية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وحمة في الجزء الخلفي من العين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: آفة صبغية حميدة، مسطحة أو مرتفعة قليلاً في المشيمية الخلفية، مع حدود واضحة. تميل إلى الثبات في الحجم وقد تظهر عليها دروسين او ضمور او تضخم في الصبغة الشبكية أو تحول ليفي.
def: "A benign, flat or slightly elevated melanocytic lesions of the posterior uvea with clearly defined margins. Choroidal nevi tend to remain stable in size, and to display features such as overlying drusen as well as retinal pigment epithelial atrophy, hyperplasia or fibrous metaplasia." []
comment: A choroidal nevus can evolve towards choroidal melanoma. Choroidal nevi can be melanotic or amelanotic. Occasionally, they are associated with hyperpigmentation of extra ocular structures such as nevus of Ota or ocular melanosis.
is_a: HP:0000610 ! Abnormal choroid morphology
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-21T01:54:28Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025315
name: Exacerbated by head trauma
synonym: "مفاقمة بسبب إصابة في الرأس" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "يزداد سوءًا بعد إصابة الرأس" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ينطبق على علامة أو عرض يزداد سوءاً أو تفاقماً بسبب إصابة في الرأس.
def: "Applies to a sign or symptom that is worsened, aggravated, or exacerbated by head trauma." []
comment: Childhood ataxia with central nervous system hypomyelination/vanishing white matter disease is an autosomal recessive disorder characterized by ataxia, spasticity, and variable optic atrophy. Chronic progressive decline can be exacerbated by rapid deterioration during febrile illnesses or following head trauma.
is_a: HP:0025285 ! Aggravated by
property_value: dc:date "2016-12-21T02:22:58Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025317
name: Cubitus varus
synonym: "كوع مائل للداخل" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تشوه الكوع" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تشوه في الكوع حيث يوجد انحراف للساعد نحو خط منتصف الجسم.
def: "A deformity of the elbow in which there is a deviation of the forearm toward the midline of the body." []
comment: Normally, if the arm is held in full extension, the forearm is aligned in valgus with respect to the arm. A decrease in valgus with neutral alignment (loss of angulation) is called cubitus rectus, and a further decreases is called varus. Cubitus varus may be congenital (often progressive), or may be a complication of humerus fracture, trochlear osteonecrosis, and malunited intercondylar fracture. Radiographically, the metaphyseo-diaphyseal angle is normally 90 degrees. With cubitus varus, the angle is larger, with cubitus valgus, the angle is smaller.
is_a: HP:0020300 ! Abnormal elbow morphology
property_value: dc:date "2017-01-13T13:20:56Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0025318
name: Ovarian carcinoma
synonym: "سرطان المبيض" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ورم خبيث ينشأ من سطح ظهارة المبيض.
def: "A malignant neoplasm originating from the surface ovarian epithelium." []
synonym: "Ovarian epithelial cancer" EXACT []
xref: NCIT:C4908
is_a: HP:0100615 ! Ovarian neoplasm
property_value: dc:date "2017-01-25T14:30:43Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

