[Term]
id: HP:0025434
name: Reduced circulating CH50 activity
synonym: "انخفاض نشاط CH50 الدوري" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انخفاض نشاط مكمل الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انخفاض في نشاط المسار المكمل التقليدي، كما يُقاس بواسطة اختبار نشاط المكمل الانحلالي بنسبة 50٪ (CH50) في مصل الدم.
alt_id: HP:0031906
def: "A diminished activity of the classical complement pathway as measured by the assay for 50% haemolytic complement (CH50) activity of serum." [PMID:20351687]
comment: Individual complement components can be quantified however this does not provide any information as to the activity of the pathway. The CH50 is a screening assay for the activation of the classical complement pathway and it is sensitive to the reduction, absence and/or inactivity of any component of the pathway. The CH50 tests the functional capability of serum complement components of the classical pathway to lyse sheep red blood cells (SRBC) pre-coated with rabbit anti-sheep red blood cell antibody (haemolysin). When antibody-coated SRBC are incubated with test serum, the classical pathway of complement is activated and haemolysis results. If a complement component is absent, the CH50 level will be zero; if one or more components of the classical pathway are decreased, the CH50 will be decreased.
synonym: "Decreased total hemolytic complement activity" EXACT []
synonym: "Reduced CH50" EXACT []
synonym: "Reduced circulating 50% hemolytic complement (CH50) activity" EXACT []
synonym: "Reduced hemolytic complement activity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031904 ! Abnormal total hemolytic complement activity
property_value: dc:date "2017-04-23T16:53:06Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

