is_a: HP:0003457 ! EMG abnormality

[Term]
id: HP:0030001
name: Lagophthalmos
synonym: "العين الأرنبية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدم القدرة على غلق الجفون" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: حالة لا تغلق فيها الجفون ولا تغطي العين بالكامل.
def: "A condition in which the eyelids do not close to cover the eye completely." [PMID:20590416]
comment: Some common causes of lagophthalmos are Bell's palsy and other types of facial paralysis, stroke, infection, and trauma. The inability to blink and effectively close the eyes leads to corneal exposure and excessive evaporation of the tear film. The main purpose when treating lagophthalmos is to prevent exposure keratitis and reestablish eyelid function. {xref="PMID:20590416"}
synonym: "Eyelids stay open" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Inability to close the eyelids" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
xref: UMLS:C4022680
is_a: HP:0000492 ! Abnormal eyelid morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030002
name: Nocturnal lagophthalmos
synonym: "العين الأرنبية الليلية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدم القدرة على غلق الجفون أثناء النوم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدم القدرة على غلق الجفون أثناء النوم.
def: "The inability to close the eyelids during sleep." [PMID:16671223]
comment: Lagophthalmos is associated with exposure keratopathy, poor sleep, and persistent exposure-related symptoms. There are a variety of causes of lagophthalmos, grouped as proptosis/eye exposure etiologies and palpebral insufficiency etiologies. {xref="PMID:16671223"}
synonym: "Eyelids stay open at night" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Inability to close the eyelids at night" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:417740005
xref: UMLS:C1563118
is_a: HP:0030001 ! Lagophthalmos

[Term]
id: HP:0030003
name: Paralytic lagophthalmos
synonym: "العين الأرنبية الشللية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "المشكلة بسبب شلل الوجه" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من العين الأرنبية يحدث بسبب شلل العصب الوجهي.
def: "A type of lagophthalmos that occurs in association with facial nerve palsy." [PMID:24618488]
comment: Patients with facial nerve palsy have a characteristic facial asymmetry and drooping of the angle of mouth. The temporal and zygomatic branches of facial nerve supply the forehead and eyelid muscles. Their involvement in a disease leads to paralysis of orbicularis oculi muscle resulting in lagophthalmos and ectropion. {xref="PMID:24618488"}
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:59890007
xref: UMLS:C0155197
is_a: HP:0030001 ! Lagophthalmos

[Term]
id: HP:0030004
name: Cicatricial lagophthalmos
synonym: "العين الأرنبية التندبية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مشكلة بسبب ندبات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من العين الأرنبية يحدث بعد التعرض لصدمة أو جراحة.
def: "A type of lagophthalmos that occurs following trauma or surgery." []
synonym: "Eyelids stay open due to scarring" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Inability to close the eyelids due to scarring" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:9042000
xref: UMLS:C0155199
is_a: HP:0030001 ! Lagophthalmos

[Term]
id: HP:0030005
name: Capillary leak
synonym: "تسرب الشعيرات" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تسرب السوائل من الأوعية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ظاهرة حادة تتميز بانخفاض ضغط الدم وتورم الجسم بسبب فقدان حجم البلازما إلى الأنسجة المحيطية، مع دليل على نقص حجم البلازما (زيادة تركيز الدم) وفقدان البروتين من الفضاء الوعائي (نقص الألبومين في الدم) أثناء النوبات الحادة.
def: "An acute phenomenon characterized by hypotension and anasarca due to the loss of plasma volume into peripheral tissues, with evidence of decreased plasma volume (hemoconcentration) and protein loss from the intravascular space (hypoalbuminemia) during acute episodes." [PMID:24467750, PMID:24808988]
synonym: "Increased capillary permeability" EXACT []
synonym: "Systemic capillary leak syndrome" RELATED []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:1608005
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:87730004
xref: UMLS:C0343084
xref: UMLS:C1382398
is_a: HP:0025018 ! Abnormal capillary physiology

[Term]
id: HP:0030006
name: Single fiber EMG abnormality
synonym: "شذوذ تخطيط كهربية العضلات عند الألياف الفردية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل تخطيط كهربية العضلات عند الألياف الفردية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ في تسجيل تخطيط كهربية العضلات للألياف الفردية، وهي تقنية تسمح بتحديد الجهدات الكهربائية من الألياف العضلية الفردية.
def: "Abnormality in single fiber EMG recording, a technique that allows identification of action potentials (APs) from individual muscle fibers." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:21654930]
synonym: "Single fibre EMG abnormality" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: UMLS:C4022679
is_a: HP:0003457 ! EMG abnormality

[Term]
id: HP:0030007
name: EMG: positive sharp waves
synonym: "EMG: موجات حادة موجبة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "موجات غير طبيعية في اختبار العضلات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: هذه هي الإجراءات الكهربائية ذاتية التحفيز الناتجة عن حركة الإبرة في ألياف عضلية مصابة. يتم الانتشار إلى طرف الإبرة ولكن لا يتجاوزه، مما يمنع عرض الانحراف السلبي لشكل الموجات.
def: "These are spontaneous firing action potentials stimulated by needle movement of an injured muscle fiber. There is propagation to, but not past, the needle tip. This inhibits the display of the negative deflection of the waveform." [PMID:15961866]
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:251527008
xref: UMLS:C0429349
is_a: HP:0003482 ! EMG: axonal abnormality

