[Term]
id: HP:0030438
name: Anal canal squamous cell carcinoma
synonym: "سرطان الخلايا الحرشفية في القناة الشرجية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "سرطان القناة الشرجية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: سرطان خلية حرشفية ينشأ في قناة الشرج.
def: "A squamous cell carcinoma that originates in the anal canal." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22379406]
comment: Patients typically present with bright red bleeding, pain, and/or a palpable mass. When a clinically suspicious lesion is identified, diagnosis relies on cytologic or histologic confirmation.
xref: UMLS:C1332262
is_a: HP:0030437 ! Anal canal neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030439
name: Anal canal adenocarcinoma
synonym: "سرطان الغدية في القناة الشرجية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "سرطان في القناة الشرجية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: هو ورم غدي سرطاني ينشأ في القناة الشرجية.
def: "An adenoma carcinoma that originates in the anal canal." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22379406]
comment: Differentiating true anal canal adenocarcinoma from low rectal adenocarcinoma can be challenging. Most anal canal adenocarcinomas originate from anal glands, but cases developing in chronic tracts from fistula in ano are described. Multiple factors, including infection with HPV and HIV, history of receptive anal intercourse, smoking, and immunosuppression have been identified as risk factors. Clinical features include anal pain, induration of the anal canal, or abscess formation and a palpable lump.
xref: NCIT:C2852
xref: UMLS:C1332259
is_a: HP:0030437 ! Anal canal neoplasm
is_a: HP:0040275 ! Adenocarcinoma of the large intestine

[Term]
id: HP:0030440
name: Anal margin neoplasm
synonym: "ورم هامش الشرج" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ورم في حافة الشرج" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ورم يحدث في حافة الشرج.
def: "A tumor of the anal margin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22379406]
comment: The anal canal is defined as the caudal part of the large intestine extending from the anorectal ring to the anal verge and is about 3 to 5 cm in length. Outside of the anal verge lies the anal margin, also referred to as the perianal skin, which commonly encompasses a radius of 5 cm. The anal verge can be identified visually as the part of the anal canal remaining closed when the buttocks are gently retracted. The upper anal canal is lined by columnar tissue that transitions into squamous epithelium at the dentate line. The dentate line, identified by the termination of the anal columns, lies 1 to 2 cm above the anal verge.
xref: UMLS:C2064234
is_a: HP:0007378 ! Neoplasm of the gastrointestinal tract

[Term]
id: HP:0030441
name: Anal margin Paget's disease
synonym: "داء باغيت هامش الشرج" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مرض باغيت في حافة الشرج" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: هو سرطان غدي داخل الظهارة ينشأ في هامش الشرج ويتميز بوجود خلايا باغيت النموذجية، التي تظهر كخلايا كبيرة مدورة ومفرغة.
def: "An intraepithelial adenocarcinoma originating in the anal margin and characterized by presence of typical Paget's cells, appearing as large rounded vacuolated cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22379406]
comment: Macroscopically, anal margin Paget's disease presents as an erythematous and eczematous rash similar to benign skin conditions or other perianal diseases such as Bowen's disease, hydradenitis suppurativa, pruritus ani, or Crohn's disease.
xref: UMLS:C1332270
is_a: HP:0030440 ! Anal margin neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030442
name: Anal margin squamous cell carcinoma
synonym: "سرطان الخلايا الحرشفية في هامش الشرج" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "سرطان في حافة الشرج" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: هو سرطان الخلايا الحرشفية الذي ينشأ في جلد حافة الشرج.
def: "A squamous cell carcinoma that originates in the skin of the anal margin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22379406]
comment: Clinical presentations include pain, bleeding, palpable lump, and discharge. Typically, SCC of the anal margin appears as an ulcerated lesion with rolled everted edges. A significant number of patients are misdiagnosed with an anal fissure, fistula, eczema, or hemorrhoids; therefore a biopsy is recommended for any persistent anal margin lesion not responding to conservative therapy.
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:255084004
xref: UMLS:C1412037
is_a: HP:0030440 ! Anal margin neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030443
name: Anal margin basal cell carcinoma
synonym: "سرطان خلايا القاعدة في هامش الشرج" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "سرطان في حافة الشرج" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: هو سرطان خلايا القاعدة الذي ينشأ في هامش الشرج.
def: "A basal cell carcinoma that originates in the anal margin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
