is_a: HP:0000591 ! Abnormal sclera morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030824
name: Mizuo phenomenon
synonym: "ظاهرة ميتسو" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تغير لون قاع العين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تغير في لون قاع العين من الأحمر في حالة التكيف مع الظلام إلى اللون الذهبي مباشرة أو بعد فترة قصيرة من التعرض للضوء. وقد وُصف لون منعكس قاع العين في حالة التكيف مع الضوء بأنه أصفر ذهبي، رمادي أبيض، وأصفر أبيض. ويمكن أن يظهر هذا الانعكاس إما متجانسًا أو في خطوط بقاع العين. وتظهر الأوعية الشبكية بارزة على خلفية لامعة. يؤدي التكيف مع الظلام إلى زوال تغير اللون غير المعتاد لقاع العين.
def: "Change in the color of the fundus from red in the dark-adapted state to golden immediately or shortly after the onset of the light. The color of the fundus reflex in the light adapted state has also been described as golden-yellow, gray-white, and yellow-white. This reflex can appear either homogeneous or in streaks in the fundus. The retinal vessels appear to be protruding in contrast to the radiant background. Dark adaptation leads to disappearance of the unusual fundus coloration [Digital Journal of Ophthalmology 2008; Volume 14, Number 14]." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Mizuo-Nakamura phenomenon" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4280748
is_a: HP:0001098 ! Abnormal fundus morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030825
name: Absent foveal reflex
synonym: "غياب انعكاس النقرة المركزية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "غياب اللمعة في النقرة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدم وجود اللمعان الطبيعي للنقرة المركزية، والتي تُرى عادةً كنقطة ضوء لامعة تتحرك جانبيًا أو لأعلى ولأسفل استجابةً لحركة منظار العين.
def: "Absent reflectivity of the fovea, which normally is a bright pinpoint of light that is observed to move sideways or up and down in response to movement of the opthalmoscope." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:27491360]
comment: Absence of the foveal reflex can occur with macular edema, central serous retinopathy, or other macular abnormalities such as macular dystrophy. The macular reflex is often less pronounced in adults than in children, and may be absent in otherwise normal eyes of older individuals.
synonym: "Foveal reflex absent" EXACT []
synonym: "Loss of foveal reflex" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:247144003
xref: UMLS:C0423420
is_a: HP:0000493 ! Abnormal foveal morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030826
name: Eyelid fasciculation
synonym: "ارتجاف الجفن" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ارتعاش الجفن" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تقلصات عضلية صغيرة ومتكررة في الجفون تسبب ظهورها وكأنها ترتجف.
def: "Tiny, repetitive muscle contractions in the eyelids, causing the appearance of twitching." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Eyelid fluttering" EXACT []
synonym: "Fasciculation of the eyelid" EXACT []
synonym: "Muscle twitches in eye lid" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Muscle twitches in eyelid" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Twitching around eyes" EXACT layperson []
xref: UMLS:C4280682
is_a: HP:0031785 ! Abnormal eyelid movement

[Term]
id: HP:0030828
name: Wheezing
synonym: "أزيز" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "صوت أزيز" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: صوت صفير حاد يرتبط بالتنفس الشاق.
def: "A high-pitched whistling sound associated with labored breathing." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:26229557]
comment: Wheezes and rhonchi are continuous musical lung sounds. The American Thoracic Society (ATS) Committee on pulmonary nomenclature defines wheezes as high-pitched continuous sounds with a dominant frequency of 400 Hz or more, and rhonchi as low-pitched continuous musical sounds with a dominant frequency of about 200 Hz or less
synonym: "Wheezing" EXACT layperson []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:56018004
xref: UMLS:C0043144
is_a: HP:0030829 ! Abnormal breath sound

[Term]
id: HP:0030829
name: Abnormal breath sound
synonym: "صوت تنفس غير طبيعي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "صوت التنفس غير طبيعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: صوت غير طبيعي (غير معتاد) يتم إنتاجه أثناء عملية التنفس.
def: "An anomalous (adventitious) sound produced by the breathing process." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Abnormal lung auscultation finding" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:301273002
xref: UMLS:C0231856
is_a: HP:0002795 ! Abnormal respiratory system physiology

[Term]
id: HP:0030830
name: Crackles
synonym: "طقطقات" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "صوت طقطقة التنفس" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الصوت الطقطقي هو أصوات رئوية غير مستمرة وانفجارية وغير موسيقية تُسمع عادةً أثناء الشهيق وأحيانًا أثناء الزفير. وتُصنّف الطقطقات عادةً على أنها طقطقات دقيقة وخشنة بناءً على مدتها وحدتها وارتفاعها وتوفيرها وتوقيتها في دورة التنفس وعلاقتها بالسعال أو تغيير وضع الجسم.
def: "Crackles are discontinuous, explosive, and nonmusical adventitious lung sounds normally heard in inspiration and sometimes during expiration. Crackles are usually classified as fine and coarse crackles based on their duration, loudness, pitch, timing in the respiratory cycle, and relationship to coughing and changing body position." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754, PMID:26229557]
comment: Rales are fine, discontinuous crackles that can sound like cellophane being crumpled or velcro being pulled apart. They may be heard with a stethoscope when listening over lungs containing more than the normal amount of fluid secretiions.
synonym: "Crepitations" EXACT []
synonym: "Rales" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:48409008
xref: UMLS:C0034642
is_a: HP:0030829 ! Abnormal breath sound

[Term]
id: HP:0030831
name: Rhonchi
synonym: "رونكاي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "صوت خرخرة التنفس" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أصوات تنفس غير طبيعية تتميز بصوت منخفض النبرة يشبه الشخير أو الخشخشة.
def: "Abnormal breath sounds characterized by low-pitched, snoring or rattle-like sounds." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754, PMID:26229557]
comment: Wheezes and rhonchi are continuous musical lung sounds. The American Thoracic Society (ATS) Committee on pulmonary nomenclature defines wheezes as high-pitched continuous sounds with a dominant frequency of 400 Hz or more, and rhonchi as low-pitched continuous musical sounds with a dominant frequency of about 200 Hz or less.
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:24612001
xref: UMLS:C0035508
is_a: HP:0030829 ! Abnormal breath sound

