[Term]
id: HP:0030860
name: Abnormal CSF amyloid concentration
synonym: "خلل تركيز الأميلويد في السائل النخاعي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في مستوى الأميلويد في السائل النخاعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل في تركيز الأميلويد في السائل النخاعي.
def: "Abnormal concentration of amyloid in the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF)." []
comment: In Alzheimer disease, histopathology typically reveals extracellular accumulations of amyloid beta (Abeta) in senile plaques and intracellular neurofibrillary tangles of hyperphosphorylated tau (P-tau). A[beta]42 is the 42 amino acid isoform of amyloid beta. Using positron emission tomography several studies found an inverse correlation between brain amyloid load and CSF A[beta]42.
synonym: "Abnormal CSF A[beta]42 level" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Abnormal CSF amyloid level" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C4280740
