property_value: dc:date "2017-01-13T21:44:36Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0030950
name: Pulmonary venous hypertension
synonym: "ارتفاع ضغط الأوردة الرئوية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ارتفاع ضغط الدم في الأوردة الرئوية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة غير طبيعية في الضغط في الأوردة الرئوية، عادة نتيجة لارتفاع ضغط الأذين الأيسر.
def: "An abnormal increase in pressure in the pulmonary veins, usually as a result of left atrial hypertension." []
comment: Common causes of pulmonary venous hypertension are obstruction to left ventricular (LV) inflow, LV systolic dysfunction, severe mitral regurgitation, and acute pulmonary and systemic volume overload. As the pulmonary venous pressure nears 22 mm Hg, interstitial pulmonmary edema may develop. As it reaches 25 mm Hg, alveolar edema may ensue.
is_a: HP:0030875 ! Abnormality of pulmonary circulation
property_value: dc:date "2017-01-13T21:56:41Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0030951
name: Skeletal muscle fibrosis
synonym: "تليف العضلات الهيكلية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تليف في العضلات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تكون مفرط للأشرطة الليفية النسيجية في النسيج العضلي.
def: "Excessive formation of fibrous bands of scar tissue in between muscle fibers." [PMID:21798099]
comment: Pathophysiologic fibrosis, which is essentially an excessive accumulation of extracellular matrix components, particularly collagen, is the end result of a cascade of events proceeding from tissue injury via inflammation, and resulting in permanent scar formation. Fibrosis can impair tissue function. In skeletal muscle, fibrosis is most often associated with the muscular dystrophies.
synonym: "Muscle biopsy: fibrosis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011805 ! Abnormal skeletal muscle morphology
property_value: dc:date "2017-01-13T22:27:25Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0030952
name: Birdshot choroidal lesions
synonym: "آفات الكورويد الطائر" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تغيرات في الكورويد مرتبطة بالكورويد الطائر" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: آفات متعددة ذات لون أصفر كريمي وفقدان صبغة تقع عادة على مستوى الجزء الخارجي من الكورويد. تتراوح حجمها بين 50 و1500 ميكرومتر وتتميز بتوزيع شعاعي فيزائلي في منطقة ما بعد الاستواء.
def: "Multiple cream-yellow colored hypopigmented lesions typically located at the level of the outer choroid. They are between 50 and 1,500 micrometers in size with a characteristic nasal, radial distribution in the postequatorial fundus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9114-8737, PMID:25667738, PMID:33845003]
comment: Birdshot choroidal lesions are associated with Birdshot retinochoroidopathy.
synonym: "Birdshot choroidal lesions" EXACT []
synonym: "Birdshot laesions" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Birdshot lesions" EXACT []
synonym: "Birdshot retinochoroidopathy" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000610 ! Abnormal choroid morphology
property_value: dc:date "2017-01-13T22:33:03Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

