[Term]
id: HP:0031160
name: Myelokathexis
synonym: "ميليكاثيكسيس" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مشاكل في نضوج كريات الدم البيضاء" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ضعف خروج الخلايا الناضجة من النخاع العظمي مما يسبب نقص العدلات.
def: "Impaired egress of mature neutrophils from bone marrow causing neutropenia." [PMID:10607719, PMID:25662009]
comment: The word myelo-kathexis is derived from the Greek words for marrow (myelo) retention (kathexis). Unlike other forms of severe neutropenia, myelokathexis is characterized by granulocytic hyperplasia in the bone marrow, which contains neutrophils with cytoplasmic vacuoles, nuclear hypersegmentation, and pyknotic nuclear lobes connected by thin filaments.
is_a: HP:0012135 ! Abnormal granulocytopoietic cell morphology
property_value: dc:date "2017-06-18T14:13:54Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

