[Term]
id: HP:0031433
name: Alexithymia
synonym: "أليكسيثيميا" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدم الوعي بمشاعر الآخرين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تتميز الأليكسيثيميا بوجود خلل في القدرة على الوعي بمشاعر الفرد وتحديدها ووصفها بشكل صريح.
alt_id: HP:5200122
def: "Alexithymia is characterized by an impaired ability to be aware of, explicitly identify, and describe one's feelings." [PMID:34389125]
comment: Whereas implicit (e.g., physiological arousal) and explicit (e.g., self-reported emotion intensity) indicators of emotional reactivity tend to be highly associated in healthy volunteers, in alexithymia there is a decoupling of implicit and explicit emotional responses Alexithymia may manifest as a limited ability to respond to facial cues or other signs of emotions in others, often accompanied by detached connections to others.
synonym: "Unaware of others' emotions" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0012760 ! Reduced social responsiveness
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-16T12:21:45Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031434
name: Abnormal prosody
synonym: "اضطراب التصويت" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نمط صوت غير طبيعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يشير التصويت إلى أنماط الإيقاع والتوتر والتنغيم في اللغة المنطوقة. يشير اضطراب التصويت إلى شذوذ في هذه الأنماط التي يمكن سماعها من قبل المراقب. بشكل عام، يشير ذلك إلى انحرافات واضحة عن الأنماط المقبولة ثقافياً، ولكن قد يشمل أيضاً الاختلافات الملحوظة مقارنة بالأنماط المعتادة للفرد.
def: "Prosody refers to the patterns of rhythm, stress, and intonation in spoken language. Abnormal prosody refers to abnormalities in the patterns of rhythm, stress, or intonation of speech or vocalization that can be heard by the observer. In general, this refers to overt and clear deviations in patterns from culturally accepted norms but many also include differences noted in comparison to the usual patterns of the individual (a quiet person suddenly becomes loud or vice versa)." []
comment: Abnormal prosody refers to overt and clear deviations in patterns from culturally accepted norms but many also include differences noted in comparison to the usual patterns of the individual (a quiet person suddenly becomes loud or vice versa).
is_a: HP:0002167 ! Abnormal speech pattern
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-16T12:34:05Z" xsd:dateTime
