synonym: "شذوذ حجم صمام يوتساكيان" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "صمام يوتساكيان كبير الحجم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: صمام يوتساكيان كبير الحجم بشكل غير طبيعي (بعد الولادة). يُعرف صمام يوتساكيان أيضاً بصمام الوريد الأجوف السفلي، وهو بقايا جنينية لصمام الوريد الأجوف السفلي.
def: "An abnormally large Eustachian valve (postnatally). The Eustachian valve is also known as the valve of the inferior vena cava, and is an embryologic remnant of the valve of the inferior vena cava." [PMID:12484622]
comment: During fetal life, the eustachian valve directs oxygen-rich blood from the inferior vena cava (IVC) toward the foramen ovale and away from the tricuspid valve. After the closure of the foramen ovale, it does not have a specific function. In echocardiographic examinations, the eustachian valve may appear as a thin flap originating from the orifice of the IVC, or it may be totally absent. Sometimes it may appear as a rigid, elongated structure in the inferior portion of the right atrium or as a membranous, undulating, echogenic mass within the right atrial cavity.
synonym: "Enlarged inferior vena cava valve" EXACT []
synonym: "Giant Eustachian valve" NARROW []
is_a: HP:0025576 ! Abnormal inferior vena cava morphology
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-15T12:51:38Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031592
name: Situs inversus with levocardia
synonym: "انقلاب الوضعية مع وجود القلب على اليسار" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تغيير وضع الأعضاء مع وجود القلب على اليسار" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انقلاب وضعية الأحشاء الصدرية والبطنية مع بقاء القلب في وضعه الطبيعي على اليسار؛ وغالباً ما يرتبط بوجود عيوب قلبية خلقية مثل تبديل الأوعية الدموية العظمى و/أو عيوب الطحال بما في ذلك نقص الطحال أو تعدد الطحال.
def: "Situs inversus of thoracic and abdominal viscera with the heart remaining normally situated on the left; usually associated with congenital cardiac abnormalities such as transposition of the great vessels and/or spleen defects including asplenia or polysplenia." [Fyler:0102, Fyler:102, MP:0011253]
is_a: HP:0011534 ! Abnormal spatial orientation of the cardiac segments
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-15T13:19:50Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031593
name: Abnormal PR interval
synonym: "شذوذ في الفاصل الزمني PR" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في الفاصل الزمني PR" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل في الفاصل الزمني PR، وهو الجزء من رسم القلب الممتد من بداية موجة P إلى بداية مركب QRS. الفاصل الزمني الطبيعي في البالغين يبلغ 0.12-0.2 ثانية.
def: "An anomaly of the PR interval, which is the portion of the ECG from the onset of the P wave to the beginning of the QRS complex. A normal PR interval in adults is 0.12-0.2 seconds." [PMID:23677846]
comment: The PR interval begins at the onset of the P wave and ends at the onset of the QRS complex. This interval reflects the time the impulse takes to reach the ventricles from the sinus node. In contrast, the PR segment begins at the endpoint of the P wave and ends at the onset of the QRS complex. It reflects the conduction from the atrioventricular node, down the bundle of His and through the bundle branches to the muscle.
is_a: HP:0003115 ! Abnormal EKG
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-15T13:27:21Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031594
name: PR segment depression
synonym: "انخفاض شريحة PR" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انخفاض في الجهد الكهربي لشريحة PR تحت الخط الأساسي.
def: "A reduction in voltage of the PR segment below baseline." []
comment: The differential diagnosis includes normal variant, pericarditis or atrial infarct.
synonym: "PR interval depression" EXACT []
synonym: "PTa depression" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031596 ! Abnormal PR segment
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-15T13:31:27Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031595
name: Abnormal P wave
synonym: "شذوذ في موجة P" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في موجة P" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أي خلل في موجة P من رسم القلب، والتي تنتج عن إزالة الاستقطاب الأذيني. تحدث موجة P عندما يخلق العقدة الجيبية الأذينية جهد فعل يقوم بإزالة استقطاب الأذنية.
def: "Any anomaly of the P wave of the EKG, which results from atrial depolarization. The P wave occurs when the sinoatrial node creates an action potential that depolarizes the atria." []
comment: P waves are normally upright in leads I and II and inverted in aVR.
is_a: HP:0003115 ! Abnormal EKG
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-15T13:31:59Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031596
name: Abnormal PR segment
synonym: "شذوذ شريحة PR" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في شريحة PR" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل في شريحة PR، والتي تبدأ عند نهاية موجة P وتنتهي عند بداية مركب QRS. عادة ما تكون شريحة PR مسطحة ومتكافئة.
def: "An anomaly of the PR segment, which begins at the endpoint of the P wave and ends at the onset of the QRS complex. The PR segment is normally flat and isoelectric." []
comment: The PR interval begins at the onset of the P wave and ends at the onset of the QRS complex. This interval reflects the time the impulse takes to reach the ventricles from the sinus node. In contrast, the PR segment begins at the endpoint of the P wave and ends at the onset of the QRS complex. It reflects the conduction from the atrioventricular node, down the bundle of His and through the bundle branches to the muscle.
is_a: HP:0003115 ! Abnormal EKG
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-15T13:35:56Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031597
name: PR segment elevation
synonym: "ارتفاع شريحة PR" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة في الجهد الكهربي لشريحة PR فوق الخط الأساسي.
def: "An increase in voltage of the PR segment above baseline." []
synonym: "PR interval elevation" EXACT []
synonym: "PTa elevation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031596 ! Abnormal PR segment
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-15T13:45:12Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031598
name: Notched P wave
synonym: "موجة P مثلمة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "قطع في موجة P" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يتضمن ذلك وجود قطع على شكل V (ثلمة) في منتصف موجة P.
def: "V-shaped cut (notch) in the middle of the P wave." []
comment: One may observe notched P-waves in the frontal plane in partial interatrial block.
is_a: HP:0031595 ! Abnormal P wave
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-15T13:53:22Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031599
name: P mitrale
synonym: "P ميترايلي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "موجة P عريضة في تخطيط القلب" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: موجة P ذات شكل عريض (مدة 120 مللي ثانية أو أكثر) ومزدوجة في التخطيط الكهربائي للقلب في المسار الثاني.
def: "A broad (120 ms or longer in duration) and bifid P-wave in EKG lead II." []
is_a: HP:0031595 ! Abnormal P wave
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-15T14:01:02Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031600
name: P wave inversion
synonym: "انعكاس موجة P" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انعكاس موجة P في تخطيط القلب" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: موجة P تكون تحت الخط الأساسي بدلاً من أن تكون فوقه. قد يشير انعكاس موجة P في المسارات السفلية إلى أصل غير جيبي لموجات P.
def: "P wave below instead of above the baseline. P-wave inversion in the inferior leads may indicate a non-sinus origin of the P waves." []
is_a: HP:0031595 ! Abnormal P wave
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-15T14:02:33Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031601
name: P pulmonale
synonym: "P بولمونالي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شكل غير طبيعي للموجة في تخطيط القلب" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود موجات P عالية ومحدبة في الرصاص II من تخطيط القلب.
def: "The presence of tall, peaked P waves in EKG lead II." []
comment: P pulomonale may indicate right atrial enlargement, usually due to pulmonary hypertension.
