[Term]
id: HP:0031686
name: Increased stool alpha1-antitrypsin concentration
synonym: "زيادة تركيز الألفا-1 أنتيتريبسين في البراز" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة في مستوى الألفا-1 أنتيتريبسين في البراز" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: كمية مرتفعة بشكل غير طبيعي من الألفا-1 أنتيتريبسين في البراز.
def: "An abnormally elevated amount of alpha1-antitrypsin in the feces." []
comment: Alpha-1-antitrypsin is resistant to degradation by digestive enzymes and can therefore be used as a marker for the presence of blood proteins in the intestinal tract (e.g., protein-losing enteropathy).
is_a: HP:0031685 ! Abnormal stool composition
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-17T21:09:20Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031687
name: Abnormally loud pulmonic component of the second heart sound
synonym: "ارتفاع الصوت المكون الرئوي للنبضة الثانية للقلب" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "صوت رئوي أعلى من المعتاد للنبضة الثانية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يُشار إلى صوت غير معتاد في المكون الرئوي للنبضة الثانية للقلب.
comment: The pulmonic component is considered to be abnormally loud in a subject over age 20 if it is greater than the aortic component in the second left ICS or if it is audible at the cardiac apex. This may be due either to pulmonary artery hypertension or right ventricular dilatation, with part of the right ventricle assuming the position normally occupied by the left ventricle. A split second sound at the apex is, therefore, definitely abnormal. The loud P2 commonly heard at the apex in patients with atrial septal defect is probably due to a dilated right ventricle encroaching upon the cardiac apex [source-NCBI:NBK341].
synonym: "Accentuation of the pulmonic component of the second heart sound" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031661 ! Abnormal second heart sound
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-17T21:17:09Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031688
name: Erythroid dysplasia
synonym: "خلل تنسجي في الخلايا الحمراء" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في تكوّن الخلايا الحمراء" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل تنسجي في النسب الحمراء، والذي يعرض مجموعة متنوعة من التغيرات المورفولوجية في نخاع العظم، بما في ذلك تكون البراعم النووية أو تباين الحافة النووية في الأروميات الحمراء.
def: "Dysplasia in the erythroid lineage, which presents with a variety of morphological changes in the bone marrow, including nuclear budding or irregular nuclear contour in erythroblasts." [PMID:26791933]
synonym: "Dyserythropoiesis" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0012130 ! Abnormal erythroid lineage cell morphology
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-17T22:04:44Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031689
name: Megakaryocyte dysplasia
synonym: "خلل تنسجي في الخلايا الضخمة النواء" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في تكوّن الخلايا الضخمة النواء" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود خلايا ضخمة النواء صغيرة بالحجم أو بنوى قليلة الفصوص أو غير مفلوقة في الخلايا الضخمة لكل الأحجام ونوى متعددة متفرقة.
def: "The presence of micro-megakaryocytes, hypo-lobed, or non-lobed nuclei in megakaryocytes of all sizes and multiple, widely-separated nuclei." [PMID:27127725]
synonym: "Dysmegakaryopoiesis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012143 ! Abnormal megakaryocyte morphology
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-17T22:09:51Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031690
name: Opportunistic infection
synonym: "عدوى انتهازية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى تستغل ضعف المناعة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى تسببها ممرضات عادةً لا تستطيع التسبب في العدوى لدى شخص ذي جهاز مناعي طبيعي، حيث تستغل هذه الممرضات الفرصة المتاحة بسبب ضعف الجهاز المناعي.
def: "An infection that is caused by a pathogen that would generally not be able to cause an infection in a host with a normal immune system. Such pathogens take advantage of the opportunity, so to speak, that is provided by a weakened immune system." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Opportunistic infection are infections that occur more often or are more severe in people with weakened immune systems than in those with normal immune system functioning.
is_a: HP:0032101 ! Unusual infection
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-17T22:11:49Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031691
name: Severe viral infection
synonym: "عدوى فيروسية شديدة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى فيروسية قوية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى فيروسية شديدة بشكل غير اعتيادي.
def: "An unusually severe viral infection." [PMID:21960712]
comment: The majority of viral infections acquired by nonimmunosuppressed individuals are asymptomatic or result in mild clinical manifestations. These individuals are able to mount effective immune responses that either clear the virus from the body or, for viruses that establish latency, maintain the virus in a dormant state. For individuals who are immunocompromised, because of a genetic immunodeficiency or immunosuppressive drug therapy, viral infections may result in life-threatening disease. Such patients present with infections that are severe, persistent, recurrent, or refractory to therapy and are usually caused by viruses of low virulence prevalent in the community.
is_a: HP:0032169 ! Severe infection
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-17T22:28:59Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031692
name: Severe cytomegalovirus infection
synonym: "عدوى شديدة بفيروس السيتوميجالو" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى قوية بفيروس السيتوميجالو" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى شديدة بشكل غير اعتيادي بفيروس السيتوميجالو.
def: "An unusually severe infection by cytomegalovirus." [PMID:12588074]
comment: A typical mononucleosis syndrome consists of an acute febrile illness with an increase of 50 percent or more in the number of lymphocytes or monocytes, with at least 10 percent of the lymphocytes being atypical. Immunocompromised patients may experience more severe complications such as CMV retinitis.
is_a: HP:0031691 ! Severe viral infection
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-17T22:31:35Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

