synonym: "انخفاض عد اليوزينيات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انخفاض غير طبيعي في العدد المطلق لليوزينيات في الدم، لكل ميكرولتر، مقارنة بنطاق مرجعي لجنس معين وفئة عمرية معينة.
def: "Abnormal decrease of absolute number of eosinophils in the blood, per microlitre, compared to a reference range for a given sex and age-group." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Decreased eosinophil count" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020064 ! Abnormal total eosinophil count
property_value: dc:date "2018-05-13T20:35:28Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031898
name: Rouleaux formation
synonym: "تكون التكدسات" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تراكم الخلايا الحمراء" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة تراكم كريات الدم الحمراء في شكل سلاسل طويلة. هذا التكون يُلاحظ عند زيادة بروتينات المصل، خصوصاً الفيبرينوجين والجلوبيولينات، ويمثل سبب زيادة معدل ترسيب الكريات الحمراء لأن التكدسات تترسب بسهولة أكثر من كريات الدم الحمراء المنفردة.
def: "Increased amount of stacking of erythrocytes into long chains. Rouleaux (singular: rouleau) is derived from a French word that can refer to a stack of coins put into a cylindircal paper roll. Rouleaux formation is observed with increased serum proteins, particularly fibrinogen and globulins, and represents the cause of increased erythrocte sedimentation rate because rouleaux sediment more readily than isolated red blood cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:16739263]
synonym: "Increased rouleaux formation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001877 ! Abnormal erythrocyte morphology
property_value: dc:date "2018-05-19T15:09:54Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0031899
name: Abnormal coagulation factor V activity
synonym: "خلل نشاط عامل التخثر V" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في عامل التخثر V" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أي انحراف عن نشاط عامل التخثر الخامس.
def: "Any deviation from the activity of coagulation factor V." []
comment: Factor V is activated to factor Va by means of minute amounts of thrombin (and inactivated by larger amounts of thrombin). Activated factor V (fVa) is a cofactor in the formation of the prothrombinase complex.
synonym: "Abnormal factor V activity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010990 ! Abnormality of the common coagulation pathway
property_value: dc:date "2018-05-19T15:11:38Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

