[Term]
id: HP:0032009
name: Infantile constant exotropia
synonym: "حوَل وحشي ثابت عند الرضع" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "حوَل وحشي مستمر عند الرضع" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: حالة حوَل وحشي ثابت يحدث قبل سن 6 أشهر؛ غالبًا ما يُصاحب بزاوية انحراف كبيرة وتشوهات في العين أو الجهاز العصبي المركزي.
def: "Constant exotropia occurring before 6 months of age.; often associated with a large angle of deviation and ocular/CNS abnormalities." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
comment: Typically infantile constant exotropia suggests presentation at 6 months of age or younger, while basic constant exotropia suggests later presentation (older than 6-12 months). (OHO 745 & 750).
synonym: "Infantile (constant) exotropia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031713 ! Constant exotropia
property_value: dc:date "2018-07-22T15:37:33Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032010
name: Basic constant exotropia
synonym: "حول وحشي ثابت أساسي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "حول مستمر للعينين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: حول وحشي ثابت للرؤية القريبة والبعيدة، يظهر بعد سن 6 أشهر.
def: "Constant exotropia for near and distance, presenting after 6 months of age." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
comment: Typically infantile constant exotropia suggests presentation at 6 months of age or younger, while basic constant exotropia suggests later presentation (older than 6-12 months). (OHO 745 & 750).
synonym: "Basic (constant) exotropia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031713 ! Constant exotropia
property_value: dc:date "2018-07-22T15:39:30Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032011
name: Heterophoria
synonym: "غيري الانحراف" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدم توازن العينين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الانحرافات الكامنة التي تُسيطر عليها عملية الانصهار. في ظل ظروف معينة (مهام بصرية محددة، إرهاق، مرض، إلخ)، لا يمكن الحفاظ على الانصهار ويحدث عدم تعويض.
def: "Heterophorias are latent deviations that are controlled by fusion. In certain circumstances (specific visual tasks, fatigue, illness, etc.), fusion can no longer be maintained and decompensation occurs." []
comment: In contrast to heterophoria, heterotropias are manifest deviations. Some individuals may be phoric in one situation (e.g. for distance) and tropic in another (e.g. for near). The distinction between heterotropia and heterophoria is that heterotropia refers to a misalignment of the eyes when the affected individual is looking at an object while the eyes are uncovered whereas heterophoria is a misalignment that is observed only when the two eyes are no longer looking at the same object. The monocular cover-uncover test is the most important test for detecting the presence of manifest strabismus and for differentiating a heterophoria from a heterotropia.
is_a: HP:0000486 ! Strabismus
property_value: dc:date "2018-07-22T15:44:43Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032012
name: Heterotropia
synonym: "غيري الحول" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "حول العينين الظاهر" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انحراف ظاهر لمحاور الرؤية لا يتم التحكم به بواسطة الانصهار.
def: "Manifest deviation of the visual axes not controlled by fusion." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
comment: The distinction between heterotropia and heterophoria is that heterotropia refers to a misalignment of the eyes when the affected individual is looking at an object while the eyes are uncovered whereas heterophoria is a misalignment that is observed only when the two eyes are no longer looking at the same object. The monocular cover-uncover test is the most important test for detecting the presence of manifest strabismus and for differentiating a heterophoria from a heterotropia.
is_a: HP:0000486 ! Strabismus
property_value: dc:date "2018-07-22T15:46:55Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

