[Term]
id: HP:0032146
name: HbC hemoglobin
synonym: "الهيموجلوبين HbC" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "الهيموجلوبين غير الطبيعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود نوع غير طبيعي من الهيموجلوبين يتميز باستبدال حمض الجلوتاميك في الموضع 7 بعد الميثيونين الأول باللايسين (6GAG>6AAG). يمكن تحديد وجود HbC بواسطة عملية تحليل الهيموجلوبين الكهربائي.
def: "Presence of an abnormal type of hemoglobin characterized by the substitution of a glutamic acid residue at position 7 following the initial methionine residue by a lysine (6GAG>6AAG). The presence of HbC can be determined by hemoglobin electrophoresis." [PMID:15215497, PMID:20301551]
synonym: "Haemoglobin C" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "HbC haemoglobin" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Hemoglobin C" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011902 ! Abnormal hemoglobin
property_value: dc:date "2018-11-22T16:41:53Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032147
name: Erythromelalgia
synonym: "إريثروميلالجيا" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "احمرار وألم الأطراف" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوبات متكررة من الاحمرار، والألم الحارق، والحرارة في الأطراف بعد التعرض للحرارة أو الجهد، والأعراض عادة ما تؤثر بشكل أساسي على القدمين.
def: "Recurrent episodes of redness, burning pain, and warmth of the extremities following exposure to heat or exercise with symptoms predominantly involving the feet." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1089-1543, PMID:26419464]
comment: Warmth, ambulation, physical exercise, sitting, leg dependence and wearing shoes or gloves can provoke and aggravate symptoms while immersion in ice/cold water, uncovering affected areas, ventilation and elevation can ameliorate these symptoms. Pain attacks usually start with an itchy-like feeling and then progress to a severe burning sensation as was reported by most patients, with the durations of which ranging from several minutes to hours and even days. Erythromelalgia can be a Mendelian trait or can be triggered by polycythemia vera, lymphoproliferative disorders, hypertension, and hyperviscosity.
is_a: HP:0012531 ! Pain
property_value: dc:date "2018-12-02T12:02:08Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

