[Term]
id: HP:0032232
name: Elevated circulating CK-MB concentration
synonym: "ارتفاع تركيز CK-MB في الدم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة CK-MB في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تركيز CK-MB (= كرياتين كيناز MB) في دوران الدم يتجاوز الحد الأعلى للطبيعي.
def: "The concentration of CK-MB (= creatine kinase MB) in the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal." []
comment: All CK isoforms are encoded by separate nuclear genes and, in most tissues, a single cytosolic CK isoform is co-expressed together with a single mitochondrial CK isoform (mtCK). Cytosolic muscle-type CK (M-CK) and brain-type CK (B-CK) form homodimers or heterodimers, e.g. MM-CK in skeletal muscle, MM, MB and BB-CK in heart, or BB-CK in brain, kidney, spermatozoa, skin and many other tissues. MtCK is situated in the outer mitochondrial compartment and occurs as sarcomeric mtCK (smtCK) expressed mainly in muscle tissue and as ubiquitous mtCK (umtCK) expressed in a large number of other cells and tissues. CK-MB levels can rise upon myocardial injury, CK-MM rises upon skeletal muscle damage, and CK-BB can rise with brain injury.
synonym: "Increased circulating CK MB isoform" EXACT abbreviation [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7941-2961]
is_a: HP:0040081 ! Abnormal circulating creatine kinase concentration
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-26T17:05:00Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032233
name: Increased circulating creatine kinase BB isoform
synonym: "زيادة نسبة نظير كرياتين كيناز BB في الدم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ارتفاع كرياتين كيناز BB في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة تركيز نظير كرياتين كيناز BB في الدورة الدموية.
def: "An increased concentration of the BB isoform of creatine kinase in the blood circulation." [PMID:21448658]
comment: All CK isoforms are encoded by separate nuclear genes and, in most tissues, a single cytosolic CK isoform is co-expressed together with a single mitochondrial CK isoform (mtCK). Cytosolic muscle-type CK (M-CK) and brain-type CK (B-CK) form homodimers or heterodimers, e.g. MM-CK in skeletal muscle, MM, MB and BB-CK in heart, or BB-CK in brain, kidney, spermatozoa, skin and many other tissues. MtCK is situated in the outer mitochondrial compartment and occurs as sarcomeric mtCK (smtCK) expressed mainly in muscle tissue and as ubiquitous mtCK (umtCK) expressed in a large number of other cells and tissues. CK-MB levels can rise upon myocardial injury, CK-MM rises upon skeletal muscle damage, and CK-BB can rise with brain injury.
synonym: "Increased circulating CK BB isoform" EXACT abbreviation [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7941-2961]
is_a: HP:0040081 ! Abnormal circulating creatine kinase concentration
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-26T17:11:51Z" xsd:dateTime
