[Term]
id: HP:0032247
name: Persistent CMV viremia
synonym: "الفيروسيمية المزمنة لفيروس CMV" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وجود دائم لفيروس CMV في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود مستمر وغير محكم لفيروس المضخم للخلايا (CMV) في الدورة الدموية.
def: "Lasting (uncontrolled) presence of cytomegalovirus in the blood circulation." [PMID:28130404]
comment: Persistent CMV infection has important clinical relevance in the global population. Although immune-mediated control of CMV in healthy individuals prevents disease and overt clinical symptoms, immune dysregulation caused by immunosuppressive treatments in transplant and cancer patients, congenital immunodeficiencies, HIV/AIDS, and/or aging can result in CMV viremia, life threatening disease, and even death.
is_a: HP:0031692 ! Severe cytomegalovirus infection
is_a: HP:0032248 ! Persistent viremia
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T13:32:28Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032248
name: Persistent viremia
synonym: "الفيروسيمية المزمنة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وجود دائم للفيروس في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: استمرار وجود الفيروس في دورة الدم لفترة أطول مما هو طبيعي لدى المضيف المناعي الكفء.
def: "Persistence of virus in the blood circulation longer than would be normal in an immunocompetent host." []
is_a: HP:0020071 ! Viremia
is_a: HP:0032169 ! Severe infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T13:36:30Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032249
name: Coccidioidomycosis
synonym: "الفطار الكرواني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "حمى الوادي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: التهاب ناتج عن فطر من أنواع الكوكسيديويدات. هذه الفطريات ثنائية الشكل، تعيش في التربة، تُعرف بقدرتها على إحداث طيف واسع من الأمراض التي تتراوح من حمى بسيطة إلى أعراض تنفسية خطيرة أو مرض منتشر. يتكون جنس الكوكسيديويد من نوعين جينيين متميزين: Coccidioides immitis وC. posadasii.
def: "Infection by a Coccidioides species fungus. These are dimorphic, soil-dwelling, fungi known to cause a broad spectrum of disease, ranging from a mild febrile illness to severe pulmonary manifestations or disseminated disease. The genus Coccidioides is comprised of two genetically distinct species: Coccidioides immitis and C. posadasii." [PMID:23843703]
comment: Persons with immunodeficiency diseases, diabetics, transplant recipients, and prisoners are also particularly vulnerable to infection by Coccidioides.
synonym: "Valley fever" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032255 ! Opportunistic fungal infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T13:37:54Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032250
name: Acinetobacter infection
synonym: "عدوى الزائفة الزنجارية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى زائفة زنجارية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى تنتج عن Acinetobacter baumannii، وهو عصية سالبة الجرام، هوائية، متغيرة الشكل وغير متحركة. يعتبر هذا الممرض ممرضاً انتهازياً وله نسبة انتشار عالية بين الأفراد الذين يعانون من نقص في المناعة، خاصة أولئك الذين قضوا فترة طويلة (أكثر من 90 يومًا) في المستشفى.
def: "An infection by Acinetobacter baumannii, a Gram-negative bacillus that is aerobic, pleomorphic and non-motile. An opportunistic pathogen, A. baumannii has a high incidence among immunocompromised individuals, particularly those who have experienced a prolonged (over 90 d) hospital stay." [PMID:22546906]
is_a: HP:0032260 ! Opportunistic bacterial infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T16:38:23Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032251
name: Abnormal immune system morphology
synonym: "شذوذ مورفولوجيا الجهاز المناعي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شكل غير طبيعي للجهاز المناعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أي خلل أو شذوذ في بنية الجهاز المناعي.
is_a: HP:0002715 ! Abnormality of the immune system
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T16:44:33Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032252
name: Granuloma
synonym: "الورم الحبيبي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مجموعة خلايا مناعية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تجمع مضغوط ومنظم من البالعات أحادية النواة الناضجة، والذي قد تصاحبه أو لا تصاحبه ميزات إضافية مثل النخر.
def: "A compact, organized collection of mature mononuclear phagocytes, which may be but is not necessarily accompanied by accessory features such as necrosis." [PMID:10908370, PMID:11168676, PMID:937513]
comment: Granulomas vary considerably in their degree of complexity, physical size and organization. Not surprisingly, their classification has attracted much attention, and a numbers of schemes have been described. The cornerstone of the granulomatous response, however, is the predominant involvement of mononuclear phagocytes. As granulomas develop, tissue-resident, as well as inflammatory mononuclear phagocytes become intimately acquainted, and these cells may develop highly differentiated epithelioid cell characteristics. In many cases, elegant multinucleate populations can be seen, distinct from the syncytia formed after viral infection as evident by their extended life-span. Accumulating lymphocytes, mainly T cells, contribute to the developing microarchitecture of the granuloma, often with characteristic patterns of subset organization relative to the core of mononuclear phagocytes and to each other. B lymphocytes, plasma cells, NK cells and neutrophils may all be present, though a relative paucity of neutrophils delineates these sites of inflammation from those associated with necrosis. At its extreme, the granuloma may serve as the focus for irreversible fibrotic reactions, but, even in less dramatic cases, a substantive degree of local tissue remodeling occurs.
is_a: HP:0032251 ! Abnormal immune system morphology
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T16:44:42Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032253
name: Eosinophilic granuloma
synonym: "ورم حبيبي حمضي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ورم حبيبي خلايا حمضية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من الورم الحبيبي يتميز بشكل مورفولوجي بتفوق خلايا لانجرهانز ذات النوى المحززة والمطوية والمحفورة في وسط يشمل أعدادًا متفاوتة من الخلايا الحمضية والخلايا البلعمية بما في ذلك الأشكال متعددة النوى، التي تبدو غالبًا مشابهة للخلايا العظمية أو الخلايا العملاقة الشبيهة بخلايا توتون، الخلايا العدلية والخلايا الليمفاوية الصغيرة. يتراوح تركيز التسلل الحمضي من خلايا ناضجة متناثرة إلى كتل كبيرة من الخلايا. في بعض الأحيان، قد تقطع مناطق نخر العظام التسلل الخلوي. قد تتجمع الخلايا الرغوية أيضًا في كتل، والتي ليس لها أهمية سريرية لأنها تمثل عملية البلعمة لحطام الدهون.
def: "A type of granuloma characterized morphologically by the predominance of Langerhans cells with characteristic grooved, folded, indented nuclei in the appropriate milieu that includes variable numbers of eosinophils and histiocytes including multinucleated forms, often appearing similar to osteoclasts or touton like giant cells, neutrophils and small lymphocytes. The concentration of the eosinophilic infiltrate varies from scattered mature cells to sheet-like masses of cells. Occasionally, areas of bone necrosis may interrupt the cellular infiltrate. The foamy cells may also be amassed in clumps, which are of no clinical significance because these clumps represent phagocytosis of lipid debris." [PMID:21938183]
comment: Eosinophilic granuloma (EG) is a benign disorder that affects children and young adults, particularly males. Solitary EG accounts for the majority of Langerhans cell histiocytosis cases, usually involving bone and less commonly the lymph nodes, lung or skin.
is_a: HP:0032252 ! Granuloma
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T16:50:48Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032254
name: Increased circulating copper concentration
synonym: "زيادة تركيز النحاس في الدوران الدموي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة النحاس في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تركيز مرتفع بشكل غير طبيعي للنحاس في الدورة الدموية. يشير هذا المصطلح إلى التركيز الكلي للنحاس.
def: "An abnormally elevated concentration of copper in the blood circulation. This term refers to the total copper concentration." []
synonym: "Elevated serum copper" EXACT []
synonym: "Hypercupremia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010836 ! Abnormal circulating copper concentration
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T17:13:31Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032255
name: Opportunistic fungal infection
synonym: "عدوى فطرية انتهازية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى فطرية لدى مرضى نقص المناعة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى تسببها فطريات لا تكون قادرة على إحداث عدوى في المضيف الذي يمتلك جهاز مناعي طبيعي. تستغل هذه الفطريات الفرصة بسبب ضعف الجهاز المناعي.
def: "An infection that is caused by a fungus that would generally not be able to cause an infection in a host with a normal immune system. Such fungi take advantage of the opportunity, so to speak, that is provided by a weakened immune system." []
is_a: HP:0020100 ! Unusual fungal infection
is_a: HP:0031690 ! Opportunistic infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T18:09:57Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032256
name: Histoplasmosis
synonym: "الهستو بلازما" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى فطرية لدى مرضى نقص المناعة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تسببها الفطر هستوبلازما كبسولاتوم وتعتبر عدوى انتهازية في الأفراد المثبطين مناعياً.
def: "Histoplasmosis is caused by the fungus Histoplasma capsulatum and is consider to be an opportunistic infection in immunosuppressed persons." [PMID:26897068, PMID:30619685]
comment: Most patients exhibit pulmonary signs and symptoms, accompanied by radiographic abnormalities, which often are mistaken for community-acquired pneumonia caused by bacterial or viral agents. Most of the infected individuals remain asymptomatic or have very mild illness that does not get diagnosed as histoplasmosis. Significant symptoms develop in less than 1% of patients and most frequently present as pulmonary or disseminated histoplasmosis. Immunocompromised individuals, including patients with AIDS, hematologic malignancies, transplant recipients, and patients receiving prolonged steroids, are at higher risk of developing acute disseminated disease with a rapid and aggressive course.
is_a: HP:0032255 ! Opportunistic fungal infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T18:10:09Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032257
name: Disseminated histoplasmosis
synonym: "الهستو بلازما المنتشرة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انتشار الهستو بلازما في الجسم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى الهستو بلازما التي تشمل مواقع متعددة من الجسم. يمكن أن تشمل أعضاء مختلفة مثل الأعضاء الشبكية البطانية والجهاز الهضمي والغدد الكظرية والجهاز العصبي المركزي والأوعية الدموية والكلى والجلد. تظهر عادة بأعراض نظامية مثل الحمى والتعب العام والتعرق الليلي وفقدان الوزن، إلى جانب الأعراض المرتبطة بالعضو المصاب. قد تظهر الأمراض المنتشرة الشديدة في صورة صدمة إنتانية وفشل متعدد الأعضاء ومتلازمة الضائقة التنفسية الحادة.
def: "Histoplasmosis infection involving multiple sites of the body. Disseminated histoplasmosis can involve various organs, including reticuloendothelial organs, gastrointestinal tract, adrenal glands, central nervous system, endovascular structures, kidney, and skin. It typically presents with systemic symptoms like fever, generalized fatigue, night sweats, weight loss, and the symptoms related to the specific organ involved. Severe disseminated disease can manifest as septic shock, multi organ failure, and ARDS." [PMID:30619685]
is_a: HP:0032256 ! Histoplasmosis
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T18:15:01Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032258
name: Pulmonary histoplasmosis
synonym: "الهستو بلازما الرئوية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "التهاب الرئة بسبب فطر الهستو بلازما" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى الرئة بفطر الهستو بلازما كبسولاتوم. الأعراض قد تشمل الحمى والصداع والضعف وألم الصدر والسعال الجاف. عند إجراء تصوير للصدر، قد تُظهر الصور شعاعيات مواضع الالتهاب الرئوي بشكل مبقع يشمل فص واحد أو أكثر مع تضخم العقد اللمفاوية في المنصف أو الجيب.
def: "Infection of the lungs with Histoplasma capsulatum. Symptoms may include fever, headache, weakness, chest pain and dry cough. When imaging is done, chest radiographs may show patchy pneumonia involving one or more lobes with adenopathy of the mediastinum or hilum." [PMID:21810958]
is_a: HP:0032256 ! Histoplasmosis
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T18:17:55Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032259
name: Chronic tinea infection
synonym: "عدوى السعفة المزمنة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى جلدية فطرية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مصطلح السعفة يعني عدوى فطرية، بينما يشير مصطلح الفطر الجلديفي إلى الكائنات الفطرية التي تسبب السعفة. يشير هذا المصطلح إلى عدوى السعفة التي تكون مزمنة أو مقاومة للعلاج وقد تعكس وجود خلل في المناعة.
def: "The term tinea means fungal infection, whereas dermatophyte refers to the fungal organisms that cause tinea. This term refers to a tinea infection that is chronic or recalcitrant to treatment and may be reflective of an immune defect." [PMID:25403034]
comment: Tinea is usually followed by a Latin term that designates the involved site, such as tinea corporis and tinea pedis. Tinea versicolor (now called pityriasis versicolor) is not caused by dermatophytes but rather by yeasts of the genus Malassezia. Tinea unguium is more commonly known as onychomycosis. Dermatophytes are usually limited to involvement of hair, nails, and stratum corneum, which are inhospitable to other infectious agents. Dermatophytes include three genera: Trichophyton, Microsporum, and Epidermophyton.
is_a: HP:0031035 ! Chronic infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T18:30:04Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032260
name: Opportunistic bacterial infection
synonym: "عدوى بكتيرية انتهازية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى بكتيرية لدى مرضى ضعف المناعة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى تسببها بكتيريا لا تكون قادرة على إحداث عدوى في المضيف الذي يمتلك جهاز مناعي طبيعي. تستغل هذه البكتيريا الفرصة بسبب ضعف الجهاز المناعي.
def: "An infection that is caused by a bacterium that would generally not be able to cause an infection in a host with a normal immune system. Such bacteria take advantage of the opportunity, so to speak, that is provided by a weakened immune system." []
is_a: HP:0031690 ! Opportunistic infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T18:37:49Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032261
name: Nontuberculous mycobacterial pulmonary infection
synonym: "عدوى رئوية بالبكتيريا غير السليّة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى رئوية ببكتيريا غير السلية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى في الرئة تسببها البكتيريا البيئية. يمكن أن تحدث هذه العدوى في الأشخاص الذين يعانون من مرض الرئة الاستعدادي أو أمراض المناعة.
def: "An infection of the lung caused by environmental mycobacteria. Such infections can occur in individuals with predisposing lung disease or immune disease." [PMID:24624285, PMID:7472715]
comment: Historically, human infections due to Mycobacterium were due almost exclusively to Mycobacterium tuberculosis (TB); the extensive societal impact of this infection is legendary. More recently, other species of mycobacterium causing clinical disease have been identified and, in many geographical regions, cause greater disease burden than TB. These organisms are referred to by a variety of collective names such as anonymous or atypical mycobacteria, mycobacteria other than tuberculosis (MOTT) and nontuberculous mycobacteria (NTM).
is_a: HP:0032260 ! Opportunistic bacterial infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T18:38:45Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032262
name: Pulmonary tuberculosis
synonym: "السل الرئوي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "السل الذي يؤثر على الرئتين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى الرئة ببكتيريا المتفطرة السلية وهي سلالات من المتفطرات التي تكون منحنية قليلاً، غير متحركة، هوائية، غير مغلفة وغير منتجة للأبواغ.
def: "A lung infection by Mycobacterium tuberculosis a slightly curved non-motile, aerobic, non-capsulated and non-spore forming strains of mycobacteria." [PMID:30345099]
comment: Predisposing factors include poverty, social disruption, malnutrition, different causes of immune suppression, human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection, HIV-TB co-infection and increasing drug resistance.
synonym: "Pulmonary TB" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0032260 ! Opportunistic bacterial infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T19:04:54Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032263
name: Increased blood pressure
synonym: "ارتفاع ضغط الدم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة غير طبيعية في ضغط الدم. لا تعتبر قياس واحد لضغط الدم المرتفع أنه يشير تلقائياً إلى الإصابة بارتفاع ضغط الدم. من الناحية العملية، يُوصى بإجراء قياسات متعددة لتشخيص وجود ارتفاع ضغط الدم.
def: "Abnormal increase in blood pressure. An individual measurement of increased blood pressure does not necessarily imply hypertension. In practical terms, multiple measurements are recommended to diagnose the presence of hypertension." [PMID:9137951]
synonym: "Increased BP" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0030972 ! Abnormal systemic blood pressure
property_value: dc:date "2019-01-27T20:07:59Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032264
name: Anti-NMDA receptor antibody positivity
synonym: "وجود أضداد مستقبلات NMDA في الدم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "أضداد مستقبلات NMDA" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود الأجسام المضادة الذاتية (الغلوبولينات المناعية) في المصل والتي تتفاعل ضد مستقبل الغلوتامات NMDA (N-methyl-D-aspartate).
def: "The presence of autoantibodies (immunoglobulins) in the serum that react against the NMDA (N-methyl-D-aspartate)-type glutamate receptor." [PMID:24729779]
synonym: "Presence of anti-N-methyl-D-aspartate Receptor antibody in blood" EXACT []
synonym: "Presence of anti-NMDAR antibody in blood" EXACT []
