[Term]
id: HP:0032397
name: Citrullinuria
synonym: "سيترولينوريا" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ارتفاع مستوى السيترولين في البول" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يكون مستوى السيترولين في البول، عند تعديله لتركيز البول، أعلى من الحد الطبيعي الأقصى.
def: "The amount of citrulline in the urine, when normalized for urine concentration, is above the upper limit of normal." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8169-9049, PMID:29695388]
comment: Citrulline is an alpha-amino acid that is a key intermediate in the urea cycle.
synonym: "Citrulline high in urine" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033098 ! Increased urinary non-proteinogenic amino acid level
property_value: dc:date "2019-02-24T16:59:47Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032398
name: Dysgyria
synonym: "ديسجيريا" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نمط تلافيف غير طبيعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمط تلافيفي غير طبيعي يتميز باختلالات في عمق أو اتجاه التلافيف.
def: "An abnormal gyral pattern characterized by abnormalities of sulcal depth or orientation." [http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q90573458, PMID:26130693, PMID:26564436, PMID:32895508]
comment: Dysgyria translates as abnormal gyration and can therefore be applied to almost every type of MCD (malformations of cortical development). However, this term was introduced to describe cortical malformations that do not meet classic features of any of the abovementioned well-established MCD types. Dysgyria describes a cortex of variable thickness and an abnormal gyral pattern characterized by abnormalities of sulcal depth or orientation (for example, obliquely oriented sulci directed radially towards the center of the cerebrum and narrow gyri separated by abnormally deep or shallow sulci). In the vast majority of cases, the term dysgyria describes an abnormal non-lissencephaly, non-polymicrogyria cortex within the spectrum of tubulinopathies.
is_a: HP:0002536 ! Abnormal cortical gyration
property_value: dc:date "2019-02-24T17:04:20Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032399
name: Dysgyria with normal cortical thickness
synonym: "ديسجيريا مع سمك قشري طبيعي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نمط تلافيف غير طبيعي مع سمك قشرة طبيعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمط تلافيفي غير طبيعي يتميز باختلالات في عمق أو اتجاه التلافيف ولكن مع سمك طبيعي للقشرة.
def: "An abnormal gyral pattern characterized by abnormalities of sulcal depth or orientation but with a normal thickness of the cortex." [http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q90573458]
is_a: HP:0032398 ! Dysgyria
property_value: dc:date "2019-02-24T17:05:51Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032400
name: Dysgyria with thickened cortex
synonym: "ديسجيريا مع قشرة سميكة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نمط تلافيف غير طبيعي مع قشرة سميكة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمط تلافيفي غير طبيعي يتميز باختلالات في عمق أو اتجاه التلافيف مع قشرة سميكة بين الباكيجيريا والبوليميكرجيريا.
def: "An abnormal gyral pattern characterized by abnormalities of sulcal depth or orientation and a thickened cortex intermediate between pachygyria and polymicrogyria." [http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q90573458]
is_a: HP:0006891 ! Thick cerebral cortex
