[Term]
id: HP:0032434
name: Delayed umbilical cord separation
synonym: "تأخر انفصال الحبل السري" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انفصال الحبل السري المتأخر" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يحدث انفصال الحبل السري في وقت متأخر عن الوقت الطبيعي.
def: "Separation of the umbilical cord occurs at an abnormally late timepoint." [PMID:11483823]
comment: The umbilical cord of the newborn usually separates and sloughs by the end of the second postnatal week. However, a wide variation exists in the age at which cord separation occurs in healthy infants with regard to ethnicity, geographical location, and methods of cord care. A marked delay in cord separation raises the suspicion of leukocyte adhesion deficiency, a rare disorder leading to defective neutrophil function.
synonym: "Delayed separation of umbilical cord" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010881 ! Abnormality of the umbilical cord
property_value: dc:date "2019-03-02T15:01:57Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032435
name: Neonatal omphalitis
synonym: "التهاب السرة الوليدي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى في السرة عند المولود" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى تصيب السرة و/أو الأنسجة المحيطة بها في فترة الولادة.
def: "An infection of the umbilicus and/or surrounding tissues occurring in the neonatal period." [PMID:30020710]
comment: The umbilical cord stump then gradually dries and typically falls off within 5 to 15 days. Both skin and enteric bacteria may colonize the devitalized tissue of the stump and lead to infection. Omphalitis is, therefore, a polymicrobial infection and the most common pathogens are Staphylococcus aureus, Streptococcus pyogenes, and gram-negative bacteria such as Escherichia coli, Klebsiella pneumoniae, and Proteus mirabilis.
synonym: "Omphalitis" EXACT []
synonym: "Umbilical cord stump infection" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010881 ! Abnormality of the umbilical cord
property_value: dc:date "2019-03-02T15:07:20Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

