def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration of C-reactive protein in the blood circulation." []
comment: C-reactive protein (CRP) is produced by the liver, and increases in concentration in response to inflammation.
synonym: "Abnormal C-reactive protein level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
property_value: dc:date "2019-03-02T15:10:11Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032437
name: Reduced circulating C-reactive protein concecntration
