[Term]
id: HP:0032446
name: Pulmonary bulla
synonym: "نفاخ رئوي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "فقاعة في الرئة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الفقاعات الرئوية هي مناطق دائرية من النفاخ ذات جدار رقيق ويزيد قياسها عن 1 سم في القطر. غالبًا ما تكون تحت الجنب في الموقع وعادة ما تكون أكبر في القمم. في بعض الحالات، يمكن أن تكون الفقاعات ضخمة وتؤدي إلى ضغط على الأنسجة الرئوية المجاورة. الفقاعة العملاقة تعرف بشكل تعسفي بأنها تلك التي تشغل على الأقل ثلث حجم الجنبة. عندما تكون كبيرة، يمكن للفقاعات أن تحاكي الاسترواح الصدري. السبب الأكثر شيوعًا هو النفاخ الجنبي، ولكن يمكن أيضًا رؤية الفقاعات في ارتباط مع النفاخ الحدي المركزي.
def: "Pulmonary bullae are rounded focal regions of emphysema with a thin wall which measure more than 1 cm in diameter. They are often subpleural in location and are typically larger in the apices. In some cases, bullae can be very large and result in compression of adjacent lung tissue. A giant bulla is arbitrarily defined as one that occupies at least one third of the volume of a hemithorax. When large, bullae can simulate pneumothorax. The most common cause is paraseptal emphysema but bullae may also be seen in association with centrilobular emphysema." [PMID:18195376, PMID:20028879, PMID:24106540]
comment: Blebs and bullae are commonly subpleural and are mostly seen in both upper lobes in patients with coexisting centrilobular and paraseptal emphysema.
synonym: "Pulmonary bullae" EXACT plural_form []
is_a: HP:0002097 ! Emphysema
property_value: dc:date "2019-03-03T17:45:09Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032447
name: Pulmonary bleb
synonym: "بليب رئوي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "فقاعة صغيرة في الرئة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: البليب هو حيز صغير يحتوي على الغاز داخل الجنب الحشوي أو في الرئة تحت الجنب، ولا يزيد قطره عن 1 سم. تظهر فحوصات التصوير المقطعي للبليب كحيز هوائي كيسي بجدران رقيقة وملاصق للجنب.
def: "A bleb is a small gas-containing space within the visceral pleura or in the subpleural lung, not larger than 1 cm in diameter. CT findings show a bleb as a thin-walled cystic air space contiguous with the pleura." [PMID:12934786, PMID:18195376, PMID:20028879]
is_a: HP:0002097 ! Emphysema
property_value: dc:date "2019-03-03T17:47:36Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032448
name: Achlorhydria
synonym: "انعدام الهيدروكلوريد" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدم وجود حمض في المعدة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: حالة يكون فيها إنتاج حمض الهيدروكلوريك في المعدة غائبًا.
def: "A condition in which production of hydrochloric acid in the stomach is absent." [PMID:29939570]
comment: Gastric acid is the fluid secreted by the stomach. It is composed of hydrochloric acid, potassium chloride, and sodium chloride. Hydrochloric acid plays an integral part in the digestion of food and protects our body against pathogens ingested with food or water. The parietal cells lining the stomach are mainly involved in its production.
is_a: HP:0012719 ! Functional abnormality of the gastrointestinal tract
property_value: dc:date "2019-03-03T17:54:51Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032449
name: Abnormal dermoepidermal hemidesmosome morphology
synonym: "شذوذ في شكل نصف الجسيم الالتصاقية الجلدية البشرة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شكل غير طبيعي في نصف الجسيمات الالتصاقية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: هيكل أو مظهر غير طبيعي لنصف الجسيمات الالتصاقية، وهي مجمعات متعددة البروتينات تسهل الالتصاق المستقر للخلايا الظهارية القاعدية بالغشاء القاعدي.
def: "An abnormal structure or appearance of hemidesmosomes, multiprotein complexes that facilitate the stable adhesion of basal epithelial cells to the underlying basement membrane." [PMID:25487405, PMID:26017636]
comment: Hemidesmosomes (HDs) are highly specialized integrin-mediated epithelial attachment structures that make cells firmly adhere to the extracellular matrix by establishing a link between the underlying basement membrane (BM) and the internal mechanical stress-resilient keratin intermediate filament (IF) network. Although HDs are defined by their ultrastructural appearance, two types of HDs, type I and II, can be distinguished on the basis of their protein components. Classical type I HDs, found in stratified and pseudostratified epithelia, for example in the epidermis, consist in five major components, namely integrin alpha6beta4, plectin isoform 1a (P1a), tetraspanin CD151, bullous pemphigoid antigen (BPAG)1 isoform e (BPAG1e, also called BP230) and BPAG2 (also called BP180 or type XVII collagen). Type II HDs, found in simple epithelia such as that of the intestine, consist of integrin alpha6beta4 and plectin and lack the two BP antigens.
is_a: HP:0031538 ! Abnormal dermoepidermal junction morphology
property_value: dc:date "2019-03-03T18:24:45Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

