[Term]
id: HP:0032462
name: Increased circulating palmitate level
synonym: "زيادة مستوى حمض النخيل في الدوران الدموي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ارتفاع حمض النخيل في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ارتفاع مستويَ الشحميات الحمضية (حمض النخيل) في الدورة الدموية عن المستوى الطبيعي.
def: "An elevation beyond the normal concentration of palmitate (palmitic acid) in the blood circulation." [PMID:29167646]
comment: Palmitic acid (16:0, PA) is the most common saturated fatty acid found in the human body and can be provided in the diet or synthesized endogenously from other fatty acids, carbohydrates and amino acids. PA represents 20-30% of total fatty acids (FA) in membrane phospholipids, and adipose triacylglycerols (TAG).
is_a: HP:0003455 ! Elevated circulating long chain fatty acid concentration
property_value: dc:date "2019-03-09T17:54:11Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032463
name: Reduced circulating fibronectin level
synonym: "انخفاض مستوى الفيبرونيكتين في الدوران الدموي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انخفاض فيبرونيكتين الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انخفاض في مستوى البروتين الفيبرونيكتين في الدورة الدموية عن المستوى الطبيعي.
def: "A reduction below the normal concentration of fibronectin the the blood circulation." [PMID:27185500]
comment: Fibronectin is a large vertebrate glycoprotein that is found in soluble and insoluble forms and involved in diverse processes. Protomeric fibronectin is a dimer of subunits, each of which comprises 29-31 modules - 12 type I, two type II and 15-17 type III. Plasma fibronectin is secreted by hepatocytes and circulates in a compact conformation before it binds to cell surfaces, converts to an extended conformation and is assembled into fibronectin fibrils.
synonym: "Decreased plasma fibronectin" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
property_value: dc:date "2019-03-09T18:08:23Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

