[Term]
id: HP:0032514
name: Supernumerary lacrimal punctum
synonym: "قناة دمعية إضافية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وجود قناة دمعية زائدة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تشوه خلقي يتميز بوجود قناة دمعية إضافية في الجفن.
def: "A congenital developmental anomaly characterized by the presence of an additional lacrimal punctum in an eyelid." [PMID:19875171, PMID:25943682]
comment: Tears mainly produced by the lacrimal gland travel nasally across the eye toward the punctum, found on the medial margin of each eyelid. This term describes a congenital anomaly chanracterized by the presence of more than one lacrimal punctum in an eyelid. Accessory puncta are typically located on the lower lid medial to the normal punctum with a slit-like appearance.
synonym: "Accessory puncta" EXACT []
synonym: "Double lacrimal puncta" EXACT []
synonym: "Double punctum" EXACT []
synonym: "Lacrimal punctum, duplication" EXACT []
synonym: "Punctum reduplication" EXACT []
synonym: "Supernumerary punctum" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011479 ! Abnormal lacrimal punctum morphology
property_value: dc:date "2019-05-23T23:34:54Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032515
name: Deep dermatophytosis
synonym: "التهاب جلدي عميق فطري" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "التهاب فطري جلدي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من عدوى الفطريات الجلدية الغازية للجلد العميق تتميز بتسلل جلدي واسع بواسطة عناصر فطرية.
def: "A type of invasive dermatophyte infection of the deep dermis characterized by extensive dermal infiltration by fungal elements." [PMID:20092423]
comment: Deep dermatophytosis is is found primarily in immunocompromised patients with chronic dermatophytosis. This form of invasive disease may result from follicular rupture with direct cutaneous invasion, sometimes augmented by trauma or topical corticosteroid creams. It is not necessarily associated with hair follicles and tends to be more rapid in onset, larger, and extend deeper than Majocchi's granuloma. These infections can form clusters of granulomas, pseudomycetomas, lymphedema and draining sinuses.
is_a: HP:0032516 ! Invasive dermatophyte infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-05-26T10:20:58Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032516
name: Invasive dermatophyte infection
synonym: "عدوى فطرية غازية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى جلدية فطرية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدوى تمتد بعمق في الأدمة بواسطة الفطريات الجلدية، وهي فطريات تسبب عادة أنواع مختلفة من العدوى السطحية (القوباء) أو في الجلد والشعر أو الأظافر.
def: "Infection that extends deeply into the dermis by dermatophytes, fungi that typically cause different types of superficial infection (tinea) or skin, hair, or nails." [PMID:20092423]
comment: The most common presentation of dermatophytosis in clinical practice is the appearance of scaly, cutaneous lesions found on the trunk in tinea coporis (ringworm), the feet or toes in tinea pedis (athlete's foot), the crural fold in tinea cruris (jock itch), the scalp in tinea capitis (cradle cap), or a discoloration of the fingernails or toenails in tinea unguium (onychomycosis). Dermatophytosis is a typically noninvasive infection but can evolve into a more aggressive disease in the immunocompromised host.
is_a: HP:0032162 ! Unusual skin infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-05-26T10:24:20Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032517
name: Majocchi's granuloma
synonym: "ورم حبيبي ماجوتشي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "التهاب جلدي حبيبي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ورم حبيبي ماجوتشي هو عدوى جلدية فطرية التهابية وحبيبية تتميز بالتهاب حبيبي حول بصيلة الشعر. يشمل النسيج المرضي للورم الحبيبي النخاعي لميجوتشي تسلل حبيبي للعقد اللمفاوي، والبلاعم، والخلايا الظهارية، والخلايا العملاقة متعددة النويات، والعدلات. على عكس التينيا الجلدية السطحية، يمكن الكشف عن خيوط الفطريات والجراثيم ليس فقط على سطح البشرة ولكن أيضًا داخل أو حول بصيلات الشعر.
def: "Majocchi's granuloma (MG) is an inflammatory and granulomatous, dermatophytic infection characterized by a granulomatous inflammation around the hair follicle. Histopathologically, MG demonstrates a nodular perifollicular granulomatous infiltrate of lymphoid cells, macrophages, epithelioid cells, multinucleated giant cells, and neutrophils. Unlike superficial dermatophytoses, fungal hyphae and spores can be detected not only on the surface of the epidermis but also within or around the hair follicles." [PMID:22435879, PMID:29861637]
comment: Majocchi's granuloma (MG) is classified into two forms, depending on the affected individual's health situation and clinical picture. The first form is mainly observed in healthy individuals and is defined as a perifollicular, papular form induced by penetrating trauma that is mostly observed in the lower extremities. The second form is granulomatous, related to immunosuppression, seen in a nodular form, and usually appears on the upper extremities. The main cause of MG is Trichophyton rubrum, followed by T. mentagrophytes, T. violaceum, and T. tonsurans. However, several fungi, such as T. interdigitale, Microsporum canis, Nannizzia gypsea (former M. gypseum), Epidermophyton floccosum, and Aspergillus species, can also cause MG.
is_a: HP:0032516 ! Invasive dermatophyte infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-05-26T10:32:18Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032518
name: Disseminated dermatophytosis
synonym: "التهاب جلدي فطري منتشر" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدوى فطرية منتشرة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من العدوى الفطرية الغازية يتميز بالتورط الوعائي والانتشار إلى أعضاء أخرى.
def: "A type of invasive dermatophyte infection characterized by vascular involvement and dissemination to other organs." [PMID:20092423, PMID:29861637]
comment: Disseminated dermatophytosis tends to occur in patients with both defi cient T cell-mediated immunity and an impaired infl ammatory response. This process occurs either by direct extension, draining lymphatics, or hematogenous spread. It can present with involvement of distant skin areas, lymph nodes, bone, muscle, liver, spleen, testes or the central nervous system. Ultimately, disseminated infection can result in bacterial superinfection, osteomyelitis, organ dysfunction and eventual death.
is_a: HP:0032516 ! Invasive dermatophyte infection
property_value: dc:date "2019-05-26T10:37:28Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032519
name: Increased Burr cell count
synonym: "زيادة عدد خلايا بور" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة خلايا بور" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلايا بور، التي تعرف أيضًا بالخلايا الشائكة، تمتلك حدودًا متكهنًا على كامل سطح الخلية. توجد خلايا بور عادة في حالات المرض الكلوي في مرحلته النهائية وأمراض الكبد. يمكن العثور على أعداد صغيرة من خلايا بور لدى الأفراد الأصحاء.
def: "Burr cells, also known as echinocytes, have a speculated border over the entire cell surface. Burr cells are commonly found in both end-stage renal disease and liver disease. Small numbers of Burr cells are commonly found in healthy individuals." [PMID:5614071]
is_a: HP:0001877 ! Abnormal erythrocyte morphology
property_value: dc:date "2019-05-26T11:08:57Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032520
name: Masseter muscular weakness
synonym: "ضعف عضلات الماضغة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ضعف عضلة الفك" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انخفاض قوة عضلة الماضغة، التي تتمثل وظيفتها الأساسية في رفع الفك السفلي وبالتالي رفع الفك السفلي نحو الفك العلوي لإغلاق الفك.
def: "Reduced strength of the masseter muscle, whose primary function is to elevate the mandible and thereby raise the mandible towards the maxilla, closing the jaw." []
is_a: HP:0031815 ! Abnormal oral physiology
property_value: dc:date "2019-05-26T11:14:27Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032521
name: Self hugging
synonym: "احتضان الذات" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: حركات لا إرادية تشبه التشنجات تتكون من تقاطع كلا الذراعين عبر الصدر وشد الجسم أو تشابك اليدين وضغط الذراعين على الجانبين. تستمر الحركة لبضع ثوان ويمكن أن تحدث في سلسلة أو سريعة، عادة ما تصاحبها تشنجات في الوجه وأحيانًا همهمات.
def: "Involuntary, tic-like movements consisted of crossing both arms across the chest and tensing the body or clasping the hands and squeezing the arms to the sides. The movements last a few seconds and may occur in series or flurries, generally accompanied by facial grimacing and occasional grunting." [PMID:8132119]
comment: This is a characteristic behavior in Smith-Magenis syndrome.
synonym: "Spasmodic upper-body squeeze" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8430-6039, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4422-1708, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3777-1389]
is_a: HP:4000079 ! Sensory seeking
is_a: HP:5200019 ! Stereotypic whole-body movements
property_value: dc:date "2019-05-26T11:19:58Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8430-6039
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
