comment: Arabic Definition: تراكم داخل الخلايا للسكر المتعدد المرتبط بالدهون والوسيط Man5GlcNAc2-PP-dolichol.
def: "Intracellular accumulation of the lipid-linked oligosaccharide intermediate Man5GlcNAc2-PP-dolichol." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, PMID:10581255, PMID:16053906, PMID:28575298]
comment: Intracellular accumulation of Dol-PP-GlcNAc2Man5 can result from a defect in ALG3, which encodes a mannosyltransferase that transfers mannose from dolichyl phosphate mannose. The accumulation can be measured in fibroblasts. During protein N-glycosylation, glycans from lipid-linked oligosaccharides (LLOs) are transferred onto asparagine residues located in N-glycosylation sequons. The synthesis of LLO comprises three steps: It begins with the biosynthesis of the intermediate Dol-PP-GlcNAc2Man5, which occurs on the cytoplasmic side of the endoplasmic reticulum (ER). The second step is the flipping of this intermediate to the luminal side of the ER. The third step comprises the glycan extension in the ER lumen, yielding Dol-PP-GlcNAc2Man9.
is_a: HP:0011017 ! Abnormal cellular physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032577
name: Clonal T cell receptor rearrangement
synonym: "إعادة ترتيب مستقبِل T الخليوي الكلوني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وجود نوع واحد بارز من خلايا T" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود نوع غالب من خلايا T. في الفحوص المعتمدة على تقنية تفاعل البوليميراز المتسلسل (PCR)، يتم استدلال هذه الظاهرة بناءً على ظهور شريط واحد أو شريطين بارزين ضمن نطاق حجم صالح. في الفحوص المعتمدة على تسلسل الجيل الجديد (NGS)، يتم الاستدلال بناءً على العدد الكبير من القراءات التي تناظر مستقبِل T الخليوي المنفرد.
def: "Presence of a predominant T cell clone. In PCR-based assays, this finding is inferred on the basis of one or two prominent bands within a valid size range. In NGS-based assays, this finding is inferred on the basis of a high number of reads that map to a single T cell receptor clone." [PMID:24688753]
is_a: HP:0025845 ! Abnormal TCR repertoire
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032578
name: Third ventricle colloid cyst
synonym: "كيسة كولودية في البطين الثالث" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "كيسة في البطين الثالث" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: كيسة مبطنة بالظهارة ومملوءة بمادة جلاتينية. تحتوي المادة الجلاتينية عادةً على الميوسين، دم قديم، الكوليسترول، والأيونات. أغلب الكيسات الكولودية المكتشفة تكون بدون أعراض وتكشف صدفةً من خلال التصوير. عندما تسبب الكيسة الكولودية مشاكل، فهي غالباً تسبب استسقاء الرأس المعوق.
def: "An epithelial lined cyst filled with gelatinous material. The gelatinous material commonly contains mucin, old blood, cholesterol, and ions. Most colloid cysts identified are currently asymptomatic and identified incidentally on imaging. When a colloid cyst does cause issues, it most commonly causes obstructive hydrocephalus." [PMID:30542631]
comment: The colloid cyst is most commonly found in the rostral third ventricle at or near the foramen of Monro. The foramen of Monro is the conduit of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) outflow from the lateral ventricles to the third ventricle. A colloid cyst can act as a ball valve, stopping CSF flow out of the lateral ventricles. If this occurs, CSF backs up into the lateral ventricles and causes ventriculomegaly and hydrocephalus.
is_a: HP:0010576 ! Intracranial cystic lesion
is_a: HP:0010951 ! Abnormal third ventricle morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032579
name: Vascular hamartoma
synonym: "ورم وعائي حميد" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تنمو زيادات غير ضارة من الأنسجة الوعائية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمو بؤري حميد يتكون من الأنسجة الوعائية.
def: "A benign focal growth composed of vascular tissue." [NCIT:C3438]
is_a: HP:0010566 ! Hamartoma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032580
name: Abnormal bulbus cordis morphology
synonym: "شذوذ شكل الحويصلة القلبية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شذوذ في شكل جزء من القلب" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ في بنية الحويصلة القلبية، وهي المسار الوحيد لتدفق الدم من القلب خلال التكوّن الجنيني المبكر.
def: "Abnormal structure of the bulbus cordis, which is the single outflow tract of the heart during early embryogenesis." [PMID:25274757]
comment: The portion of the embryonic heart that receives blood is called the sinus venosus. There are two horns, the left and the right, that pump blood into the primordial atrium, which is then pumped into the ventricle and the bulbus cordis. From the bulbus cordis, it goes into the aortic sac which is connected to the first aortic arch.
is_a: HP:0001627 ! Abnormal heart morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032581
name: Abnormal renal insterstitial morphology
synonym: "شذوذ شكل الخلال الكلوي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شذوذ في تركيب نسيج الكلية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أي شذوذ بنيوي في نسيج الكلى. يتم تعريف الخلال الكلوي بأنه المساحة الواقعة بين الأنابيب والغدد بدون أوعية دموية.
def: "Any structural anomaly of the interstitium of the kidney. The renal interstitium is defined as the intertubular, extraglomerular, extravascular space of the kidney. It is bounded on all sides by tubular and vascular basement membranes and is filled with cells, extracellular matrix, and interstitial fluid." [PMID:25813241]
is_a: HP:0012210 ! Abnormal renal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032582
name: Renal interstitial foam cells
synonym: "خلايا رغوية بالنسيج الخلالي في الكلى" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلايا دهون في الكلى" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تراكم الخلايا الرغوية في النسيج الخلالي للكلية. تظهر خلايا الكلى الرغوية خصائص شكلية مشابهة لخلايا الجهاز المناعي وتكون جزءاً من سلالة الخلايا وحيدة النواة/الماكروفاج. من الناحية النسيجية، تتميز خلايا الكلى الرغوية بأنها خلايا مستديرة ذات نوى صغيرة وغشاء خلوي موجب لحمض شبه دوري يحتوي على حويصلات مليئة بالشحوم.
def: "Accumulation of foam cells (FC) in the interstitium of the kidney. Renal FCs display phenotypic characteristics of macrophages and belong to the monocyte/macrophage lineage. Histologically, renal FCs are characterized by round cells with small nuclei and an abundant PAS-positive cytoplasm with lipid-containing vacuoles." [PMID:19672113, PMID:25887903]
comment: FCs are the outcome of cellular lipid accumulation due to lipid metabolic dysfunction. Normally, lipid is in a dynamic equilibrium outside and inside of the cell. When factors facilitate cell lipid intake or reduce its efflux, it subsequently resulted in cellular lipid accumulation and FC formation. Renal interstitial FCs are commonly encountered in Alport syndrome and are occasionally observed in various other kidney diseases, including idiopathic membranous nephropathy (IMN), IgA nephropathy (IgAN), focal and segmental glomerulosclerosis (FSGS), and membranoproliferative glomerulonephritis.
is_a: HP:0003651 ! Foam cells
is_a: HP:0032581 ! Abnormal renal insterstitial morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0032583
name: Renal glomerular foam cells
synonym: "خلايا رغوية في الكبيبة الكلوية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلايا رغوية في الجزء المصفى من الكلية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود خلايا رغوية في الجزء الخارج من الكلية المعروف بالكبيبة.
comment: Accumulation of foam cells (FC) in glomeruli of the kidney. Renal FCs display phenotypic characteristics of macrophages and belong to the monocyte/macrophage lineage. Histologically, renal FCs are characterized by round cells with small nuclei and an abundant PAS-positive cytoplasm with lipid-containing vacuoles. {xref="PMID:25887903", xref="PMID:19672113"}
is_a: HP:0000095 ! Abnormal renal glomerulus morphology
is_a: HP:0003651 ! Foam cells
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

