[Term]
id: HP:0033039
name: Increased circulating precipitin level
synonym: "زيادة مستوى الراسب المحيط" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة في الأجسام المضادة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود مستويات مرتفعة من الأجسام المضادة IgG التي تترسب بالمستضد في الدم.
def: "The presence of high titers of antigen-precipitating IgG in the serum." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7371-8158, PMID:22796841, PMID:26310038]
comment: Sensitization to inhaled antigens may cause high titers of antigen-precipitating IgGs. Precipitins support the diagnosis of hypersensitivity pneumonitis, also known as extrinsic allergic, in symptomatic individuals. They may also be found in asymptomatic individuals, indicating exposure to a certain antigen. Major antigens causing hypersensitivity pneumonitis are mushrooms, fungi, yeasts, bird proteins, certains chemicals, bacteria or mycobacteria.
synonym: "Increased level of antigen-precipitating IgG antibodies" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003237 ! Increased circulating IgG concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033040
name: Anti-Sm antibody positivity
synonym: "إيجابية الأجسام المضادة ل-SM" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وجود أجسام مضادة معينة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود أجسام مضادة ذاتية في الدم تتفاعل مع سبعة بروتينات تشكل جزء من جزيئات ريبونوكليوبروتين النووية الصغيرة.
def: "The presence of autoantibodies in the serum that react to seven proteins that consist of a core of small nuclear ribonucleoprotein (snRNP) particles." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0104-692X, PMID:31552434]
comment: Anti-Sm-autoantibodies are highly specific for systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE).
synonym: "Anti-Smith autoantibody" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033476 ! Extractable nuclear antigen positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033041
name: Cytokine storm
synonym: "عاصفة السيتوكين" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة شديدة في السيتوكينات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: إفراز مفرط أو غير مسيطر عليه للسيتوكينات المثيرة للالتهاب.
def: "Excessive or uncontrolled release of proinflammatory cytokines." [PMID:22390970]
comment: Cytokines are a diverse group of small proteins that are secreted by cells for the purpose of intercellular signaling and communication. Specific cytokines have autocrine, paracrine, and/or endocrine activity and, through receptor binding, can elicit a variety of responses, depending upon the cytokine and the target cell. Among the many functions of cytokines are the control of cell proliferation and differentiation and the regulation of angiogenesis and immune and inflammatory responses. Inflammation associated with a cytokine storm begins at a local site and spreads throughout the body via the systemic circulation. Rubor (redness), tumor (swelling or edema), calor (heat), dolor (pain), and function laesa (loss of function) are the hallmarks of acute inflammation. While the general concept of an excessive or uncontrolled release of proinflammatory cytokines is well known, a precise definition of what constitutes a cytokine storm is lacking. The first use of cytokine storm appears to be in an article published in 1993 on graft-versus-host disease. Cytokine storm has subsequently been described in patients infected by cytomegalovirus, Epstein-Barr virus-associated hemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis, group A streptococcus, influenza virus, variola virus, severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus (SARS-CoV), avian H5N1 influenza virus, and SARS-CoV-2
synonym: "Hypercytokinemia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011113 ! Abnormality of cytokine secretion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

