[Term]
id: HP:0033102
name: Monkey wrench femoral neck
synonym: "تشكيل رأس الفخذ على شكل مفتاح قرد" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شكل غير طبيعي لرأس الفخذ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يظهر في منطقة عنق الفخذ تشوه في الشكل بتضخم داخلي للجزء الأوسط وتضخم كبير للمدور الصغير (مع بعض التوسع أيضًا في المدور الأكبر)، مما يؤدي إلى تشكيل يشبه مفتاح القرد (المفتاح السويدي) في الجزء العلوي من الفخذ.
def: "The femoral neck region shows medial metaphyseal beaking and a significant enlargement of the lesser trochanter (with some enlargement also of the greater trochanter), producing a monkey wrench (Swedish key) configuration of the proximal femur. A monkey wrench refers to a type of adjustable wrench with one fixed and one adjustable jaw at right angles to a straight handle." [PMID:7977470]
synonym: "Monkey wrench appearance of femoral neck" EXACT []
synonym: "Monkey wrench configuration of the proximal femur" EXACT []
synonym: "Swedish key appearance of femoral neck" EXACT []
synonym: "Swedish key configuration of the proximal femur" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003367 ! Abnormal femoral neck morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033103
name: Elevated circulating CHI3L1 level
synonym: "ارتفاع مستوى بروتين CHI3L1 في الدم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة بروتين في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة تركيز بروتين شيتيناز شبيه 1 (CHI3L1) في الدورة الدموية.
def: "Increased concentration of chitinase 3-like 1 (CHI3L1) in the blood circulation." [PMID:18182077, PMID:7577068]
comment: Chitinase 3-like 1 (CHI3L1; previously known as YKL-40) is a glycoprotein with homology to the chitinase protein family, but without chitinase activity. Elevations of serum CHI3L1 can be measured by ELISA and are related to some kinds of bone disease.
synonym: "Elevated circulating chitinase 3-like 1 level" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated circulating YKL40 level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033104
name: Inappropriate absence of fever
synonym: "الغياب غير المناسب للحمى" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "غياب الحمى مع العدوى" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الفشل في تطور الحمى في وجود عدوى من المفترض أن تؤدي إلى استجابة حمية.
def: "Failure to develop fever in the presence of an infection that normally would be expected to elicit a febrile response." [PMID:31235509]
comment: The induction and maintenance of fever during infection involves the tightly coordinated interplay between the innate immune system and neuronal circuitry within the central and peripheral nervous systems. Some diseases (such as Hyper-IgE recurrent infection syndrome 5, autosomal recessive, which is due to IL6R mutation) are associated with a lack of clinically adequate inflammatory response in the face of marked infection.
is_a: HP:0004370 ! Abnormality of temperature regulation
property_value: dc:date "2020-08-29T13:06:30Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033105
name: Interhypothalamic adhesion
synonym: "التصاق ما بين تحت المهاد" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "التصاق في الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود شريط لحمي غير طبيعي يربط الحواف الإنسيّة للجزء الأيسر والأيمن من تحت المهاد عبر البُطَيْن الثالث.
def: "An abnormal parenchymal band connecting the medial margins of the left and right hypothalami across the third ventricle." [PMID:24874532]
comment: The appearance of the interhypothalamic adhesions visible in the sagittal plane as an additional small ovoid structure between the fornices and lamina terminalis, centered near the level of the midbrain cranial margin. Anatomically, this location corresponds to the anterior and tuberalis regions of the periventricular hypothalamus.
synonym: "Hypothalamic adhesion" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012286 ! Abnormal hypothalamus morphology
property_value: dc:date "2020-08-29T11:25:49Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033106
name: Elevated circulating D-dimer concentration
synonym: "ارتفاع تركيز D-dimer في الدم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة D-dimer في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة تركيز D-dimers، وهو علامة لتحلل الفبرين، في الدورة الدموية.
def: "An increased concentration of D-dimers, a marker of fibrin degradation, in the blood circulation." [PMID:19008457]
comment: The D-dimer antigen is a unique marker of fibrin degradation that is formed by the sequential action of 3 enzymes: thrombin, factor XIIIa, and plasmin. First, thrombin cleaves fibrinogen producing fibrin monomers, which polymerize and serve as a template for factor XIIIa and plasmin formation. Second, thrombin activates plasma factor XIII bound to fibrin polymers to produce the active transglutaminase, factor XIIIa. Factor XIIIa catalyzes the formation of covalent bonds between D-domains in the polymerized fibrin. Finally, plasmin degrades the crosslinked fibrin to release fibrin degradation products and expose the D-dimer antigen. D-dimer measurement has been most comprehensively validated in (1) the exclusion of venous thromboembolism (VTE) in certain patient populations and (2) the diagnosis and monitoring of coagulation activation in disseminated intravascular coagulation. Abnormal D-dimer in the appropriate clinical context denotes that there is no major ongoing activation of intravascular coagulation, and serves as a reliable tool for the exclusion of VTE.
synonym: "Elevated D-dimers" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated fibrin degradation fragment concentration" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0040224 ! Abnormality of fibrinolysis
property_value: dc:date "2020-08-29T11:29:26Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033107
name: Abnormal circulating proteinogenic amino acid concentration
synonym: "خلل تركيز الحمض الأميني البروتينوجيني الدوري" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة حمض أميني في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مستوى مرتفع من حمض أميني بروتينوجيني في الدورة الدموية. هذه الأحماض هي 23 حمضًا أمينيًا ألفا تُعتبر طليعة للبروتينات، وتندمج في البروتينات أثناء الترجمة. تتضمن المجموعة 20 حمضًا أمينيًا مُرمَّزًا بواسطة جينات النواة للكائنات الحقيقية للنواة إلى جانب السيلينوسيستين، البيروليزين، و N-فورميل ميثيونين.
def: "An elevated level of a proteinogenic amino acid in the blood circulation. These are the 23 alpha-amino acids that are precursors to proteins, and are incorporated into proteins during translation. The group includes the 20 amino acids encoded by the nuclear genes of eukaryotes together with selenocysteine, pyrrolysine, and N-formylmethionine." []
is_a: HP:0003112 ! Abnormal circulating amino acid concentration
property_value: dc:date "2020-08-29T11:59:15Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033108
name: Abnormal circulating proteinogenic amino acid derivative concentration
synonym: "خلل تركيز مشتقات الحمض الأميني البروتينوجيني الدوري" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تغير مشتقات الحمض الأميني في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أي انحراف عن التركيز الطبيعي في الدورة الدموية لمركب مشتق من حمض أميني.
def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration in the blood circulation of a compound that is derived from an amino acid." []
is_a: HP:0003112 ! Abnormal circulating amino acid concentration
property_value: dc:date "2020-08-29T12:01:40Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033109
name: Abnormal circulating non-proteinogenic amino acid concentration
synonym: "خلل تركيز الحمض الأميني غير البروتينوجيني الدوري" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تغير في الأحماض الأمينية غير البروتينوجينية في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أي انحراف عن التركيز الطبيعي في الدورة الدموية للحمض الأميني ألفا الذي ليس عضوًا في مجموعة الأحماض الأمينية البروتينوجينية 23.
def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration in the blood circulation of an alpha-amino acid which is not a member of the group of 23 proteinogenic amino acids." []
