[Term]
id: HP:0033126
name: Cutaneous necrosis
synonym: "تنخر جلدي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "موت الأنسجة الجلدية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تنخر الجلد والأنسجة تحت الجلد (موت الأنسجة). قد يظهر التنخر الجلدي سريرياً كقشرة سوداء مؤلمة وحساسة للغاية محاطة بجلد ذو لون رمادي أحمر باهت أو كشريحة ميتة (عادةً ما تكون بلون الكريم أو الأصفر).
def: "Skin and subcutaneous tissue necrosis (tissue death). Clinically, cutaneous necrosis may present as a painful and extremely tender black eschar (dead tissue found in a full-thickness wound) surrounded by dusky grey-red colored skin or as slough (dead tissue, usually cream or yellow in colour)." [PMID:16455730, PMID:28470091]
synonym: "Skin necrosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Skin necrotic patch" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011355 ! Localized skin lesion
property_value: dc:date "2020-09-05T13:12:04Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033127
name: Abnormality of the musculoskeletal system
synonym: "شذوذ الجهاز العضلي الهيكلي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مشاكل في الجهاز العضلي الهيكلي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شذوذ في الجهاز العضلي الهيكلي، الذي يتكون من عظام الهيكل العظمي، والعضلات، والغضاريف، والأوتار، والأربطة، والمفاصل، وأنسجة ضامة أخرى. يدعم الجهاز العضلي الهيكلي وزن الجسم، ويحافظ على وضعية الجسم، ويُنتج حركات الجسم أو أجزاء منه.
def: "An anomaly of the musculoskeletal system, which consists of the bones of the skeleton, muscles, cartilage, tendons, ligaments, joints, and other connective tissue. The musculoskeletal system supports the weight of the body, maintains body position and produces movements of the body or of parts of the body." []
is_a: HP:0000118 ! Phenotypic abnormality
property_value: dc:date "2020-09-05T13:35:03Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033128
name: Delayed ability to crawl
synonym: "تأخر القدرة على الزحف" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تأخر الزحف عند الأطفال" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: فشل في تحقيق القدرة على الزحف في المرحلة التطورية المناسبة. يتميز التطور الحركي الطبيعي للرضع بسلسلة من المراحل الوضعية بما في ذلك تعلم الزحف باليدين والركبتين بين سن 6 و10 أشهر.
def: "A failure to achieve the ability to crawl at an appropriate developmental stage. Normal infant motor development is marked by a series of postural milestones including learning to crawl on hands and knees between the ages of 6 and 10 months." []
is_a: HP:0002194 ! Delayed gross motor development
property_value: dc:date "2020-09-05T13:40:32Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033129
name: Abnormal shoulder physiology
synonym: "خلل الوظيفة الكتفية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تغير وظيفة الكتف" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل وظيفي في الكتف. الكتف هو مفصل كروي ومقبسي مكون من العظم العضدي، الكتف وعظم الترقوة الذين يرتبطون بالمفصل القصي الترقوي ، المفصل الأخرمي الترقوي ، المفصل الحقاني العضدي ، والمفصل الكتفصدرية. تربط الوصلات GH و AC و SC الطرف العلوي بالهيكل المحوري عند الصدر و تُمكن الحركة في مفصل الكتف: الثني، التمديد، والدوران للذراع.
def: "Anopmalous function of the shoulder. The shoulder is a ball-and-socket joint that is made up of humerus, scapula and clavicle, which are connected by the sternoclavicular joint (SC), the acromioclavicular joint (AC), the glenohumeral joint (GH), and the scapulothoracic joint (ST). The GH, AC and SC joints link the upper extremity to the axial skeleton at the thorax and enable movement at the shoulder joint: flexion, extension, and rotation of the arm." []
is_a: HP:0034430 ! Abnormal joint physiology
property_value: dc:date "2020-09-05T13:42:07Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033130
name: Abnormal renal echogenicity
synonym: "شذوذ في الصدى الكلوي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تغير في مظهر الكلى بالأشعة الصوتية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: اختلاف الصدى الكلوي عن الطبيعي عند الفحص بالأشعة الصوتية.
def: "Anomalous echogenicity of the kidney on ultrasound examination." [PMID:24235286]
comment: For diagnostic ultrasonography, high-frequency sound waves are generated and received by the ultrasonography transducer, which is placed on the skin. Returning sound waves (echoes) are processed by a computer and displayed on a computer screen. A gray-scale image is produced when the ultrasonography machine operates in B-mode, or brightness mode, in which returning echoes are represented as bright dots; the brightness of the dots represents the strength of the reflected echoes. Echogenicity, therefore, refers to how bright or dark something appears in the gray-scale image; the brighter something appears, the more echogenic it is. With regard to the kidney, echogenicity generally refers to how bright or dark the kidney parenchyma appears in comparison to the liver.
is_a: HP:0012210 ! Abnormal renal morphology
property_value: dc:date "2020-09-09T12:48:13Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033131
name: Renal medullary hyperechogenicity
synonym: "فرط الصدى في النخاع الكلوي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة الصدى في النخاع الكلوي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة صدى النخاع الكلوي.
def: "Increased echogenecity of the medullary region of the kidney." [PMID:24235286]
comment: Increased echogenicity of the kidney parenchyma results from the increased presence of material that can reflect sound waves back, thus increasing its brightness on the ultrasonography image. Because fibrous tissue (e.g., glomerulosclerosis, interstitial fibrosis) increases echogenicity, CKD is typically associated with increased echogenicity. Inflammatory infiltrates may explain the increased echogenicity that occurs with acute interstitial nephritis and GN. Proteinaceous casts are thought to cause the increased echogenicity associated with acute tubular necrosis (ATN). Calcium deposits and stones are very echogenic; thus, medullary nephrocalcinosis is characterized by increased medullary echogenicity and a relatively normal-appearing cortex. Several renal diseases are associated with medullary nephrocalcinosis, including medullary sponge kidney, hyperparathyroidism, renal tubular acidosis, and vitamin D toxicity. Other kidney diseases that have been associated with a hyperechoic medulla include sickle cell disease and gout
synonym: "Increased renal medullary echogenicity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033130 ! Abnormal renal echogenicity
property_value: dc:date "2020-09-09T12:57:19Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033132
