def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration of a short-chain fatty acid in the blood circulation." []
comment: A short-chain fatty acid is defined as n aliphatic monocarboxylic acid with a chain length of less than C6. If any non-hydrocarbon substituent is present, the compound is not normally regarded as a short-chain fatty acid.
