[Term]
id: HP:0033255
name: Congenital lobar overinflation
synonym: "التضخم الفصي الخلقي للرئة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تضخم خلقي في جزء من الرئة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تشوه خلقي يتميز بوجود جزء من الرئة في حالة تمدد مفرط، مما يؤثر على جزء أو فص بأكمله وينتج عنه تمدد متزايد في فص واحد أو أكثر.
def: "A congenital malformation characterized by an overdistended segment of lung, affecting an party of a lobe or the entire one. It results in progressive overinflation of one or more lobes." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0113-912X, PMID:31118601]
comment: Lobar overinflation is more commonly present in neonate or early infancy with life-threatening respiratory distress. The upper lobes are more frequently affected than the lower one. And more common in males (M:F = 3:1). On imaging, it classically presents on chest radiographs as a hyperlucent lung segment with overinflation and contralateral mediastinal shift.
synonym: "Congenital lobar emphysema" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002101 ! Abnormal lung lobation
property_value: dc:date "2020-11-27T19:32:15Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

