[Term]
id: HP:0033783
name: Molar incisor malformation
synonym: "تشوه القاطع الطاحني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تشوه الطواحين والقواطع" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تشوه القاطع الطاحني يتكون من تاج طبيعي مع تضيق عنق بارز، وجذور رقيقة قصيرة وجمع من العلامات التي تحدث في الأضراس اللبنية والدائمة.
def: "Molar incisor malfomation (MIM) is composed of normal crown with marked cervical constriction, thin, narrow short roots which is a combination of signs that occurs in deciduous and permanent molars." [PMID:31468724]
comment: MIM affects one or more roots of deciduous second molars and permanent first molars. Permanent maxillary central incisors may also be affected. The diagnosis requires clinical and radiographic examinations.
is_a: HP:0011070 ! Abnormal molar morphology
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-07T10:32:47Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033784
name: Dentin dysplasia
synonym: "خلل تنسجي في العاج" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مشاكل في الأسنان" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: هذا مصطلح شامل لأن خلل تنسج العاج يتضمن جذور قصيرة بأطراف حادة وتورودنتية وتكلسات داخلية باللب.
def: "This is a bundled term as dentin dysplasia is composed of short roots with pointed ends and taurodontism and intrapulpal calcifications." [PMID:31468724]
comment: This term designates a genetic condition, and an Element of Morphology rending its utilization sometimes confusing. The condition is characterized by multiple dental anomalies that affect both deciduous and permanent dentitions. It can exist in isolation or be associated with other signs and symptoms of various syndromes.
is_a: HP:0010299 ! Abnormal dentin morphology
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-07T10:38:57Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033785
name: Enamel agenesis
synonym: "عدم التكوّن في المينا" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "غياب المينا" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الغياب التام أو شبه التام للمينا.
def: "Complete or almost complete absence of enamel." [PMID:31468724]
comment: Enamel agenesis can indicate a total absence of enamel or the presence of a very thin enamel layer that is difficult to visualize during clinical examination. It may need microscopic studies to determine whether any enamel is still present. It can be present isolated and as part of rare syndromic entities.
is_a: HP:0000682 ! Abnormal dental enamel morphology
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-07T10:59:43Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033786
name: Hypomature enamel
synonym: "المينا غير الناضجة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تغير لون المينا" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: المينا ذات تلون أبيض أو بني بدون نقص التنسج.
def: "Enamel with a white or brown discoloration without hypoplasia." [PMID:31468724]
comment: Enamel maturation is a process through which enamel matrix proteins are removed to allow full growth of the enamel hydroxyapatite crystals. Hypomature enamel can be caused by genetic or environmental factors. It may occur in both deciduous and permanent dentitions, although more often in the permanent dentition. Hypomature enamel may concern a single tooth, several teeth, or the complete dentition and may affect part or the complete surface of the tooth. The enamel is usually hard, colored but not translucid. It is a qualitative defect of enamel.
synonym: "Enamel opacity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000682 ! Abnormal dental enamel morphology
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-07T11:02:43Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033787
name: Cementum hypoplasia
synonym: "نقص تنسج أو عدم تنسج في الملاط" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "غياب أو نقص الملاط" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نقص أو غياب الملاط. يثبت الملاط ألياف الرباط اللثوي بين جذر السن والعظم السنخي. يؤدي غيابه إلى فقدان الأسنان المبكر.
def: "The decrease or absence of cementum. The cementum anchors the periodontal ligament attachment fiber between the tooth root and the alveolar bone. Its absence leads to early loss of teeth." [PMID:31468724]
synonym: "Cementum aplasia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100717 ! Abnormal cementum morphology
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-07T11:07:41Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033788
name: Cementum overgrowth
synonym: "فرط ملاط" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة الملاط" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة لمادة الملاط على سطح جذر السن.
def: "Excess of cementum on the tooth root surface." [PMID:31468724]
comment: The excessive buildup of normal cementum (calcified tissue) on the roots of one or more teeth is an idiopathic, non-neoplastic condition. Cementum overgrowth may be either hyperplasia or hypertrophy of the cement; these terms can only be used if histological evidence of hypertrophy or hyperplasia have been established.
synonym: "Cementation hyperplasia" EXACT []
synonym: "Cementum hypertrophy" EXACT []
synonym: "Cementum overdeveloped" EXACT []
synonym: "Drumstick-shaped root" EXACT []
synonym: "Hypercementosis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100717 ! Abnormal cementum morphology
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-07T11:08:51Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033789
name: Triggered by cheese ingestion
synonym: "محفز بتناول الجبن" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تفاقم بسبب الجبن" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ينطبق على علامة أو عرض يتم تحفيزه أو يحدث نتيجة تناول الجبن.
def: "Applies to a sign or symptom that is provoked or brought about by eating cheese." [PMID:9398858]
comment: Cheese contains tyramine, which is thought to be responsible for tachycardia and hypertension that can be tirggered by eating cheese in persons with Trimethylaminuria.
is_a: HP:0033793 ! Triggered by food ingestion
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-07T11:11:07Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033790
name: Thistle tube shaped pulp
synonym: "لب بشكل أنبوب الشوكة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "توسع غير طبيعي لللب" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شكل غرفة اللب على هيئة أنبوب الشوكة، مما يعني وجود غرفة لب تاجية متضخمة مع قنوات لب ضيقة تعطي مظهراً أشعاعياً بشكل أنبوب الشوكة أو اللهب. قد تحدث بشكل معزول أو مرتبطة بعيوب أخرى في الأسنان وأمراض نادرة مثل تكوّن عاج غير مكتمل، والتي يجب تقييمها وتشفيرها بشكل منفصل. يعتمد تشخيص لب بشكل أنبوب الشوكة على الفحوصات السريرية والشعاعية.
def: "A thistle tube shape of the pulp chamber, meaning an enlarged coronal pulp chamber with narrow pulp canals giving a radiographic appearance of the shape of a thistle tube or a flame. It may occur isolated or associated with other dental anomalies and rare diseases such as dentinogenesis imperfecta, which should be assessed and coded separately. The diagnosis thistle tube shape pulp requires clinical and radiographic examinations." [PMID:31468724]
synonym: "Flame-shaped pulp" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0006479 ! Abnormal dental pulp morphology
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-07T11:14:26Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033791
name: Tooth ankylosis
synonym: "التصاق السن بالعظم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "التحام السن بالعظم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: التحام السن مع العظم السنخي.
def: "Fusion of a tooth with alveolar bone." [PMID:31468724]
comment: Ankylosis is uncommon in the deciduous dentition and very rare in the permanent dentition. It may be observed after trauma. Ankylosis may occur at the crown or root level.
is_a: HP:0006482 ! Abnormal dental morphology
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-07T11:24:36Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033792
name: Cross bite
synonym: "العضة المعكوسة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "اضطراب تراكب الأسنان" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الإطباق اللساني للسفوح الخدية و/أو حافة القواطع للأسنان العلوية إلى السفوح الخدية و/أو حافة القواطع للأسنان السفلية.
def: "Lingual occlusion of buccal cusps and/or incisal edge of maxillary teeth to the buccal cusps and/or incisal edge of mandibular teeth." [PMID:31468724]
comment: Cross bite may occur unilaterally, bilaterally, or frontally. A total cross bite with buccal displacement of the maxillary posterior teeth, with or without contact between the lingual surface of the maxillary lingual cusp and the buccal surface of the buccal cusp of its mandibular antagonist, has been called scissor bite. If only a single tooth is affected, the term single cross bite can be used.
is_a: HP:0000692 ! Tooth malposition
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-07T11:30:03Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033793
name: Triggered by food ingestion
synonym: "يُحفز بسبب تناول الطعام" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "يحدث بسبب الأكل" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ينطبق على علامة أو عرض يثيره أو يسببه تناول طعام معين.
def: "Applies to a sign or symptom that is provoked or brought about by eating a certain food." []
is_a: HP:0025204 ! Triggered by
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-07T17:28:49Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033794
name: Acral overgrowth
synonym: "نمو الأطراف الزائد" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تضخم اليدين والقدمين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمو مفرط في اليدين والقدمين (يعود بشكل رئيسي إلى تضخم الأنسجة الرخوة). تشمل المظاهر النموذجية زيادة حجم الحذاء، وتضخم القدم، وضيق القفازات، وتضخم اليد.
def: "Excessive growth of hands and feet (predominantly due to soft tissue swelling). Typical manifestations include shoe size increase, foot enlargement, glove tightness, and hand enlargement." [PMID:27477558, PMID:27812777, PMID:30853479]
comment: This term should be used to encode the overgrowth of hands and feet that can be seen in acromegaly, a rare disorder caused by excessive growth hormone production, most commonly from an adenoma of the anterior pituitary gland. The resulting production of insulin-like growth factor 1 causes the characteristic overgrowth of certain tissues resulting in coarsening of facial features, enlarging hands and feet, as well as effects on multiple systems throughout the body. The Figure in PMID:30853479 illustrates large hands with stubby fingers characteristic of acromegaly.
synonym: "Acral enlargement" EXACT []
synonym: "Acral hypertrophy" EXACT []
synonym: "Acromegalic growth" EXACT []
synonym: "Acromegaly" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0001507 ! Growth abnormality
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-08T12:21:48Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033795
name: Growth without growth hormone
synonym: "النمو بدون هرمون النمو" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "النمو بلا هرمون النمو" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: النمو الذي يحدث في الجسم بدون الحاجة إلى إفراز هرمون النمو.
comment: Growth hormone (GH) is essential for normal growth. However, cases of normal growth without GH may occur. The mechanism of growth without GH remains still unclear. However, regarding normal growth without GH arising after brain surgery, hypothalamic damage caused by the brain surgery is thought to induce obesity, and the resulting hyperinsulinemia and/or hyperprolactinemia are assumed to be important mechanisms of normal growth without GH in postsurgery patients. It is assumed that elevated insulin and/or prolactin concentration normalize IGF-1 levels even in GHD patients, restricts the increase in serum levels of IGFBP-3, and changes the distribution of circulating IGF-1. Thus, normal growth without GH continues because of the effects of IFG-I, which are independent of GH. {xref="PMID:28443260"}
is_a: HP:0001507 ! Growth abnormality
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-09T11:28:27Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033796
name: Abnormal leukocyte physiology
synonym: "خلل فسيولوجيا الكريات البيضاء" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في وظيفة خلايا الدم البيضاء" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل وظيفي في خلايا الدم البيضاء.
def: "A functional abnormality of a white blood cell." []
is_a: HP:0001871 ! Abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues
is_a: HP:0010978 ! Abnormality of immune system physiology
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-08T13:50:44Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0033797
name: Leukocyte migration defect
synonym: "خلل في هجرة الكريات البيضاء" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مشكلة في حركة الكريات البيضاء" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أي خلل في حركة الكريات البيضاء استجابةً للمواد الكيميائية الجاذبة، وهو ضروري للاستجابة الالتهابية للعدوى، ولتطور الأعضاء، واستقرار الأنسجة، والتوعية.
def: "Any abnormality of leukocyte motility in response to chemokines, which is required for the inflammatory response to infections, and for organ development, tissues homeostasis, and vascularization." []
synonym: "Abnormal leukocyte migration" EXACT []
synonym: "Defects of leukocyte migration" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033796 ! Abnormal leukocyte physiology
property_value: dc:date "2021-05-08T13:51:57Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

