[Term]
id: HP:0034050
name: Elevated urinary prostaglandin E2 metabolite level
synonym: "زيادة مستوى نواتج بروستاجلاندين E2 في البول" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ارتفاع نواتج بروستاجلاندين E2 في البول" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة كمية نواتج البروستاجلاندين E2 (PGE-M) في البول.
def: "An increased amount of prostaglandin E2 metabolite (PGE-M) in the urine." [PMID:28700713]
comment: In vivo, PGE2 is rapidly converted to its 13,14-dihydro-15-keto metabolite, with more than 90% of circulating PGE2 cleared by a single passage through the lungs. This metabolite is chemically unstable and undergoes a variable amount of degradation to prostaglandin A (PGA) products. Thus, plasma and urine samples from patients actually contain very little intact PGE2, and the PGE2 metabolites (PGEM) can be measured to provide a more reliable estimate of actual PGE2 production.
is_a: HP:0003527 ! Hyperprostaglandinuria
property_value: dc:date "2021-10-19T16:57:43Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

