[Term]
id: HP:0034180
name: Fusion of the caudate and putamen
synonym: "الالتحام بين النواة الذنبية والمخطط" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "التحام في الدماغ" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ظهور غير طبيعي للالتحام بين النواة الذنبية والمخطط مع غياب الطرف الأمامي للكبسولة الداخلية.
def: "Abnormal joined appearance of the caudate and putamen with an absence of the anterior limb of the internal capsule." [PMID:26251641, PMID:31194327]
comment: The putamen, combined with the globus pallidus, forms the lentiform nucleus; and with the caudate nucleus, it shapes the striatum, which is a subcortical structure that forms the basal ganglia.
