def: "Lack of development of lanugo, the fine, soft, unpigmented hair on the body of a fetus or newborn baby." [PMID:26119818, PMID:30252348]
comment: Lanugo arises about three months into development and plays an essential role in binding the vernix caseosa to the skin of fetuses.
