[Term]
id: HP:0034299
name: Sertoli cell-only phenotype
synonym: "النمط الظاهري لخلايا سرتولي فقط" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وجود خلايا سرتولي فقط في الخصية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمط ظاهري نسيجي يُلاحظ في خزعة الخصية حيث تبطن خلايا سرتولي فقط الأنابيب المنوية في الخصية.
def: "A histological phenotype observed on testicular biopsy in which only Sertoli cells line the seminiferous tubules of the testis." [PMID:30484998]
comment: Sertoli cells are found in the convoluted seminiferous tubules and form part of the blood-testis barrier in males. With Sertoli cell-only phenotype, spermatogenic cells, which are normally located in between the Seroli cells, are absent.
