def: "The concentration of prekallikrein in the blood circulation is below the lower limit of normal." []
comment: Prekallikrein (PK; also known as Fletcher factor) is the precursor of plasma kallikrein, a serine protease that activates kinins. PK is cleaved to produce kallikrein by activated Factor XII. Most cases of prekallikrein deficiency are asymptomatic.
