comment: Arabic Definition: يكون تركيز الجلوبيولين المرتبط بالثيروكسين (TBG) في الدورة الدموية أقل من الحد الأدنى الطبيعي.
alt_id: HP:0012509
def: "The concentration of thyroxine-binding globulin (TBG) in the blood circulation is below the lower limit of normal." []
comment: Thyroxin-binding globulin (TBG) is known as serpin peptidase inhibitor, clade A (alpha-1 antiproteinase, antitrypsin), member 7 (SERPINA7), Entrez Gene ID 6906. Individuals with TBG deficiency are euthyroid. TBG is responsible for carrying the thyroid hormones thyroxine (T4) and 3,5,3'-triiodothyronine (T3) in the bloodstream.
synonym: "Reduced thyroxin-binding globulin" EXACT []
synonym: "Thyroxine-binding globulin low in blood" EXACT []
