property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0034790
name: Abnormal muscle succinate dehydrogenase staining
synonym: "شذوذ صبغ مستخلص السكسينات ديهيدروجينيز في العضلات" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في صبغ العضلات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أي انحراف عن الكمية الطبيعية لصبغ إنزيم السكسينات ديهيدروجينيز في أنسجة العضلات الهيكلية، والتي يمكن أن تعكس خللاً في نشاط الإنزيم.
def: "Any deviation from the normal amount of staining of succinate dehydrogenase in skeletal muscle tissue." [PMID:27556822]
comment: Succinate dehydrogenase (SDH) is a mitochondrial enzyme complex located in the inner mitochondrial membrane that has dual roles in the oxidation of succinate to fumarate in the Krebs cycle and in electron transport during oxidative phosphorylation.
is_a: HP:0034510 ! Abnormal muscle tissue enzyme activity or level
property_value: dc:date "2023-06-12T13:36:22Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0034791
