synonym: "تقلص انكماشي للدوران الخارجي في الكتف" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تقلص في الكتف" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من تقلصات الكتف يتميز بانخفاض دوران الكتف الداخلي، أي بتقليل مزمن في القدرة الفعلية والسلبية على تدوير عظم العضد داخلياً عند مفصل الكتف.
def: "A type of shoulder contracture characterized by decreased internal rotation of shoulder, that is, by a chronic reduction in active and passive ability to internally rotate the humerus at the shoulder joint (if the arm is flexed at the elbow, Internal rotation of the shoulder rotates the forearm towards the center of the body)." []
synonym: "External rotation contracture of the shoulder joint" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034665 ! Shoulder contracture
property_value: dc:date "2023-07-18T17:32:50Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0034992
name: Thumb adduction contracture
synonym: "تقلص انكماشي في إبهام اليد عند التقريب" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تقلص في الإبهام" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من تقلصات الإبهام يتميز بانخفاض مزمن في القدرة الفعلية والسلبية لمفاصل الميتاكاربال-فالنجي أو الإنتربالانجي في الإبهام على العودة من الجانب الأوسط إلى الموضع المحايد.
def: "A type of thumb contracture characterized by a chronic reduction in active and passive ability of the metacarpal-phalangeal and/or interphalangeal joints of the thumb to bring from medial side to neutral position, where the neutral position for the thumb is when the distal and proximal segments of the thumb joint are in linear alignment." []
is_a: HP:0009600 ! Thumb contracture
property_value: dc:date "2023-07-18T17:41:33Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:0034993
name: Hip internal rotation contracture
synonym: "تقلص انكماشي للدوران الداخلي في الورك" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تقلص في الورك" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدم القدرة على تدوير الجزء العلوي من الطرف العلوي lateralial past anatomic neutral move away from the midline, when viewed from the outside.
def: "The inability to rotate the proximal or upper limb segment laterally past anatomic neutral moving away from the midline, when viewed from anteriorly. Anatomic neutral position is defined as the trans-epicondylar axis of the distal humerus (for upper extremity) or femur (for lower extremity) is parallel to the sagittal plane of the body. This type of contracture is characterized by a turning of the knee from a neutral position to one facing more the midline, where the neutral position for the hip is with knee pointing directly anteriorly (less than or equal to 45 degrees)." []
is_a: HP:0003273 ! Hip contracture
property_value: dc:date "2023-07-18T17:59:08Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

