[Term]
id: HP:0040049
name: Macular edema
synonym: "وذمة بقعية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تورم في البقعة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة في سماكة شبكية العين نتيجة تجمع السوائل خارج الخلايا في البقعة استجابة لانحلال حاجز الدم في الشبكية. قد يكون له مظهر كيسي في الحفرة أو مظهر أكثر انتشارًا.
def: "Thickening of the retina that takes place due to accumulation of extracellular fluid in the macula as a nonspecific response to blood-retinal barrier breakdown. It can either have a cystoid aspect in the fovea, or a more diffuse aspect." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123, PMID:35015421]
comment: Macular edema is a common pathological response to a wide variety of ocular insults, most commonly after intraocular (e.g. cataract) surgery or in association with retinal vascular (e.g. diabetic eye disease, retinal vein occlusion) or inflammatory (e.g. uveitis) disease.
synonym: "Macular oedema" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:37231002
xref: UMLS:C0271051
is_a: HP:0030498 ! Macular thickening
is_a: HP:0031527 ! Retinal edema
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399

