[Term]
id: HP:0040200
name: Motor impersistence
synonym: "عدم الثبات الحركي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدم قدرة على الثبوت في الحركة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عدم القدرة على الحفاظ على الوضعيات أو الحركات (مثل إغلاق العيون، مد اللسان، الحفاظ على نظرة متصلة في اتجاه ثابت، أو إصدار صوت 'آه' مطول) باستمرار دون تذكير.
def: "The inability to maintain postures or positions (such as keeping eyes closed, protruding the tongue, maintaining conjugate gaze steadily in a fixed direction, or making a prolonged 'ah' sound) without repeated prompts." [DOI:10.1007/978-0-387-79948-3_2046, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754]
comment: Damage to premotor and prefrontal regions results in motor-intentional disorders that disrupt initiation, maintenance, and termination of volitional movements. Motor impersistence (i.e., failure to maintain movement) more frequently develops following right than left hemisphere lesions. {xref="PMID:17353476", xref="DOI:10.1007/978-0-387-79948-3_2046", xref="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199"}
synonym: "Negative chorea" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754]
xref: UMLS:C4073148
is_a: HP:0011443 ! Abnormality of coordination
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754

[Term]
id: HP:0040201
name: Simultanapraxia
synonym: "عدم الثبات الحركي المتزامن" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "صعوبة القيام بحركات متزامنة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوع من عدم الثبات الحركي، يُعرّف كعدم القدرة على أداء أكثر من عمليتين إراديتين بسيطتين في الوقت نفسه، مثل إغلاق العيون ومد اللسان.
def: "A subset of motor impersistence, defined as the inability to perform more than two of the simple voluntary acts simultaneously, such as closing the eyes and protruding the tongue." [DOI:10.1007/978-0-387-79948-3_2046, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754]
xref: UMLS:C4073149
is_a: HP:0040200 ! Motor impersistence
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754

