[Term]
id: HP:0040297
name: Preauricular cyst
synonym: "كيس ما قبل الأذن" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "كيس أمام الأذن" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: كيس تحت الجلد يتكون بالقرب من حافة الأذن ويتصل بالغضروف التراجي.
def: "Preauricular sinus is an occasional finding and most frequently appears as a small pit close to the anterior margin of the ascending portion of the helix. The opening has also been reported along the postero superior margin of the helix, the tragus or the lobule. Preauricular sinus may lead to the formation of a subcutaneous cyst that is intimately related to the tragal cartilage and the anterior crus of the helix." [PMID:24427573]
