[Term]
id: HP:0200146
name: Mucoid extracellular matrix accumulation
synonym: "تراكم المصفوفة خارج الخلوية المخاطية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تجمع من المادة المخاطية بين الأنسجة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة في المصفوفة خارج الخلوية المخاطية للطبقة الوسيطة، مما يؤدي إلى توسعات عبر الطبقة أو بين الطبقات تشمل تجمعات خارج الخلية، كما يلاحظ في صبغة H&E و/أو صبغة تبرز مادة المصفوفة خارج الخلوية (مثل Movat's pentachrome و Alcian blue).
def: "An increase of medial mucoid extracellular matrix creating translamellar and/or intralamellar expansions including extracellular pools as noted on an H&E stain and/or a stain to highlight extracellular matrix material (Movat's pentachrome, Alcian blue, etc.)." [PMID:27031798]
comment: MEMA replaces a variety of terms used in the past such as cystic medial necrosis, cystonecrosis, cystic degeneration, mucoid degeneration which, while generally understood by pathologists, are inaccurate. This histopathology can be subclassified and graded according to distribution, severity, and/or whether it crosses over multiple lamellar units as described. The grading should be reported as mild/moderate/severe and the distribution should be reported as focal, multifocal, or extensive.
synonym: "Cystic medial necrosis of the aorta" EXACT []
synonym: "MEMA" EXACT abbreviation []
