[Term]
id: HP:0430104
name: Abnormal superficial temporal artery morphology
synonym: "شذوذ في شكل الشريان الصدغي السطحي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شكل غير طبيعي للشريان على الجبهة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أي شذوذ هيكلي في الشريان الصدغي السطحي الذي ينشأ من الشريان السباتي الخارجي ويمر فوق العظم الوجني. يقع الشريان الصدغي السطحي على الأجزاء السطحية من الجبهة وجوانب الرأس والوجه.
def: "Any structural abnormality of a superficial temporal artery, originating from the external carotid artery and passing over the zygomatic process. The superficial temporal artery is located on the superficial parts of the forehead and sides of the head and face." []
is_a: HP:0011004 ! Abnormal systemic arterial morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T08:08:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0430105
name: Skip lesions on temporal artery biopsy
synonym: "آفات قافزة في خزع شريان الصدغي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "التهاب متقطع في شريان الرأس" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: التهاب بقعي في شريان الصدغي السطحي يشكل بؤراً معزولة من التهاب الشرايين.
def: "Patchy inflammation of the superficial temporal artery, forming isolated foci of arteritis." [PMID:10767830, PMID:950804]
comment: This feature may be observed in temporal arteritis. The foci are characterized by mononuclear cell infiltrates or a granulomatous process with multinucleated giant cells.
is_a: HP:0430104 ! Abnormal superficial temporal artery morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T08:13:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0430106
name: Abnormal brain-evoked potentials
synonym: "اضطراب الجهود الدماغية المستثارة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "اضطراب في الإشارات الدماغية المحفزة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: أي شذوذ في الجهود الدماغية المستثارة، وهي جهود تُنتجها محفزات خارجية تعكس نشاطًا متزامنًا لمجموعة من الأعصاب والمحاور العصبية في الجهاز العصبي المركزي نتيجة لوصول النبضات العصبية بعد تحفيز العصب الطرفي أو مستقبلاته. اعتمادًا على نوع المحفز، تُصنّف الجهود المستثارة إلى بصرية (VEP)، سمعية (AEP)، أو حسية جسدية (SSEP). تحدث الجهود الحركية المستثارة (MEP) عند تحفيز منطقة الحركة في الدماغ. تنتج هذه الجهود عن تنشيط عدد كافٍ من الوحدات الحركية.
def: "Any anomaly of brain-evoked potentials, defined as potentials generated by exteroceptive stimuli reflect synchronized activity by neuronal and axonal groups in the central nervous system (CNS) resulting from the arrival of nerve impulses after stimulation of a peripheral nerve or its receptors. Depending on the type of stimulus, evoked potentials are categorized as visual (VEP), auditory (AEP), or somatosensory (SSEP). Motor evoked potentials (MEP) occur when the brain's motor area is stimulated. They result from the activation of a sufficient number of motor units." [PMID:22995526]
is_a: HP:0030178 ! Abnormality of central nervous system electrophysiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T17:19:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0430107
name: Sputum infectious agent
synonym: "العامل المعدي في البلغم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "جراثيم في البلغم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود عامل معدي في البلغم، وذلك كما يتبين من خلال زراعة البلغم أو من خلال تحقيقات أخرى.
def: "The presence of an infectious agent in the sputum, as characterized by sputum culture or other investigation." [PMID:33085342]
is_a: HP:0430151 ! Positive respiratory tract infectious agent test
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T17:56:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0430108
name: Positive Mycobacterium avium sputum culture
synonym: "زراعة بلغم إيجابية للمتفطرة الطيرية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وجود المتفطرة الطيرية في البلغم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمو المتفطرة الطيرية في زراعة البلغم.
def: "Growth of mycobacterium avium in a sputum culture." [PMID:8996008]
comment: Mycobacterium avium-intracellulare complex (MAC) is a ubiquitous environmental microorganism whose pathogenicity ranges from innocuous colonization to disease, in immunocompetent as well as immunocompromised individuals.
is_a: HP:0430107 ! Sputum infectious agent
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T17:58:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0430109
name: Positive bloodstream infectious agent antigen test
synonym: "اختبار إيجابي لمستضد العامل المعدي في مجرى الدم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وجود مستضد عامل معدي في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نتيجة اختبار تُظهر وجود مستضد (علامة مثل بروتين يتفاعل معه الجسم المضاد) خاص بعامل معدي.
def: "A test result demonstrating the presence of an antigen (marker such as a protein against which an antibody reacts) specific to an infectious agent." []
is_a: HP:0430150 ! Positive blood infectious agent test
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-20T09:00:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0430110
name: Positive bloodstream Cysticercosis antigen test
synonym: "اختبار إيجابي لمستضد داء الكيسات في مجرى الدم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وجود مستضد داء الكيسات في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: إظهار مستضد خاص بداء الكيسات في مجرى الدم.
def: "Demonstration of an antigen specific to Cysticercosis in the bloodstream." [PMID:23265553]
comment: Cysticercosis, the infection with the larval stage of Taenia solium, is a cause of neurological symptoms including seizures.
is_a: HP:0430109 ! Positive bloodstream infectious agent antigen test
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-20T09:04:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0430111
name: Klazomania
synonym: "كلازومانيا" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "نوبات صراخ لاإرادي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نوبات لاإرادية من الصراخ بشكل قسري ونوبات. قد تكون التصرفات الصراخية عالية جدًا وغير مرتبطة بالحالة العقلية الجارية للشخص المصاب. قد تحدث نوبات الصراخ في فترات وتستمر لعدة ساعات.
def: "Involuntary attacks of compulsive paroxysmal shouting. The shouting behaviors may be extremely loud and not related to the ongoing mental state of the affected individual. Shouting episodes may occur in bouts and last for several hours." [PMID:31651053]
is_a: HP:4000074 ! Involuntary vocalization
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-22T06:16:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0430112
name: Coprolalia
synonym: "كوبروفيليا" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "الصراخ بألفاظ نابية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تشير الكوبروفيليا إلى النطق اللاإرادي بألفاظ نابية. يعد القصد عاملًا مهماً في تصنيف السلوكيات المُصَنفة ككوبروفيلية، ولسوء الحظ، لا يزال من غير الواضح كيفية التميز بشكل موضوعي بين الكوبروفيليا والسب العادي.
def: "Coprolalia denotes the involuntary utterance of obscenities. Intent is an important classifier in coprolalic behaviors, and unfortunately it remains unclear how to objectively distinguish coprolalia from common swearing." []
comment: In Tourette syndrome (TS), the unintended expression of coprolalic behaviors is encountered in about one-fifth of patients. Typical coprolalic behaviors in TS are characterized by the utterance of single short obscenities (e.g., in English, so-called four-letter words) with a different pitch or tone from ongoing speech. There have been only a few reports of patients exhibiting coprolalia in other neurological conditions, such as neurodevelopmental disorders (e.g., Kleine-Levin and fragile X syndrome), neurodegenerative syndromes (e.g., FTD, Alzheimer's disease, and chorea-acanthocytosis), after focal brain lesions, in encephalitis lethargica, or as ictal phenomenon.
is_a: HP:4000074 ! Involuntary vocalization
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-22T06:21:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0430113
name: Continuous involuntary vocalizations
synonym: "التلفظات اللاإرادية المستمرة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "أصوات مستمرة غير إرادية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الأصوات المستمرة مثل الأنين، الشكاء، الشخير، والصراخ.
def: "Continuous groaning, moaning, grunting, and shrieking." [PMID:31651053]
comment: Continuous involuntary vocalizations are most frequently associated with neurodegenerative diseases. in dementias, such as Alzheimer's disease and Huntington disease, continuous involuntary vocalizations, often labeled as vocally disruptive behavior, are part of a spectrum of behavioral symptoms that correlate with the severity of cognitive impairment and may be exacerbated with emotional arousal. Purposeless noisemaking, for example, groaning or howling in parkinsonism may also be encountered.
is_a: HP:4000074 ! Involuntary vocalization
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-22T06:24:32Z" xsd:dateTime

