[Term]
id: HP:5200028
name: Reduced responsiveness to social cues
synonym: "انخفاض الاستجابة للإشارات الاجتماعية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "قلة الاستجابة للإشارات الاجتماعية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ميل لإظهار استجابات للإشارات الاجتماعية تعتبر (مثلًا من قبل أفراد الأسرة، الزملاء، أو مقدمي الرعاية) بأنها أقل مما هو متوقع بناءً على المرحلة التطورية والسياق الثقافي للفرد.
alt_id: HP:5200036
alt_id: HP:5200053
alt_id: HP:5200054
def: "A tendency to display responces to social cues that are interpreted (e.g., by family members, peers, or caregivers) as diminished compared to what would be expected based on the developmental stage and cultural context of an individual." []
comment: This term describes a behavioral abnormality and does not apply if the lack of response is assessed to be due to hearing impairment or intellectual disability.
synonym: "Lack of response to verbal cues" NARROW []
synonym: "Reduced response to social cues" EXACT []
synonym: "Reduced responsiveness to verbal cues" NARROW []
is_a: HP:0012760 ! Reduced social responsiveness
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9112-5148
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6670-9157
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9593-5508

[Term]
id: HP:5200029
name: Social disinhibition
synonym: "نزع المحظورات الاجتماعية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "التصرف بدون كبح اجتماعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ميل لخرق القواعد الاجتماعية نتيجة لفشل في مقاومة الإغراءات أو الرغبات في البيئات الاجتماعية.
def: "A tendency to violate social norms because of a failure to resist temptations or urges in social settings." [PMID:27696753]
comment: A tendency to social disinhibition can be acquired after traumatic brain injury and may be described as insensitivity to others. Manifestions of social disinhibition may include (1) insertion of poorly considered utterances including insensitive remarks,overly intimate information, sexual references, and swear words, (2) failure to adhereto the rules of discourse leading to poor turn-taking, excessive side tracks, off topics,and talking too much, and (3) speaking from an egocentric perspective, that is,lacking concern, selfishness, childishness, arguing, not getting along with others.
is_a: HP:0000734 ! Disinhibition
is_a: HP:5200123 ! Abnormal response to social norms
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9112-5148
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6670-9157
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9593-5508

[Term]
id: HP:5200030
name: Diminished integration of verbal and non-verbal communicative behavior
synonym: "انخفاض تكامل السلوك التواصلي اللفظي وغير اللفظي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انخفاض التكامل في التواصل" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: اضطراب تواصلي حيث يكون التواصل اللفظي وغير اللفظي مندمجان بشكل ضعيف. قد يحدث ذلك عندما يكون كل من التواصل اللفظي وغير اللفظي سليمين لوحدهم لكن يحدث شذوذ عند استخدامهم معاً، أو وجود شذوذ في استخدام النموذج النموذجي المتكامل مثل استخدام الإيماءات التوضيحية أثناء الكلام.
def: "A communicative abnormality where one's nonverbal and verbal communication are poorly integrated. This may occur when verbal and nonverbal communication are intact alone but are abnormal when used together, or an abnormality in the use of typically integrated communication such as the use of beat gestures during speech." []
is_a: HP:0034434 ! Abnormal communication
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9112-5148
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6670-9157
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9593-5508

