[Term]
id: HP:5200101
name: Limited Repertoire of gestures
synonym: "نطاق محدود من الإيماءات" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "قلة الإيماءات" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: استخدام محدود للإيماءات في التواصل، مما قد يؤثر على الفهم المتبادل مع الآخرين.
is_a: HP:4000090 ! Abnormal gesture use

[Term]
id: HP:5200102
name: Reduced social smiling
synonym: "تراجع الابتسام الاجتماعي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "قلة الابتسام" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: قلة إنتاج الابتسامات أثناء التفاعل مع والد، مقدم رعاية، أو الأقران.
def: "Reduced production of smiles during engagement with an interactive parent, caregiver, or peer." [PMID:17682330]
comment: In typical development, smiling is one of the most commonly observed social behaviors during the first 6 months of life. Most babies begin to smile by the age of about 2 months.
is_a: HP:0012434 ! Delayed early-childhood social milestone development
is_a: HP:0012760 ! Reduced social responsiveness

