id: HP:6000003
name: History of mastectomy
synonym: "تاريخ استئصال الثدي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "إزالة الثدي جراحياً في السابق" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تاريخ مرضي سابق لإزالة الثدي جراحياً.
def: "Past medical history of surgical breast removal." []
is_a: HP:0430103 ! Past surgical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10211
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000004
name: Lymphangiosarcoma
synonym: "لمفانجيوساركوما" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "سرطان الأوعية اللمفاوية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ورم خبيث ينشأ من الخلايا البطانية للأوعية اللمفاوية.
def: "A malignant neoplasm arising from the endothelial cells of the lymphatic vessels." [PMID:22682884]
is_a: HP:0012797 ! Lymphatic vessel neoplasm
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10212
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000005
name: Exposure to inhaled lipids
synonym: "التعرض للدهون المستنشقة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "استنشاق الدهون" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: شفط أو استنشاق منتجات تحتوي على دهون.
def: "Aspiration or inhalation of lipid-containing products." []
comment: Exogenous lipoid pneumonia is caused by aspiration or inhalation of lipid-containing products. In the past, the most common agents included mineral oil-based laxatives and nasal decongestants. Other causes include inhalation of petroleum jelly used as a lubricant, e.g., tracheostomy care. The incidence of exogenous lipoid pneumonia is growing exponentially in all age groups secondary to the phenomenon termed vaping. In the latter case, consider the term Electronic cigarette exposure histor (HP:0430032).
is_a: HP:4000110 ! Exposure history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10216
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000006
name: Holster sign
synonym: "علامة مسدس" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تغير لون الجلد في الفخذين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: حالة جلدية تتميز بظهور البويكيلوديرما متماثلة في الوركين والفخذين الجانبيين أسفل المدور الكبير.
def: "Symmetric poikiloderma of hips and lateral thighs below the greater trochanter." [PMID:31279808, PMID:32644343]
comment: The Holster sign may indicate dermatomyositis.
is_a: HP:0001029 ! Poikiloderma
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10223
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000007
name: Salivary basal cell adenoma
synonym: "ورم غدي قاعدي للعاب" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ورم نادر في الغدد اللعابية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ورم نادر يتكون من مجموعة من الخلايا الظهارية القاعدية متجانسة، ويمثل حوالي 1-2٪ من جميع أورام الغدة اللعابية.
def: "A rare neoplasm consisting of a monomorphic population of basaloid epithelial cells, and it accounts for approximately 1-2% of all salivary gland tumors." [PMID:26693465]
comment: Thee most frequent location of basal cell adenoma (BCA) of the salivary gland is the parotid gland. It usually appears as a firm and mobile slow-growing mass. Histologically, isomorphic cells in nests and interlaced trabecules with a prominent basal membrane are observed. In contrast to pleomorphic adenoma, it tends to be multiple and its recurrence rate after surgical excision is high.
is_a: HP:0100684 ! Salivary gland neoplasm
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10195
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000008
name: Hemidiaphragm elevation
synonym: "شذوذ نصف الحجاب الحاجز المرتفع" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ارتفاع أحد جانبي الحجاب الحاجز" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: حالة يكون فيها جزء واحد من الحجاب الحاجز أعلى من الآخر، وتحدث عندما يضعف أحد جانبي الحجاب الحاجز بسبب مرض عضلي أو فقدان التعصيب بسبب إصابة العصب الحجابي.
def: "Elevated Hemidiaphragm is a condition where one portion of the diaphragm is higher than the other. Elevated hemidiaphragm occurs when one side of the diaphragm becomes weak from muscular disease or loss of innervation due to phrenic nerve injury." [PMID:32644681]
synonym: "Elevated hemidiaphragm" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0040045 ! Abnormal hemidiaphragm morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10206
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000009
name: Cerebriform connective tissue nevus
synonym: "وحمة النسيج الضام الدماغية الشكل" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وحمة جلدية على باطن القدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تعد الوحمة النسيجية الضامة الدماغية الشكل واحدة من أكثر العلامات الجلدية تميزًا. غالبًا ما تظهر على باطن القدمين، وتسبب مشاكل بسبب الألم، الحكة، العدوى، النزيف، الإفراز، الرائحة، وصعوبة المشي.
def: "The cerebriform connective tissue nevus (CCTN) is one of the most characteristic skin findings. It commonly occurs on the soles of the feet, and frequently causes problems because of pain, pruritus, infection, bleeding,exudation, odor, and walking impairment." [PMID:20709429]
comment: The cerebriform connective tissue nevus is frequently observed in patients with Proteus syndrome and it is an important specific criterion for diagnosis.
is_a: HP:0003549 ! Abnormality of connective tissue
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10194
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727

[Term]
id: HP:6000010
name: Linear Hyperpigmentation along Blaschko's lines
synonym: "تصبغ خطي مفرط على طول خطوط بلاشك" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خطوط داكنة على الجلد" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خيوط وخطوط متعرجة من التصبغ المفرط البقعي على طول خطوط بلاشك.
def: "Linear streaks and swirls of macular hyperpigmentation along the lines of Blaschko." [PMID:33447068]
comment: Blaschko's lines are attributed to the migration lines of epidermal cells during embryogenesis and are characterized by a V-shaped pattern on the posterior midline, S-shape on the abdomen, and spiral on the posterior scalp.
is_a: HP:0007546 ! Linear hyperpigmentation
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10183
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000011
name: Guilt
synonym: "الشعور بالذنب" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "الشعور بالتقصير" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: التجربة الشخصية للشعور بالندم أو لوم الذات أو الإحساس بالمسؤولية عن نتيجة غير مرغوبة سواء كانت حقيقية أو متخيلة. قد يكون الشعور بالذنب متناسبًا مع الموقف أو غير متناسب، وقد يحدث في غياب عمل أو حدث أو مخالفة محددة. يعكس الذنب التفاعل بين العمليات العقلية مثل الأحكام حول المسؤولية والاستجابات العاطفية، ما قد يؤدي إلى اجترار أو انشغال دائم. قد يمتد الذنب إلى مواقف خارج سيطرة الفرد وقد يكون مصحوبًا بمعتقدات غير دقيقة أو مبالغ فيها حول دور الفرد في النتيجة.
def: "The experience of remorse, self-reproach, or perceived culpability for a real or perceived unfavorable outcome. Guilt may be proportionate to the context or disproportionate, and it may occur in the absence of an identifiable act, event, or offense. It reflects the interplay of cognitive processes, such as judgments about responsibility, and emotional responses, which can lead to persistent rumination or preoccupation. Guilt may extend to situations outside the individual's control and, in some cases, be accompanied by inaccurate or exaggerated beliefs about one's role in an outcome." [PMID:20451312, PMID:8204541]
comment: The individuals frequently feel they have violated their own, or universal, moral standards. Guilt often reflects a relationship between disordered thinking or cognitive processes (such as cognitive distortions) and emotional dysregulation resulting in persistent ruminations or preoccupations of remorse and shame. In severe cases, guilt may be associated with delusional beliefs, as seen in psychotic depression.
synonym: "Excessive self-reproach" EXACT []
synonym: "Feelings of worthlessness" RELATED layperson []
synonym: "Inappropriate sense of responsibility" BROAD []
synonym: "Obsessive remorse over imagined wrongs" NARROW []
synonym: "Remorse" EXACT []
synonym: "Self-blame" BROAD []
synonym: "Unfounded sense of culpability" BROAD []
synonym: "Unrealistic self-blame" NARROW []
synonym: "Unwarranted self-blame" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031467 ! Dysregulated negative emotional state
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10185
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4422-1708

[Term]
id: HP:6000012
name: Mediastinal shift
synonym: "انحراف المنصف" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تحرك القلب والرئتين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: انحراف المنصف عن موقعه الطبيعي في خط منتصف تجويف الصدر. المنصف هو جزء من تجويف الصدر الذي يحتوي على القلب وأوعيته الدموية والمريء والقصبة الهوائية والغدة الزعترية بالإضافة إلى الأعصاب والعقد الليمفاوية.
def: "A deviation of the mediastinum from its normal position in the midline of the thoracic cavity. The mediastinum is a compartment of the thoracic cavity that contains the heart and its blood vessels, the esophagus, trachea, thymus, as well as nerves and lymph nodes." [PMID:35990927, PMID:37680422]
comment: Since the pleural cavity is confined by the rib cage, large pleural effusion may push the structures in the thoracic cavity to the opposite side resulting in a shift of the upper and lower mediastinum. Other etiologies are also observed. See Figures 1 and 2 of PMID:35990927 or Figure 1 of PMID:37680422.
is_a: HP:0045026 ! Abnormal mediastinum morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10189
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000013
name: Bendopnea
synonym: "بندوبنيا" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ضيق التنفس عند الانحناء" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ضيق التنفس نتيجة الانحناء للأمام دون حبس النفس؛ ضيق التنفس أو ظهور ضيق التنفس خلال 30 ثانية من الانحناء للأمام.
def: "Dyspnea as a result of bending forward while not holding one's breath; dyspnea or shortness of breath onset within 30 seconds of bending forward." [PMID:31543202]
comment: Bendopnea is mediated by increased ventricular filling pressure during bending, which exacerbates an already high filling pressure in patients with heart failure.
is_a: HP:0002094 ! Dyspnea
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10180
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000014
name: Pain worse when lying flat
synonym: "الألم يزيد عند الاستلقاء" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "الألم عند الاستلقاء" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يشير إلى الألم الذي يتفاقم عندما يستلقي الشخص المتأثر.
def: "Refers to pain that is worse when the affected individual lies down (flat)." [PMID:31941732]
synonym: "Pain worse when lying down" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025285 ! Aggravated by
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10181
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000015
name: Tympanic membrane hypermobility
synonym: "فرط حركة الغشاء الطبلي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة حركة طبلة الأذن" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: زيادة غير طبيعية في القدرة على حركة الغشاء الطبلي.
def: "Abnormally increased ability to move of the tympanic membrane." [PMID:11556853, PMID:32901364]
comment: In Stickler syndrome, hypermobility is sometimes associated with thin, visibly hyperflaccid tympanic membranes, which is a common and otoscopically detectable sequela of chronic or recurrent otitis media and/or previous tympanostomy tubes. Hypermobility may also be found with normal appearance tympanic membranes.
is_a: HP:0031704 ! Abnormal ear physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10225
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727

[Term]
id: HP:6000016
name: Elevated circulating vitamin B12 concentration
synonym: "ارتفاع تركيز فيتامين ب12 الدوراني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة فيتامين ب12 في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تركيز فيتامين ب12 في الدورة الدموية أعلى من الحد الطبيعي الأعلى.
def: "Concentration of vitamin B12 in the blood circulation above the upper limit of normal." [PMID:14636871, PMID:20301287]
comment: Elevated levels of serum cobalamin may be a sign of a serious, even life-threatening, disease. Hematologic disorders like chronic myelogeneous leukemia, promyelocytic leukemia, polycythemia vera and also the hypereosinophilic syndrome can result in elevated levels of cobalamin.
synonym: "Elevated plasma vitamin B12 level" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated serum cobalamin level" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated serum vitamin B12 level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0040126 ! Abnormal circulating vitamin B12 concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10228
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727

[Term]
id: HP:6000017
name: Elevated circulating sFASL concentration
synonym: "ارتفاع تركيز sFASL الدوراني" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة بروتين sFASL في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تركيز sFASL (FASL القابل للذوبان، FAS-ligand القابل للذوبان) في الدورة الدموية أعلى من الحد الطبيعي الأعلى.
def: "The concentration of sFASL (soluble FASL, soluble FAS-ligand) in the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal." []
comment: The first apoptosis signal receptor (FAS) pathway regulates apoptosis and is critical for proper development and functioning of the immune system. FAS ligand (FASL) can bind to FAS receptors.
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10229
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727

[Term]
id: HP:6000018
name: Internal anal sphincter achalasia
synonym: "تعذر الارتخاء في العضلة العاصرة الداخلية الشرجية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "مشاكل في الارتخاء الشرجي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: اضطراب في العضلة العاصرة الداخلية الشرجية (IAS) حيث تفشل في الارتخاء، مما يظهر سريريًا كإمساك لا يمكن علاجه.
def: "A disorder of the internal anal sphincter (IAS) in which the IAS fails to relax that manifests clinically as intractable constipation." [PMID:19782306, PMID:33301220]
comment: The internal anal sphincter, which is a specialized smooth muscle continuation of the circular muscle layer of rectum, plays a significant role in the maintenance of anorectal continence and in the pathophysiology of incontinence and constipation. Internal anal sphincter achalasia is a clinical condition with presentation similar to Hirschsprung disease but with the presence of ganglion cells on suction rectal biopsy.
synonym: "Anal achalasia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034916 ! Abnormal anus physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10235
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8481-3559

[Term]
id: HP:6000019
name: Anthracycline exposure
synonym: "التعرض للأنثراسيكلين" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تعرض للعلاج الكيميائي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تاريخ العلاج بعامل العلاج الكيميائي أنثراسيكلين.
def: "History of treatment with an anthracycline chemotherapy agent." []
is_a: HP:4000112 ! Medication history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10240
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8481-3559

[Term]
id: HP:6000020
name: Binge drinking
synonym: "الإفراط في الشرب" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شرب الكحول بكثرة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: نمط من استهلاك الكحول الثقيل الذي يتميز باستهلاك عدد كبير من المشروبات في كل مناسبة.
def: "A pattern of episodic heavy alcohol use characterized by the consumption of a high number of drinks per occasion." []
comment: The World Health Organization defines binge drinking (BD) based on a cut-off of six drinks (i.e., 60g of alcohol) or more per occasion. The National Institute on Alcoholism and Alcohol Abuse (NIAAA) defines BD as a pattern of drinking that brings blood alcohol concentration (BAC) levels to 0.08 g/dL, which typically occurs after 4 drinks (i.e., 56 g of alcohol) for women and 5 drinks (i.e., 70 g of alcohol) for men in about 2 hours.
is_a: HP:0430037 ! Abnormal alcohol consumption
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10175
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000021
name: Decreased circulating thrombopoietin concentration
synonym: "انخفاض تركيز الترومبوبويتين في الدورة الدموية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انخفاض هرمون الترومبوبويتين في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تركيز الترومبوبويتين في الدورة الدموية أقل من الحد الأدنى الطبيعي. الترومبوبويتين هو هرمون بروتيني سكري ينتج في الكبد والكلى ويحفز إنتاج وتمايز الخلايا العملاقة.
def: "Concentration of thrombopoietin in the blood circulation below the lower limit of normal. Thrombopoietin is a glycoprotein hormone produced by the liver and kidney that stimulates the production and differentiation of megakaryocytes." [PMID:32150607]
is_a: HP:0003117 ! Abnormal circulating hormone concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10244
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000022
name: Collagenoma
synonym: "كولاجينوما" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "زيادة نمو الكولاجين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تشوه ورمي نادر يتميز بالنمو المفرط لألياف الكولاجين الطبيعية وألياف مطاطية طبيعية، منخفضة أو زائدة. يمكن أن تكون الكولاجينومات منفردة أو متعددة، وعشوائية، مكتسبة أو موروثة.
def: "A rare hamartomatous malformation characterized by the predominant proliferation of normal collagen fibers and normal, decreased, or increased elastic fibers. Collagenomas may be solitary or multiple, sporadic, acquired or inherited." [PMID:29445568]
is_a: HP:0100898 ! Connective tissue nevi
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10245
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8481-3559

[Term]
id: HP:6000023
name: Lack of sufficient daily physical activity
synonym: "نقص النشاط البدني اليومي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدم كفاية النشاط البدني" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: مستويات النشاط البدني أقل مما هو مطلوب للصحة المثلى والوقاية من الوفاة المبكرة.
def: "Physical activity levels less than those required for optimal health and prevention of premature death." [PMID:23798298]
synonym: "physical inactivity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032443 ! Past medical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10246
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000024
name: Synesthesia
synonym: "سينستيزيا" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تداخل الحواس" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ظاهرة ينتج فيها التحفيز في مسار حسي أو إدراكي واحد تجارب تلقائية ولا إرادية في مسار حسي أو إدراكي آخر. على سبيل المثال، قد يشعر الأشخاص المصابون بالسينستيزيا بألوان أو طعم أو أحاسيس غير معتادة أثناء القيام بأنشطة عادية مثل القراءة أو الاستماع للموسيقى.
def: "A phenomenon whereby stimulation of one sensory or cognitive pathway leads to automatic, involuntary experiences in a second sensory or cognitive pathway. For instance, people with synaesthesia may experience unusual colors, tastes, and other sensations when engaged in everyday activities like reading or listening to music." [PMID:32114456]
is_a: HP:0011446 ! Abnormality of mental function
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10247
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000025
name: Dark cerumen
synonym: "شمع أذن داكن" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "شمع الأذن الداكن" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: لون داكن غير طبيعي لشمع الأذن، وهو مادة شمعية تفرز في قناة الأذن عادة ما تكون بني، أو برتقالي، أو أحمر، أو أصفر، أو رمادي.
def: "Abnormally dark color of cerumen (earwax), which is a waxy substance secreted in the ear canal that normally has a brown, orange, red, yellowish or gray." [PMID:37395296]
synonym: "Dark earwax" EXACT []
synonym: "Pigmented cerumen" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030790 ! Abnormal cerumen color
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10160
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727

[Term]
id: HP:6000026
name: History of spicy food intake
synonym: "تاريخ تناول الأطعمة الحارة" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "أكل الأطعمة الحارة" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تاريخ تناول كميات كبيرة من الأطعمة الحارة التي تحتوي على مكونات مثل الكابسيسين، الفلفل، الفلفل الحار، الزنجبيل، الثوم، البصل، الحلبة، والكركم.
def: "A history of high intake of spciy foods with ingrediaents such as capsaicin, pepper, chili, ginger, garlic, onion, fenugreek, and turmeric." []
is_a: HP:4000123 ! Nutrition history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10152
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000027
name: Oil-drop brown pigmentation of the corneal limbus
synonym: "تصبغ بني على شكل زيت في حافة القرنية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "بقع بنية على حافة القرنية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: بقع صبغية بنية في الحافة (الحد الفاصل بين القرنية والصلبة).
def: "Brown pigment spots in the limbus (border between the cornea and the sclera)." [PMID:24479547]
is_a: HP:0007832 ! Pigmentation of the sclera
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10162
