[Term]
id: HP:6000202
name: Cerebrospinal fluid erythrocytes
synonym: "كريات الدم الحمراء في السائل النخاعي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "وجود خلايا الدم في السائل النخاعي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: وجود كريات الدم الحمراء (RBCs) في السائل النخاعي (CSF). عادةً لا يحتوي السائل النخاعي على كريات الدم الحمراء (إريثروسيتات).
def: "The presence of red blood cells (RBCs) in the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF). The CSF normally does not contain RBCs (erythrocytes)." [PMID:32319250]
comment: Erythrocytes may be seen in CSF following a traumatic lumbar tap, but in such cases RBC counts typically decrease in sequential samples. Penetration of blood into the subarachnoid space and/or CSF may be due to trauma, a ruptured aneurysm, intracerebral hemorrhage, or in connection with a tumor.
is_a: HP:0002921 ! Abnormal cerebrospinal fluid morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8455
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

