[Term]
id: HP:6000243
name: Reduced circulating corticosteroid-binding globulin concentration
synonym: "انخفاض تركيز الغلوبولين الرابط للكورتيكوستيرويد في الدم" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "انخفاض بروتين رابط الكورتيزول في الدم" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: تركيز الغلوبولين الرابط للكورتيكوستيرويد في الدورة الدموية أقل من الحد الأدنى للطبيعي.
def: "The concentration of corticosteroid-binding globulin in the blood circulation is below the lower limit of normal." [PMID:11502797, PMID:22223768]
comment: Corticosteroid binding globulin (CBG) is encoded by the gene for serpin family A member 6 (SERPINA6;HGNC:1540). Cortisol transport is considered the main function of CBG. In addition to cortisol, CBG binds progesterone, aldosterone, and 11-deoxycorticosterone. It is mostly produced by the liver, up-regulated by estrogens, and suppressed by steroids. Clinically, high levels are observed in pregnancy. Low levels may be observed in patients with cirrhosis as well as with corticosteroid-binding globulin deficiency caused by variants in CBG (MIM:611489).
synonym: "Reduced circulating cortisol-binding globulin concentration" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8336
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

