[Term]
id: HP:6000709
name: Absent Bell phenomenon
synonym: "غياب ظاهرة بيل" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "غياب حركة العين اللا إرادية عند غلق الجفن" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ظاهرة بيل هي حركة انعكاسية للعين ترفع الجزء الأمامي لمقلة العين عند إغلاق الجفنين. تحمي العين من خلال الحفاظ على رطوبة القرنية. يشير هذا المصطلح إلى عدم وجود هذه الظاهرة، التي يمكن ملاحظتها في بعض الحالات مثل التليف الخلقي للعضلات خارج العين.
def: "The Bell phenomenon is the reflex upward movement of the front of the eyeball when the eyelids close (or blink). It protects the eye by helping to keep the cornea moist. This term refers to a lack of this phenomenon, which can be observed with certain conditions such as congenital fibrosis of the extraocular muscles." [PMID:16815872, PMID:36780505]
synonym: "Absent palpebral-oculogyric reflex" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012547 ! Abnormal involuntary eye movements
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9644
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000710
name: Dalen-Fuchs nodules
synonym: "عقد دالين-فوكس" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عقد في شبكية العين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: عقد (آفات صفراء-بيضاء تحت الظهارة الشبكية) تتكون بين غشاء بروخ والظهارة الصبغية للشبكية.
def: "Nodules (yellow-white subretinal pigment epithelium lesions) that form between Bruch membrane and the retinal pigment epithelium." [PMID:35145783]
comment: Dalen-Fuchs nodules may be observed with sympathetic ophthalmia, a rare, severe condition that typically presents as bilateral diffuse granulomatous uveitis secondary to trauma in one eye. Dalen-Fuchs nodules could be also observed in Harada disease.
synonym: "Dalen Fuchs nodules" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030506 ! Yellow/white retinal lesion
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9657
