[Term]
id: HP:6000993
name: Pupillary hypersensitivity to parasympathomimetic agents
synonym: "تحسس بؤبؤ العين الزائد للعوامل المحاكية للودّي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "تحسس عيني للعلاجات الودية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ميل كبير أكثر من الطبيعي للعوامل المحاكية للودّي لتحفيز تضيق البؤبؤ.
def: "A higher than normal tendency of parasympathomimetic agents to induce miosis." [PMID:16754691, PMID:20301359]
comment: Topical administration of methacholine 2.5% or pilocarpine 0.0625% has no observable effect on the normal pupil but causes miosis after approximately 20 minutes in almost all individuals with familial dysautonomia.
is_a: HP:0007686 ! Abnormal pupillary function
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7797
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000994
name: Lack of pupillary response to hydroxyamphetamine
synonym: "عدم استجابة بؤبؤ العين للهيدروكسي أمفيتامين" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "عدم استجابة العين للأمفيتامين" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: الهيدروكسي أمفيتامين يستخدم في قطرات العين لتوسيع البؤبؤ، مثل لتحفيز تمدد البؤبؤ لفحص القاع. يشير هذا المصطلح إلى نقص في استجابة البؤبؤ للتطبيق الموضعي للهيدروكسي أمفيتامين.
def: "4-hydroxyamphetamine is used in eye drops to dilate the pupil, e.g.., to induce mydriasis for fundus examinations. This term refers to a lack of response of the pupil to topical application of 4-hydroxyamphetamine." [PMID:20301647]
is_a: HP:0007686 ! Abnormal pupillary function
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7801
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000995
name: Subcortical U fiber lesion
synonym: "إصابة ألياف U تحت القشرية" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في ألياف U الدماغية" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: خلل في شكل ألياف U تحت القشرية، يتم تقييمها عادة من خلال شدة غير طبيعية في التصوير بالرنين المغناطيسي للدماغ.
def: "Abnormal morphology of subcortical U fibers, typically as assessed by abnromal intensity on magnetic resonance imaging of the brain." [PMID:38223048]
comment: Subcortical U-fibers are special types of short association fibers located in the superficial white matter (SWM). In contrast to the SWM, the U-fibers only connect the adjacent gyri. Since U-fibers have a rich blood supply from long perforating arteries and short perforating arteries that span the white matter (WM) and adjacent cortex, they are usually unaffected in chronic ischemic WM disease. Anatomically, U-fibers originate from pyramidal neurons of layer 6 of the cerebral cortex and provide local integration of different sites of the same gyrus or immediately adjacent gyri. Developmentally, U-fibers do not fork until the second half of gestation when gyration and sulcation of the cerebral cortex occur. As a result, U-fibers are not readily involved in diseases of myelin metabolism, such as adrenoleukodystrophy and metachromatic leukodystrophy. However, in demyelinating diseases with normal myelin and oligodendrocyte dominance, including multiple sclerosis and progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy, U-fibers are commonly involved Pathologic processes that involve the white matter typically appear hyperintense on T2/FLAIR images.
synonym: "Subcortical U fiber involvement" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010993 ! Abnormal cerebral subcortex morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8938
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000996
name: Intraspinal extradural lipoma
synonym: "ورم شحمي خارجي الحبل الشوكي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ورم دهني في الحبل الشوكي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: ورم شحمي (كتلة حميدة مغلفة بنسيج شحمي ناضج وأنسجة ليفية) يقع داخل العمود الفقري ولكن خارج الأم الجافية.
def: "A lipoma (a benign encapsulated mass with lobulated mature adipose tissue enclosed by fibrous tissue) located within the spine but outside of the dura mater." [PMID:30488010]
is_a: HP:6000590 ! Spinal lipoma
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8971
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000997
name: Intranasal mass
synonym: "كتلة داخل الأنف" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "ورم في الأنف" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: إن تضخم أو انتفاخ غير طبيعي في تجويف الأنف. تُستخدم كلمة 'كتلة' عادة في المراحل الأولية من الفحوصات التشخيصية قبل تحديد الطبيعة الدقيقة للانتفاخ.
def: "An abnormal enlargement or swelling localized to the nasal cavity. The word mass is usually used at an early stage of the diagnostic workup before the precise nature of the swelling has been determined." []
is_a: HP:0010640 ! Abnormal nasal cavity morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8983
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6000998
name: Liver rupture
synonym: "تمزق الكبد" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: يتميز التمزق تحت المحفظة في الكبد بتكوين ورم دموي، غالباً كبير، تحت غطاء الكبد. قد يمر بضعة أيام أو ساعات بين وقت الإصابة وظهور الأعراض الأولى. يمكن أن يكون تاريخ الإصابة غير موجود تمامًا، أو قد يكون غير ملحوظ إلى حد أنه يتم اكتشافه فقط من خلال استجواب دقيق. يميل الورم الدموي إلى الزيادة في الحجم.
def: "Subcapsular hepatic rupture is characterized by the development of a hematoma, often quite large, beneath the liver capsule. An interval of days or hours may elapse between the time of injury and the first appearance of symptoms. A history of injury may be entirely lacking, or may be so unremarkable that it is elicited only by diligent interrogation. The hematoma tends to increase in size." [PMID:13915569]
is_a: HP:0410042 ! Abnormal liver morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8991
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

