[Term]
id: HP:6001124
name: Sphenoid wing dysplasia
synonym: "خلل تنسجي في جناح العظم الوتدي" EXACT [PAVS:AR]
synonym: "خلل في جناح العظم الوتدي" RELATED [PAVS:AR]
comment: Arabic Definition: هو نقص تنسج أو عدم تنسج في الجناح الأكبر أو الأصغر للعظم الوتدي، مما يؤدي عادةً إلى توسع الفتحة العلوية للعين وارتفاع الجناح الوتدي الأصغر وتوسيع الحجرة العينية الجانبية.
def: "Hypoplasia or aplasia of the greater or lesser wing of the sphenoid bone, typically resulting in widening of the superior orbital fissure, elevation of the [lesser sphenoid wing, and ipsilateral orbital enlargement." [PMID:28409229, PMID:33758729, PMID:4980937]
comment: All reported cases of congenital sphenoid wing dysplasia have been attributed to neurofibromatosis type 1 (NF1). Sphenoid bone dysplasia occurs in 3-11 percent of the subjects with neurofibromatosis type 1 NF1 patients. This malformation, a distinctive diagnostic feature for NF1, is characterized by progressive proptosis and facial disfiguration secondary to herniation of meningeal and cerebral structures. Unilateral in most of the cases, sphenoid bone dysplasia associated with plexiform neurofibroma in the territory of the trigeminal nerve in several cases and pooling of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) in all cases often described in the past as an arachnoid cyst.
is_a: HP:0011821 ! Abnormal facial skeleton morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10696
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

